## Package Manager Detection System

**Diagram: Detection Priority Cascade**

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["Need package manager"]
    
    Check1{"CLAUDE_PACKAGE_MANAGER<br/>env var?"}
    Check2{".claude/<br/>package-manager.json?"}
    Check3{"package.json<br/>packageManager field?"}
    Check4{"Lock files?"}
    Check5{"~/.claude/<br/>package-manager.json?"}
    
    Detect["detectFromLockFile()<br/>Priority: pnpm > bun > yarn > npm"]
    
    Env["Environment Variable<br/>(Highest Priority)"]
    Project["Project Config<br/>(2nd Priority)"]
    PkgJSON["package.json<br/>(3rd Priority)"]
    Lock["Lock File Detection<br/>(4th Priority)"]
    Global["Global Config<br/>(5th Priority)"]
    Fallback["npm Fallback<br/>(6th Priority)"]
    
    Commands["Generate Commands:<br/>installCmd, runCmd, execCmd,<br/>addCmd, removeCmd"]
    
    Start --> Check1
    Check1 -->|Yes| Env
    Check1 -->|No| Check2
    Check2 -->|Yes| Project
    Check2 -->|No| Check3
    Check3 -->|Yes| PkgJSON
    Check3 -->|No| Check4
    Check4 -->|Yes| Detect
    Detect --> Lock
    Check4 -->|No| Check5
    Check5 -->|Yes| Global
    Check5 -->|No| Fallback
    
    Env --> Commands
    Project --> Commands
    PkgJSON --> Commands
    Lock --> Commands
    Global --> Commands
    Fallback --> Commands
```

The package manager detection system (`scripts/lib/package-manager.js`) implements a 6-level priority cascade:

1. `CLAUDE_PACKAGE_MANAGER` environment variable
2. `.claude/package-manager.json` (project config)
3. `package.json` `packageManager` field
4. Lock file detection (pnpm-lock.yaml, bun.lockb, yarn.lock, package-lock.json)
5. `~/.claude/package-manager.json` (global config)
6. npm fallback

This avoids Windows spawn limit issues from command availability checks. The `/setup-pm` command provides interactive configuration.

**Sources:** [README.md:175-203](), Diagram 7 from context

