## Plugin Manifest (plugin.json)

The plugin manifest at `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` declares metadata and component locations. This is the entry point for plugin loading by the Claude Code CLI.

**Title: Plugin Manifest Structure**
```mermaid
graph LR
    pluginJSON[".claude-plugin/plugin.json"]
    
    metadata["Metadata<br/>name, version, author"]
    skillsPaths["skills array<br/>['./skills/', './commands/']"]
    agentsPaths["agents array<br/>['./agents/*.md']"]
    
    pluginJSON --> metadata
    pluginJSON --> skillsPaths
    pluginJSON --> agentsPaths
    
    skillsPaths --> skillsDir["skills/<br/>commands/"]
    agentsPaths --> agentsDir["agents/"]
```

Sources: [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25]()

**Key Fields:**

| Field | Type | Purpose | Example |
|-------|------|---------|---------|
| `name` | string | Plugin identifier | `"everything-claude-code"` |
| `version` | string | Semantic version (X.Y.Z) | `"1.7.0"` |
| `description` | string | Plugin description | `"Complete collection of battle-tested..."` |
| `author` | object | Author metadata | `{"name": "Affaan Mustafa", "url": "..."}` |
| `homepage` | string | Documentation URL | `"https://github.com/affaan-m/..."` |
| `repository` | string | Source repository | `"https://github.com/affaan-m/..."` |
| `license` | string | License identifier | `"MIT"` |
| `keywords` | array | Searchable tags | `["agents", "skills", "hooks", ...]` |

Sources: [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25]()

### Component Registration

The manifest uses path arrays to declare where components are located:

```json
{
  "name": "everything-claude-code",
  "version": "1.7.0",
  "skills": ["./skills/", "./commands/"],
  "agents": ["./agents/*.md"]
}
```

**Note on Hooks:** The manifest does NOT include a `"hooks"` field. Claude Code CLI v2.1+ automatically loads `hooks/hooks.json` by convention. Explicitly declaring it causes duplicate detection errors that have occurred repeatedly in issues [#29](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/29), [#52](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/52), and [#103](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/103). A regression test enforces this constraint.

Sources: [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25](), [README.md:481-489]()

### Component Types Not Supported by Plugins

**Rules** cannot be distributed via the plugin system due to upstream platform limitations. Users must manually copy rules from `rules/` to `~/.claude/rules/` (user-level) or `.claude/rules/` (project-level).

Sources: [README.md:136-153]()

## Marketplace Distribution

The plugin can be distributed via the Claude Code marketplace system using `marketplace.json`.

**Title: Marketplace Distribution Flow**
```mermaid
