### Marketplace Catalog Structure

The `marketplace.json` file defines how the plugin appears in the marketplace:

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://anthropic.com/claude-code/marketplace.schema.json",
  "name": "everything-claude-code",
  "description": "Battle-tested Claude Code configurations from an Anthropic hackathon winner",
  "owner": {
    "name": "Affaan Mustafa",
    "email": "me@affaanmustafa.com"
  },
  "plugins": [
    {
      "name": "everything-claude-code",
      "source": "./",
      "description": "The most comprehensive Claude Code plugin — 14+ agents, 56+ skills, 33+ commands...",
      "version": "1.7.0",
      "category": "workflow",
      "tags": ["agents", "skills", "hooks", "commands", "tdd", "code-review", "security"]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Key Fields:**

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `$schema` | JSON schema reference for validation |
| `name` | Marketplace identifier (must match repository) |
| `description` | Marketplace-level description |
| `owner` | Contact information |
| `plugins[].name` | Plugin identifier within marketplace |
| `plugins[].source` | Relative path to plugin directory (`./` for root) |
| `plugins[].version` | Plugin version (synced with `plugin.json`) |
| `plugins[].category` | Marketplace category (`"workflow"`) |
| `plugins[].tags` | Searchable keywords |

