## Plugin Loading Process

Claude Code loads plugins through a multi-step registration and initialization process.

**Title: Plugin Component Loading**
```mermaid
graph TB
    userAction["User Action:<br/>/plugin install or<br/>claude command with enabled plugin"]
    
    loadSettings["CLI reads<br/>~/.claude/settings.json<br/>enabledPlugins"]
    
    loadPlugin["Load plugin from<br/>marketplace source or<br/>local directory"]
    
    parseManifest["Parse<br/>.claude-plugin/plugin.json"]
    
    loadSkills["Load skills from<br/>paths in skills array<br/>./skills/, ./commands/"]
    
    loadAgents["Load agents from<br/>paths in agents array<br/>./agents/*.md"]
    
    autoLoadHooks["Auto-load<br/>hooks/hooks.json<br/>(convention-based)"]
    
    registerComponents["Register components<br/>with Claude Code runtime"]
    
    userAction --> loadSettings
    loadSettings --> loadPlugin
    loadPlugin --> parseManifest
    parseManifest --> loadSkills
    parseManifest --> loadAgents
    parseManifest --> autoLoadHooks
    loadSkills --> registerComponents
    loadAgents --> registerComponents
    autoLoadHooks --> registerComponents
```

Sources: [README.md:125-165](), [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25]()

### Component Resolution

When Claude Code loads a plugin, it resolves component paths relative to the plugin directory:

**Title: Component Path Resolution**
```mermaid
graph LR
    pluginRoot["Plugin Root<br/>~/.claude/plugins/everything-claude-code/"]
    
    skillsArray["skills array:<br/>['./skills/', './commands/']"]
    agentsArray["agents array:<br/>['./agents/*.md']"]
    hooksConvention["Convention:<br/>hooks/hooks.json"]
    
    pluginRoot --> skillsArray
    pluginRoot --> agentsArray
    pluginRoot --> hooksConvention
    
    skillsArray --> skillsDir["skills/<br/>tdd-workflow/, continuous-learning-v2/, ..."]
    skillsArray --> commandsDir["commands/<br/>plan.md, tdd.md, code-review.md, ..."]
    
    agentsArray --> agentsDir["agents/<br/>planner.md, code-reviewer.md, tdd-guide.md, ..."]
    
    hooksConvention --> hooksFile["hooks/hooks.json"]
```

Sources: [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25](), [README.md:139-241]()

### Hooks Auto-Loading

**Critical behavior:** Claude Code CLI v2.1+ automatically loads `hooks/hooks.json` from the plugin directory. The manifest must NOT declare a `"hooks"` field.

**Why:** Explicitly declaring hooks causes duplicate detection errors. This has been a recurring issue:
- Issue [#29](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/29)
- Issue [#52](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/52)
- Issue [#103](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/103)

A regression test in the repository enforces this constraint.

Sources: [README.md:481-489]()

## Installation Methods

The plugin supports two installation methods: marketplace installation (recommended) and manual installation.

### Method 1: Marketplace Installation (Recommended)

The marketplace method uses the plugin system's built-in distribution mechanism.

**Installation steps:**

```bash
# Step 1: Add marketplace source
/plugin marketplace add affaan-m/everything-claude-code

# Step 2: Install plugin
/plugin install everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code
```

This modifies `~/.claude/settings.json`:

```json
{
  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "everything-claude-code": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "affaan-m/everything-claude-code"
      }
    }
  },
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code": true
  }
}
```

**Installed components:**
- Agents (loaded from plugin directory)
- Skills (loaded from plugin directory)
- Commands (loaded from plugin directory)
- Hooks (auto-loaded from `hooks/hooks.json`)

**Not installed automatically:**
- Rules (must be copied manually - see below)
- MCP configurations (must be copied manually)

Sources: [README.md:125-165]()

### Method 2: Manual Installation

For granular control or when not using the plugin system, components can be manually copied to `~/.claude/` directories.

**Manual installation steps:**

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git
cd everything-claude-code

# Copy agents
cp agents/*.md ~/.claude/agents/

# Copy commands
cp commands/*.md ~/.claude/commands/

# Copy skills
cp -r skills/* ~/.claude/skills/

# Copy rules (always required - see below)
cp -r rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r rules/typescript/* ~/.claude/rules/  # or python, golang, etc.
```

**Hooks registration:** Copy hook definitions from `hooks/hooks.json` to the `"hooks"` field in `~/.claude/settings.json`.

**MCP configuration:** Copy desired MCP servers from `mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json` to `~/.claude.json`, replacing `YOUR_*_HERE` placeholders with actual API keys.

Sources: [README.md:549-576]()

### Rules Installation (Required for Both Methods)

Rules cannot be distributed via the plugin system due to upstream platform limitations. Users must manually install rules regardless of installation method.

**Installation options:**

```bash
# Option A: Use the installer script (recommended)
./install.sh typescript    # installs common + typescript rules

# Option B: Copy multiple languages
./install.sh typescript python golang

# Option C: Target a specific platform
./install.sh --target cursor typescript

# Option D: Manual copy (user-level)
mkdir -p ~/.claude/rules
cp -r rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r rules/typescript/* ~/.claude/rules/

# Option E: Manual copy (project-level)
mkdir -p .claude/rules
cp -r rules/common/* .claude/rules/
cp -r rules/typescript/* .claude/rules/
```

**Rules structure:**

```
rules/
├── common/              # Language-agnostic principles
│   ├── coding-style.md
│   ├── git-workflow.md
│   ├── testing.md
│   ├── performance.md
│   ├── patterns.md
│   ├── hooks.md
│   ├── agents.md
│   └── security.md
├── typescript/          # TypeScript/JavaScript specific
├── python/              # Python specific
└── golang/              # Go specific
```

Sources: [README.md:136-153](), [README.md:527-544]()

