**Purpose:** This page defines what agents are in the Everything Claude Code system, their YAML structure, model and tool configurations, delegation patterns, and orchestration strategies. For information about executable workflows that agents invoke, see [Skills](#3.3). For slash commands that invoke agents, see [Commands](#3.4).

---

## What Are Agents?

Agents are **specialized subprocesses** that handle delegated tasks with limited scope. The main Claude Code instance (the "orchestrator") delegates specific responsibilities to agents, each configured with restricted tool permissions, specific models, and focused instructions.

**Key characteristics:**

- **Focused scope** — Each agent handles one type of task (planning, code review, security analysis, etc.)
- **Separate context** — Agents run in isolated processes with their own context windows
- **Tool restrictions** — Agents have explicit `allowedTools` permissions
- **Model routing** — Different agents use different models (Haiku/Sonnet/Opus) based on task complexity
- **Stateless execution** — Agents receive input, perform work, return output, then exit

**Diagram: Agent Role in ECC Architecture**

```mermaid
graph TB
    User["User"]
    Orchestrator["Main Claude Instance<br/>(Orchestrator)"]
    
    subgraph "Agent Layer"
        Planner["planner.md<br/>Model: Sonnet<br/>Tools: Read, Grep, Glob"]
        Architect["architect.md<br/>Model: Opus<br/>Tools: Read, Grep"]
        TDD["tdd-guide.md<br/>Model: Sonnet<br/>Tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash"]
        CodeReviewer["code-reviewer.md<br/>Model: Opus<br/>Tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash"]
        SecurityReviewer["security-reviewer.md<br/>Model: Opus<br/>Tools: Read, Grep, Glob"]
        BuildResolver["build-error-resolver.md<br/>Model: Sonnet<br/>Tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Knowledge Layer"
        Skills["Skills<br/>~/.claude/skills/"]
        Rules["Rules<br/>~/.claude/rules/"]
    end
    
    User -->|Commands| Orchestrator
    Orchestrator -->|Delegate| Planner
    Orchestrator -->|Delegate| Architect
    Orchestrator -->|Delegate| TDD
    Orchestrator -->|Delegate| CodeReviewer
    Orchestrator -->|Delegate| SecurityReviewer
    Orchestrator -->|Delegate| BuildResolver
    
    Planner --> Skills
    TDD --> Skills
    CodeReviewer --> Skills
    
    Planner --> Rules
    TDD --> Rules
    CodeReviewer --> Rules
```

Sources: [README.md:593-609](), [the-shortform-guide.md:76-96](), [the-longform-guide.md:254-286]()

