## Chief-of-Staff Pattern (PostToolUse Enforcement)

**Advanced pattern:** A `chief-of-staff` agent monitors all tool use and enforces quality standards via PostToolUse hooks.

**Diagram: Chief-of-Staff Monitoring**

```mermaid
graph TB
    Main["Main Agent<br/>(Implementation)"]
    Tool["Tool Execution<br/>(Edit, Write, Bash)"]
    PostHook["PostToolUse Hook"]
    ChiefOfStaff["chief-of-staff.md<br/>Quality enforcer"]
    
    Main -->|"Edit src/auth.ts"| Tool
    Tool --> PostHook
    PostHook -->|"Spawn subprocess"| ChiefOfStaff
    ChiefOfStaff -->|"Run linters, formatters"| Verify["Verification Pass"]
    Verify -->|"Violations found"| Fix["Fix Issues<br/>(subprocess)"]
    Fix -->|"Report to Main"| Main
    Verify -->|"Clean"| Continue["Continue"]
```

**Use case:** Plankton code quality system uses this pattern to run 20+ linters after every edit and spawn Claude subprocesses to fix violations.

See [Plankton Code Quality System](#11.8) for implementation details.

Sources: [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md:1-195]()

