## How Skills Are Invoked

**Diagram: Skill Invocation Flow**

```mermaid
graph TB
    User["User Input"]
    
    subgraph "Entry Points"
        SlashCmd["/tdd<br/>/plan<br/>/verify"]
        AgentDirect["Agent directly<br/>loads skill"]
        SkillRef["Skill references<br/>another skill"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Skill Resolution"
        CmdFile["commands/*.md<br/>contains skill reference"]
        AgentFile["agents/*.md<br/>references skill in prompt"]
        SkillFile["skills/*/SKILL.md"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Skill Loading"
        LoadMD["Load SKILL.md"]
        ParseFront["Parse YAML frontmatter"]
        InjectCtx["Inject into context"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Execution"
        Agent["Agent executes<br/>with skill guidance"]
        Tools["Uses allowed tools<br/>following skill workflow"]
    end
    
    User --> SlashCmd
    User --> AgentDirect
    
    SlashCmd --> CmdFile
    AgentDirect --> AgentFile
    SkillRef --> SkillFile
    
    CmdFile --> SkillFile
    AgentFile --> SkillFile
    
    SkillFile --> LoadMD
    LoadMD --> ParseFront
    ParseFront --> InjectCtx
    
    InjectCtx --> Agent
    Agent --> Tools
```

**Sources:** [README.md:608-621](), [the-shortform-guide.md:13-36]()

### Invocation Methods

#### 1. Via Slash Commands

Commands in `commands/*.md` reference skills explicitly:

```markdown
# /tdd Command

Delegate to the tdd-guide agent with the tdd-workflow skill.

You are to follow the Test-Driven Development workflow defined in
the `tdd-workflow` skill...
```

When a user runs `/tdd`, the command file is loaded, which instructs the agent to load and follow the `tdd-workflow` skill.

**Sources:** [README.md:289-322]()

#### 2. Via Agent Delegation

Agents in `agents/*.md` can reference skills in their system prompts:

```markdown
---
name: planner
description: Feature implementation planning
tools: ["Read", "Write", "Grep", "Glob"]
model: sonnet
---

You are a feature planner. Follow the planning patterns defined in
the `backend-patterns` and `frontend-patterns` skills...
```

**Sources:** [README.md:216-229]()

#### 3. Direct Skill Loading by Agents

Agents can autonomously decide to load a skill mid-session:

```
User: "Implement authentication"
Agent: [loads search-first skill] Let me research existing solutions first...
Agent: [loads tdd-workflow skill] Now I'll write tests before implementation...
Agent: [loads security-review skill] Finally, let me audit the implementation...
```

This requires the agent to have awareness of available skills, typically through the agent's prompt or through rules.

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:87-103]()

