## MCP vs CLI Alternative Pattern

### The Trade-Off

```mermaid
graph TB
    Need["Need to interact<br/>with external service"]
    
    Need --> Choice{"Token budget?<br/>Session length?"}
    
    Choice -->|"Long session<br/>Limited context"| CLI["CLI + Skills Pattern"]
    Choice -->|"Short session<br/>Rich context OK"| MCP["MCP Integration"]
    
    CLI --> CLIBenefits["Benefits:<br/>- Zero context cost<br/>- Explicit operations<br/>- No tool pollution"]
    CLI --> CLIDownside["Downsides:<br/>- Manual command construction<br/>- No semantic exploration<br/>- Copy-paste overhead"]
    
    MCP --> MCPBenefits["Benefits:<br/>- Semantic navigation<br/>- Natural language queries<br/>- Automatic tool discovery"]
    MCP --> MCPDownside["Downsides:<br/>- Context window cost<br/>- Tool description bloat<br/>- Performance overhead"]
    
    style CLI fill:#ffe8e8
    style MCP fill:#e8f4f8
```

### When to Use CLI + Skills Instead of MCPs

**Use Case: GitHub Operations**

**MCP Approach:**
- GitHub MCP: ~50 tools, ~5k tokens
- Always loaded, even for simple commits
- Full semantic access to issues, PRs, discussions

**CLI + Skills Approach:**
- Zero context cost
- `/gh-pr` command wraps `gh pr create --title "$(git log -1 --format=%s)" --body "..."`
- `/gh-review` command wraps `gh pr checks && gh pr review`
- Skills document common `gh` CLI patterns

**Choose CLI when:**
- You only need 2-3 operations (creating PRs, checking CI)
- The platform has a robust CLI (`gh`, `vercel`, `railway`, `supabase`)
- Token optimization is critical (long sessions, complex codebases)
- Operations are scripted/repetitive (perfect for commands)

**Choose MCP when:**
- You need exploratory access (browsing issues, searching PRs)
- Semantic queries are valuable ("find all open issues labeled 'bug' with mentions of auth")
- The workflow is interactive and unpredictable
- The service lacks a good CLI (e.g., browser automation via Chrome MCP)

### Hybrid Pattern Example

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"]
    }
  }
}
```

Plus `.claude/commands/gh-pr.md`:
```markdown
# Quick PR Creation

Use bash to run:
```bash
gh pr create \
  --title "$(git log -1 --format=%s)" \
  --body "$(git log -1 --format=%b)" \
  --label "enhancement"
```
```

**Result:** Use the GitHub MCP for exploration, but commands for common operations. Reduces tool clutter.

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:23-33]()

