## Prerequisites

### Claude Code CLI Version

**Minimum required version: v2.1.0 or later**

The Everything Claude Code plugin requires Claude Code CLI v2.1.0+ due to changes in the plugin system's hook handling mechanism. Earlier versions are not supported.

**Check your version:**

```bash
claude --version
```

**Upgrade if needed:**

```bash
# Follow official Claude Code update instructions
# https://code.claude.com/docs/en/installation
```

### Critical Hook Behavior (v2.1.0+)

Claude Code v2.1.0+ automatically loads `hooks/hooks.json` from any installed plugin by convention. The plugin manifest **must not** declare a `"hooks"` field in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, as this causes duplicate detection errors:

```
Duplicate hooks file detected: ./hooks/hooks.json resolves to already-loaded file
```

This automatic loading behavior is enforced by regression tests in [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:1-50]() to prevent recurrence of issues [#29](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/29), [#52](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/52), and [#103](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/103).

Sources: [README.md:296-318](), [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-50]()

