## Verification

After installation, verify that all components are correctly configured:

### Component Verification Checklist

| Component | Verification Command | Expected Result |
|-----------|---------------------|-----------------|
| Plugin | `/plugin list everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code` | Shows enabled status |
| Commands | `/help` or `/plan` | Command executes |
| Agents | `/code-review --help` | Agent available |
| Skills | Check `~/.claude/skills/` | 30+ skill directories |
| Rules | `ls ~/.claude/rules/` | 6 markdown files |
| Hooks | Start new session | No errors on startup |
| Package Manager | `node scripts/setup-package-manager.js --detect` | Shows detected PM |

### Quick Verification Script

```bash
#!/bin/bash

echo "Verifying Everything Claude Code installation..."

# Check plugin directory
if [ -d "$HOME/.claude/plugins/everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code" ]; then
    echo "✓ Plugin directory exists"
else
    echo "✗ Plugin directory not found"
fi

# Check rules
RULE_COUNT=$(ls -1 $HOME/.claude/rules/*.md 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
if [ "$RULE_COUNT" -ge 6 ]; then
    echo "✓ Rules installed ($RULE_COUNT files)"
else
    echo "✗ Rules missing (expected 6+, found $RULE_COUNT)"
fi

# Check package manager detection
if command -v node &> /dev/null; then
    PM=$(node scripts/setup-package-manager.js --detect 2>&1 | grep "Current package manager" | cut -d: -f2)
    echo "✓ Package manager: $PM"
else
    echo "! Node.js not found (required for scripts)"
fi

# Check directories
[ -d "$HOME/.claude/sessions" ] && echo "✓ Sessions directory" || echo "- Sessions directory (will be auto-created)"
[ -d "$HOME/.claude/homunculus" ] && echo "✓ Homunculus directory" || echo "- Homunculus directory (will be auto-created)"

echo ""
echo "Verification complete. Try: /plan \"Add user authentication\""
```

### Test Commands

Run these commands to verify functionality:

```bash
# Test planning agent
/plan "Add basic logging to the application"

# Test TDD workflow
/tdd "Create a user authentication module"

# Test code review
/code-review

# Test package manager detection
/setup-pm --detect

# Check continuous learning status
/instinct-status

