## Method 1: Full Manual Copy

### Step 1: Clone Repository

```bash
# Clone to a permanent location (not temporary directory)
cd ~/projects  # or your preferred location
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git
cd everything-claude-code

# Verify clone
ls -la
# Should see: agents/ commands/ skills/ rules/ hooks/ scripts/ mcp-configs/
```

The repository should remain on disk after installation. The hooks system references scripts in [scripts/hooks/]() at runtime.

**Sources:** [README.md:553](), [the-shortform-guide.md:1-431]()

### Step 2: Copy Core Components

#### Agents

```bash
# Copy all agent definitions
mkdir -p ~/.claude/agents
cp agents/*.md ~/.claude/agents/

# Verify
ls ~/.claude/agents/
# Should see: planner.md, architect.md, tdd-guide.md, code-reviewer.md, etc.
```

Agents are subagent definitions ([agents/]()) that the main Claude instance can delegate to. Each `.md` file contains YAML frontmatter with `model`, `tools`, and `description` fields.

**Sources:** [README.md:557](), [the-shortform-guide.md:76-96]()

#### Commands

```bash
# Copy all commands
mkdir -p ~/.claude/commands
cp commands/*.md ~/.claude/commands/

# Verify
ls ~/.claude/commands/
# Should see: tdd.md, plan.md, verify.md, checkpoint.md, etc.
```

Commands are slash command definitions ([commands/]()) that execute specific workflows. Each file is a Markdown prompt invoked via `/command-name`.

**Sources:** [README.md:565](), [commands/verify.md:1-60](), [commands/checkpoint.md:1-75](), [commands/eval.md:1-121]()

#### Skills

```bash
# Create skills directory
mkdir -p ~/.claude/skills

# Recommended: Copy core skills only
cp -r .agents/skills/* ~/.claude/skills/

# Add essential standalone skills
cp -r skills/search-first ~/.claude/skills/
cp -r skills/continuous-learning-v2 ~/.claude/skills/
cp -r skills/verification-loop ~/.claude/skills/
cp -r skills/tdd-workflow ~/.claude/skills/

# Verify
ls ~/.claude/skills/
# Should see: search-first/ continuous-learning-v2/ verification-loop/ tdd-workflow/
```

**Selective skill installation:** Avoid installing all 56+ skills. Most projects only need 5-10 skills. Add framework-specific skills ([skills/django-patterns](), [skills/springboot-patterns](), [skills/frontend-patterns]()) only when working with those frameworks.

**Sources:** [README.md:569-577](), [the-shortform-guide.md:13-35]()

#### Rules (Language-Specific)

Rules installation is covered in detail in [Rules Installation](#4.4). The basic pattern:

```bash
# User-level (applies to all projects)
mkdir -p ~/.claude/rules
cp -r rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r rules/typescript/* ~/.claude/rules/  # or python, golang

# Project-level (applies to current project only)
mkdir -p .claude/rules
cp -r rules/common/* .claude/rules/
cp -r rules/typescript/* .claude/rules/
```

**Important:** Do NOT copy all language directories blindly. Select only the languages you use to avoid context window bloat.

**Sources:** [README.md:559-563](), [README.md:137-151]()

### Step 3: Configure Hooks

Hooks require both the hooks configuration file and the Node.js scripts it references.

#### Copy hooks.json Content

The hooks configuration in [hooks/hooks.json]() must be manually merged into `~/.claude/settings.json`:

```bash
# Read hooks configuration
cat hooks/hooks.json

# Manually merge into ~/.claude/settings.json
# Open ~/.claude/settings.json in your editor
# Add the hooks array from hooks/hooks.json
```

**Critical:** Claude Code v2.1+ automatically loads `hooks/hooks.json` from installed plugins, but for manual installation, hooks must be explicitly added to `settings.json`. Do NOT add a `"hooks"` field to `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` if creating a custom plugin — this causes duplicate detection errors.

#### Hooks Configuration Structure

The [hooks/hooks.json]() file defines hooks for 8 event types:

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Hook Event Types"
        PreTool["PreToolUse<br/>(validation, blocking)"]
        PostTool["PostToolUse<br/>(quality, formatting)"]
        Start["SessionStart<br/>(load context)"]
        End["SessionEnd<br/>(persist state)"]
        Stop["Stop<br/>(once per session)"]
        PreCompact["PreCompact<br/>(save state)"]
        Submit["UserPromptSubmit<br/>(input validation)"]
        Notif["Notification<br/>(permission requests)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Hook Scripts (scripts/hooks/)"
        SessionStartJS["session-start.js"]
        SessionEndJS["session-end.js"]
        PreCompactJS["pre-compact.js"]
        SuggestCompactJS["suggest-compact.js"]
        EvaluateJS["evaluate-session.js"]
        PostEditFormatJS["post-edit-format.js"]
        PostEditTypecheckJS["post-edit-typecheck.js"]
        ObserveSH["observe.sh"]
    end
    
    PreTool --> ObserveSH
    PostTool --> PostEditFormatJS
    PostTool --> PostEditTypecheckJS
    PostTool --> ObserveSH
    Start --> SessionStartJS
    End --> SessionEndJS
    Stop --> EvaluateJS
    PreCompact --> PreCompactJS
    PostTool --> SuggestCompactJS
```

**Sources:** [hooks/hooks.json:1-680](), [README.md:580-582]()

### Step 4: Configure MCP Servers

MCP server configuration in [mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json]() must be merged into `~/.claude.json`:

```bash
# View MCP configurations
cat mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json

# Manually merge into ~/.claude.json
# Select only the MCP servers you need
# Replace placeholder API keys with real values
```

**Critical:** MCP servers consume context window tokens. Install only 5-10 MCP servers maximum. See [Context Window Management](#9.3) for details on the 200k→70k context degradation problem.

**Sources:** [README.md:586-588](), [the-shortform-guide.md:127-153]()

