This page explains the manual rules installation requirement, language-specific rule selection, and the `install.sh` script with platform and language targeting. For information about what rules contain and their hierarchical structure, see [Rules Reference](#5.4). For the plugin installation process (which handles agents, skills, commands, and hooks), see [Plugin Installation](#4.1).

---

## Platform Limitation

Claude Code plugins **cannot distribute rules automatically**. This is an upstream platform limitation documented in the [Claude Code plugin reference](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference). While the plugin system can distribute agents, skills, commands, and hooks via `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, the `rules` directory must be installed manually by users.

This limitation exists across all supported platforms (Claude Code, Cursor, OpenCode, Codex). Rules files must be copied to either `~/.claude/rules/` (user-level) or `.claude/rules/` (project-level) after cloning the repository.

**Sources:** [README.md:137-152](), [README.md:527-544]()

---

## Rules Directory Structure

Rules are organized hierarchically with common (language-agnostic) rules and language-specific rule sets:

### Directory Layout

```
rules/
├── README.md              # Installation guide and structure overview
├── common/                # Universal principles (always install)
│   ├── coding-style.md    # Immutability, file organization, naming
│   ├── git-workflow.md    # Commit format, PR process, branching
│   ├── testing.md         # TDD workflow, 80% coverage requirement
│   ├── performance.md     # Model selection (Haiku/Sonnet/Opus), context mgmt
│   ├── patterns.md        # Design patterns, skeleton projects
│   ├── hooks.md           # Hook architecture, TodoWrite pattern
│   ├── agents.md          # When to delegate to subagents
│   └── security.md        # Mandatory security checks, OWASP guidelines
├── typescript/            # TypeScript/JavaScript specific
│   ├── typescript-style.md
│   ├── react-patterns.md
│   └── nextjs-patterns.md
├── python/                # Python specific
│   ├── python-style.md
│   ├── django-patterns.md
│   └── pytest-patterns.md
└── golang/                # Go specific
    ├── golang-style.md
    ├── golang-idioms.md
    └── golang-testing.md
```

### Modular Installation Philosophy

The multi-language architecture allows selective installation. A TypeScript project only needs `common/` + `typescript/`, avoiding pollution from Python or Go-specific guidelines.

**Sources:** [README.md:323-336](), [README.md:636-648]()

---

## Installation Methods

### Method 1: Using install.sh (Recommended)

The `install.sh` script handles common rules + language-specific rules safely with deduplication and platform targeting.

#### Basic Usage

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git
cd everything-claude-code

# Install for TypeScript
./install.sh typescript

# Install multiple languages
./install.sh typescript python golang

# Target Cursor IDE
./install.sh --target cursor typescript

# Target specific languages on Cursor
./install.sh --target cursor python golang swift
```

#### Installation Flow Diagram

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["User runs ./install.sh typescript"] --> Clone["Repo cloned locally"]
    Clone --> Parse["Parse arguments:<br/>--target, languages[]"]
    Parse --> CheckTarget{Target platform?}
    
    CheckTarget -->|"default (Claude Code)"| CommonCC["Copy rules/common/* to<br/>~/.claude/rules/"]
    CheckTarget -->|"cursor"| CommonCursor["Copy rules/common/* to<br/>.cursor/rules/<br/>(with YAML frontmatter)"]
    
    CommonCC --> LangLoopCC["For each language in args"]
    CommonCursor --> LangLoopCursor["For each language in args"]
    
    LangLoopCC --> CopyLangCC["Copy rules/{lang}/* to<br/>~/.claude/rules/"]
    LangLoopCursor --> CopyLangCursor["Copy rules/{lang}/* to<br/>.cursor/rules/<br/>(add globs frontmatter)"]
    
    CopyLangCC --> Verify["Verify files exist"]
    CopyLangCursor --> Verify
    
    Verify --> Done["Installation complete"]
```

**Sources:** [README.md:145-149](), [README.md:815-817]()

---

### Method 2: Manual Installation

For users who prefer explicit control or need custom configurations.

#### Option A: User-Level Rules (Global)

Applies to all projects for the current user.

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git

# Create rules directory
mkdir -p ~/.claude/rules

# Copy common rules (always required)
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/

# Copy language-specific rules (pick your stack)
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/python/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/golang/* ~/.claude/rules/
```

#### Option B: Project-Level Rules (Scoped)

Applies only to the current project directory.

```bash
# From your project root
mkdir -p .claude/rules

# Copy common rules
cp -r /path/to/everything-claude-code/rules/common/* .claude/rules/

# Copy language-specific rules
cp -r /path/to/everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* .claude/rules/
```

**Sources:** [README.md:529-544](), [README.md:559-564]()

---

## Language Targeting

### Supported Languages

The `install.sh` script recognizes the following language identifiers:

| Language | Identifier | Rule Files |
|----------|-----------|------------|
| TypeScript/JavaScript | `typescript` | `typescript-style.md`, `react-patterns.md`, `nextjs-patterns.md` |
| Python | `python` | `python-style.md`, `django-patterns.md`, `pytest-patterns.md` |
| Go | `golang` | `golang-style.md`, `golang-idioms.md`, `golang-testing.md` |
| Swift | `swift` | `swift-style.md`, `swift-concurrency.md`, `swiftui-patterns.md` |

### Multi-Language Projects

For projects using multiple languages (e.g., TypeScript frontend + Python backend):

```bash
# Install rules for both stacks
./install.sh typescript python

# Result: common/ + typescript/ + python/ all copied to ~/.claude/rules/
```

### Language Selection Decision Tree

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["Determine project languages"] --> Check{Languages used?}
    
    Check -->|"TS/JS only"| InstallTS["./install.sh typescript"]
    Check -->|"Python only"| InstallPy["./install.sh python"]
    Check -->|"Go only"| InstallGo["./install.sh golang"]
    Check -->|"Fullstack TS + Python"| InstallMulti["./install.sh typescript python"]
    Check -->|"Mobile (Swift)"| InstallSwift["./install.sh swift"]
    
    InstallTS --> Result["~/.claude/rules/<br/>common/ + typescript/"]
    InstallPy --> Result2["~/.claude/rules/<br/>common/ + python/"]
    InstallGo --> Result3["~/.claude/rules/<br/>common/ + golang/"]
    InstallMulti --> Result4["~/.claude/rules/<br/>common/ + typescript/ + python/"]
    InstallSwift --> Result5["~/.claude/rules/<br/>common/ + swift/"]
```

**Sources:** [README.md:99-103](), [README.md:561-563]()

---

## Platform-Specific Installation

### Claude Code (Default)

Rules are installed to `~/.claude/rules/` or `.claude/rules/` without modification. No frontmatter transformation required.

```bash
# User-level installation
./install.sh typescript

# Files copied as-is to ~/.claude/rules/
```

### Cursor IDE

Cursor requires YAML frontmatter with `description`, `globs`, and `alwaysApply` fields. The `--target cursor` flag adds this frontmatter during installation.

```bash
# Install rules for Cursor
./install.sh --target cursor typescript python golang swift
```

#### Frontmatter Transformation

**Original (Claude Code format):**
```markdown
# TypeScript Coding Style

Use strict TypeScript with explicit types...
```

**Transformed (Cursor format):**
```yaml
---
description: "TypeScript coding style extending common rules"
globs: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# TypeScript Coding Style

Use strict TypeScript with explicit types...
```

#### Cursor Rules Count

| Category | Count | `alwaysApply` |
|----------|-------|---------------|
| Common rules | 9 | `true` |
| TypeScript rules | 5 | `false` (glob-matched) |
| Python rules | 5 | `false` (glob-matched) |
| Go rules | 5 | `false` (glob-matched) |
| Swift rules | 5 | `false` (glob-matched) |

**Total:** 29 rules when all languages installed.

**Sources:** [README.md:815-858]()

---

## User-Level vs Project-Level Rules

### Priority Cascade

Claude Code applies rules with the following precedence:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Start["Claude reads rules"] --> UserCheck{User-level rules exist?}
    UserCheck -->|Yes| LoadUser["Load ~/.claude/rules/*"]
    UserCheck -->|No| SkipUser["Skip user rules"]
    
    LoadUser --> ProjectCheck{Project-level rules exist?}
    SkipUser --> ProjectCheck
    
    ProjectCheck -->|Yes| LoadProject["Load .claude/rules/*<br/>(overrides user rules)"]
    ProjectCheck -->|No| SkipProject["Use user rules only"]
    
    LoadProject --> Apply["Apply rules to session"]
    SkipProject --> Apply
```

### Use Cases

| Scenario | Install Location | Rationale |
|----------|------------------|-----------|
| General coding standards | `~/.claude/rules/` | Applies to all projects |
| Project-specific patterns | `.claude/rules/` | Overrides user-level rules for this project |
| Shared team standards | `.claude/rules/` (committed to repo) | All team members use same rules |
| Personal preferences | `~/.claude/rules/` | Your defaults across all projects |

### Example: Mixed Installation

```bash
# User-level: General best practices
mkdir -p ~/.claude/rules
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/

# Project-level: Strict TypeScript for this SaaS app
cd ~/projects/my-saas-app
mkdir -p .claude/rules
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* .claude/rules/
```

**Result:** When working in `~/projects/my-saas-app`, Claude sees:
- Common rules from `~/.claude/rules/common/`
- TypeScript rules from `.claude/rules/` (project-level)

**Sources:** [README.md:535-544]()

---

## Verifying Installation

### Manual Verification

```bash
# Check user-level rules
ls -la ~/.claude/rules/

# Expected output:
# coding-style.md
# git-workflow.md
# testing.md
# performance.md
# patterns.md
# hooks.md
# agents.md
# security.md
# typescript-style.md  (if TypeScript installed)
# react-patterns.md    (if TypeScript installed)
# ...

# Check project-level rules
ls -la .claude/rules/
```

### Testing Rule Application

Start a Claude Code session and verify rules are loaded:

```bash
claude

# In the session, ask:
# "What coding standards should I follow?"
# "What's the commit message format?"
# "What test coverage is required?"
```

Claude's responses should reflect the installed rules (e.g., "Use conventional commits", "Maintain 80%+ test coverage").

### Common Issues

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| Rules not applied | Installed to wrong directory | Check `~/.claude/rules/` vs `.claude/rules/` |
| Old rules persist | User-level rules not updated | Delete `~/.claude/rules/`, re-run `install.sh` |
| Language-specific rules missing | Forgot to specify language | Re-run `./install.sh <language>` |
| Cursor rules not working | Missing YAML frontmatter | Re-run with `--target cursor` |

---

## Installation Flow Summary

```mermaid
graph TB
    Clone["git clone affaan-m/everything-claude-code"] --> Choice{Installation method?}
    
    Choice -->|"Automated"| Script["./install.sh"]
    Choice -->|"Manual"| ManualCopy["cp -r rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/"]
    
    Script --> ScriptArgs["Parse arguments:<br/>--target, languages[]"]
    ScriptArgs --> ScriptCommon["Copy rules/common/*"]
    ScriptCommon --> ScriptLangs["Copy rules/{lang}/*<br/>for each language"]
    ScriptLangs --> ScriptTransform{--target cursor?}
    ScriptTransform -->|Yes| AddFrontmatter["Add YAML frontmatter<br/>to each rule file"]
    ScriptTransform -->|No| SkipTransform["Copy as-is"]
    
    ManualCopy --> ManualLangs["cp -r rules/typescript/*<br/>~/.claude/rules/"]
    ManualLangs --> ManualDone["Installation complete"]
    
    AddFrontmatter --> Done["Installation complete"]
    SkipTransform --> Done
    
    Done --> Verify["Verify with ls ~/.claude/rules/"]
    ManualDone --> Verify
    
    Verify --> Test["Test in Claude session"]
```

**Sources:** [README.md:137-152](), [README.md:527-564](), [README.md:813-858]()

