## Rules Selection & Installation

Rules are organized into common (language-agnostic) and language-specific sets, installed as flat files into `$TARGET/rules/`.

**Rules Installation Structure**

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    MultiSelect["AskUserQuestion<br/>multiSelect: true"]
    
    MultiSelect --> Common["Common rules<br/>(Recommended)<br/>8 files"]
    MultiSelect --> TS["TypeScript/JavaScript<br/>5 files"]
    MultiSelect --> Py["Python<br/>5 files"]
    MultiSelect --> Go["Go<br/>5 files"]
    
    Common --> CommonCopy["cp -r ECC_ROOT/rules/common/*<br/>TARGET/rules/"]
    TS --> TSCopy["cp -r ECC_ROOT/rules/typescript/*<br/>TARGET/rules/"]
    Py --> PyCopy["cp -r ECC_ROOT/rules/python/*<br/>TARGET/rules/"]
    Go --> GoCopy["cp -r ECC_ROOT/rules/golang/*<br/>TARGET/rules/"]
    
    CommonCopy --> Files1["coding-style.md<br/>git-workflow.md<br/>development-workflow.md<br/>testing.md<br/>security.md<br/>..."]
    
    TSCopy --> Files2["typescript-patterns.md<br/>react-hooks.md<br/>playwright-testing.md<br/>..."]
    
    PyCopy --> Files3["python-patterns.md<br/>pytest-testing.md<br/>black-ruff.md<br/>..."]
    
    GoCopy --> Files4["golang-patterns.md<br/>table-driven-tests.md<br/>gofmt-staticcheck.md<br/>..."]
    
    TS & Py & Go --> Check{Common rules<br/>also selected?}
    Check -->|"No"| Warn["Warning: Language-specific rules<br/>extend common rules.<br/>Install common rules too?"]
```

**Rules selection options** [skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md:170-196]():

| Rule Set | Files | Description |
|----------|-------|-------------|
| Common rules | 8 files | Language-agnostic: coding style, git workflow, testing, security |
| TypeScript/JavaScript | 5 files | TS/JS patterns, hooks, Playwright testing |
| Python | 5 files | Python patterns, pytest, black/ruff formatting |
| Go | 5 files | Go patterns, table-driven tests, gofmt/staticcheck |

**Installation behavior:**

Rules are installed as flat files, not in subdirectories:

```bash
# Correct structure after installation
$TARGET/rules/coding-style.md
$TARGET/rules/git-workflow.md
$TARGET/rules/typescript-patterns.md

# Incorrect (common issue to avoid)
$TARGET/rules/common/coding-style.md
```

**Dependency warning:**

If user selects language-specific rules without common rules, the wizard prompts [skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md:194-196]():

> "Language-specific rules extend the common rules. Installing without common rules may result in incomplete coverage. Install common rules too?"

