## Component Taxonomy

### Agents by Function

Agents are specialized subagents that handle delegated tasks with limited scope. Each agent has a YAML frontmatter specifying tools, model, and purpose.

| Category | Agents | Primary Model | Tools |
|----------|--------|--------------|-------|
| **Planning & Architecture** | `planner`, `architect` | Opus | Read, Grep, Glob, Bash |
| **Development** | `tdd-guide`, `build-error-resolver` | Sonnet | Read, Write, Edit, Bash |
| **Quality Assurance** | `code-reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, `database-reviewer` | Opus | Read, Grep, Glob, Bash |
| **Testing** | `e2e-runner` | Sonnet | Read, Write, Edit, Bash |
| **Maintenance** | `refactor-cleaner`, `doc-updater` | Sonnet | Read, Write, Edit, Bash |
| **Language-Specific** | `go-reviewer`, `go-build-resolver`, `python-reviewer` | Sonnet/Opus | Read, Grep, Bash |

**Agent YAML Structure**

All agents follow this format: [agents/code-reviewer.md:1-10]()

```yaml
---
name: code-reviewer
description: Reviews code for quality, security, and maintainability
tools: ["Read", "Grep", "Glob", "Bash"]
model: opus
---
```

Sources: [README.md:216-230](), [the-shortform-guide.md:76-96]()

### Skills by Domain

Skills are workflow definitions stored as Markdown files with YAML frontmatter. They can be single-file or multi-file directories.

| Category | Skill Count | Examples |
|----------|------------|----------|
| **Framework & Language** | 18 | `frontend-patterns`, `backend-patterns`, `golang-patterns`, `django-patterns`, `springboot-patterns`, `swift-concurrency-6-2` |
| **Database** | 4 | `clickhouse-io`, `postgres-patterns`, `jpa-patterns`, `database-migrations` |
| **Workflow & Quality** | 12 | `tdd-workflow`, `verification-loop`, `eval-harness`, `checkpoint`, `security-review`, `plankton-code-quality` |
