## Agent YAML Structure

All agents follow this YAML frontmatter format:

```markdown
---
name: agent-name
description: Single-line description of purpose
tools: ["Read", "Grep", "Glob", "Bash"]
model: sonnet
---

# Agent System Prompt

You are a specialized agent that...

## Your Scope

- What you DO handle
- What you DON'T handle

## Your Process

1. Step one
2. Step two
...
```

**Frontmatter Fields:**

| Field | Required | Values | Purpose |
|-------|----------|--------|---------|
| `name` | Yes | kebab-case string | Agent identifier for invocation |
| `description` | Yes | Single line | Human-readable purpose statement |
| `tools` | Yes | Array of tool names | Allowed Claude Code tools |
| `model` | No | `haiku`, `sonnet`, `opus` | Override default model |

**Common Tool Combinations:**

- **Read-only:** `["Read", "Grep", "Glob"]` — For analysis, review, auditing
- **Code editing:** `["Read", "Write", "Edit", "Grep", "Glob"]` — For implementation
- **Full access:** `["Read", "Write", "Edit", "Grep", "Glob", "Bash"]` — For complex workflows

Sources: [README.md:595-609](), [agents/ directory examples]()

