## Core Agents Reference

### Planning & Architecture Agents

| Agent | File | Model | Tools | Purpose |
|-------|------|-------|-------|---------|
| **planner** | `agents/planner.md` | Sonnet | Read, Grep, Glob | Feature implementation planning, task decomposition, dependency analysis |
| **architect** | `agents/architect.md` | Opus | Read, Grep, Glob | System design decisions, architectural patterns, technology selection |

**planner** — Used at the start of feature development to break down requirements into implementation steps. Creates detailed plans with file-level changes, dependency order, and acceptance criteria. Invoked via `/plan` command.

**architect** — Used for high-level system design. Makes architectural decisions (monolith vs microservices, database choice, caching strategy) before implementation begins. Invoked when the orchestrator encounters design questions.

Sources: [README.md:220-221](), [the-shortform-guide.md:656-677]()

---

### Development Workflow Agents

| Agent | File | Model | Tools | Purpose |
|-------|------|-------|-------|---------|
| **tdd-guide** | `agents/tdd-guide.md` | Sonnet | Read, Write, Edit, Grep, Glob, Bash | Test-driven development enforcement — RED → GREEN → IMPROVE |
| **build-error-resolver** | `agents/build-error-resolver.md` | Sonnet | Read, Write, Edit, Bash | Fix compilation errors, type errors, build failures |
| **e2e-runner** | `agents/e2e-runner.md` | Sonnet | Read, Write, Edit, Bash | Playwright E2E test generation and execution |
| **refactor-cleaner** | `agents/refactor-cleaner.md` | Haiku | Read, Write, Edit, Grep | Dead code removal, unused imports, console.log cleanup |

**tdd-guide** — Enforces test-first development. Blocks implementation until tests are written. Verifies 80%+ coverage requirement. Used via `/tdd` command or auto-delegated when rules specify TDD mode.

**build-error-resolver** — Specialized in fixing broken builds. Reads error output, identifies root cause, applies fix, verifies. Used via `/build-fix` command or when CI failures are detected.

**e2e-runner** — Generates Playwright tests for user flows. Creates Page Object Model patterns. Used via `/e2e` command.

**refactor-cleaner** — Removes code smell after implementation passes. Lighter-weight than full code review. Used via `/refactor-clean` command. See also: the de-sloppify pattern in [Autonomous Loop Patterns](#10.7).

Sources: [README.md:220-227](), [the-shortform-guide.md:656-677](), [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:315-373]()

---

### Code Review & Security Agents

| Agent | File | Model | Tools | Purpose |
|-------|------|-------|-------|---------|
| **code-reviewer** | `agents/code-reviewer.md` | Opus | Read, Grep, Glob, Bash | Quality review — maintainability, security, performance |
| **security-reviewer** | `agents/security-reviewer.md` | Opus | Read, Grep, Glob | OWASP Top 10, injection vulnerabilities, secrets detection |
| **database-reviewer** | `agents/database-reviewer.md` | Sonnet | Read, Grep, Glob | SQL injection, N+1 queries, indexing issues, migration safety |

**code-reviewer** — Comprehensive quality gate. Checks for maintainability issues, security vulnerabilities, performance problems, test coverage gaps. Uses Opus for deep reasoning. Invoked via `/code-review` command.

**security-reviewer** — Specialized security audit. OWASP Top 10 coverage, secrets detection (hardcoded keys, tokens), injection vulnerability scanning. Uses Opus for adversarial reasoning. Can be paired with AgentShield for static analysis + LLM reasoning.

**database-reviewer** — Database-specific review. Detects SQL injection risks, N+1 query patterns, missing indexes, unsafe migrations. Auto-delegated when database changes are detected in diffs.

Sources: [README.md:221-229](), [the-shortform-guide.md:656-677]()

---

### Documentation & Maintenance Agents

| Agent | File | Model | Tools | Purpose |
|-------|------|-------|-------|---------|
| **doc-updater** | `agents/doc-updater.md` | Haiku | Read, Write, Edit, Grep, Glob | Keep documentation in sync with code changes |

**doc-updater** — Updates README.md, API docs, architecture diagrams when code changes. Detects stale documentation. Uses Haiku for cost efficiency (documentation structure is straightforward). Invoked via `/update-docs` command.

Sources: [README.md:227](), [the-shortform-guide.md:656-677]()

