This page provides a comprehensive reference for all skills available in the Everything Claude Code system. Skills are workflow definitions and domain knowledge packages that guide Claude through specific development patterns, coding standards, and technical implementations. They are invoked by agents (see [Agent Reference](#5.1)) or executed directly via commands (see [Command Reference](#5.3)).

For information about rules that constrain all agent behavior, see [Rules Reference](#5.4). For hook-based automation, see [Hooks System](#6).

---

## Skill Structure

Skills are markdown files with YAML frontmatter that define reusable workflows. Each skill has a canonical `SKILL.md` file that follows this structure:

```markdown
---
name: skill-name
description: Brief description of what the skill does
origin: ECC | community | platform-specific
---

# Skill Title

## When to Activate
- Condition 1
- Condition 2

## Core Patterns
[Workflow steps, code examples, decision frameworks]

## Key Design Decisions
[Design rationale table]

## Best Practices
- Practice 1
- Practice 2

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
- Anti-pattern 1
- Anti-pattern 2

## When to Use
[Final guidance on applicability]
```

The frontmatter is parsed by Claude Code to understand skill metadata. The markdown body provides the detailed workflow guidance, examples, and best practices that agents follow when the skill is loaded.

**Sources:** [README.md:231-287](), [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:1-8](), [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:1-8]()

---

## Skill Loading and Invocation

Skills can be loaded in three ways:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Loading Methods"
        CMD["Command Invocation<br/>(/tdd, /plan, /e2e)"]
        AGENT["Agent Delegation<br/>(planner, tdd-guide)"]
        MANUAL["Manual Reference<br/>(user prompt)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Skill Storage"
        USER["~/.claude/skills/<br/>User-level skills"]
        PROJECT[".claude/skills/<br/>Project-level skills"]
        PLUGIN[".claude-plugin/<br/>Plugin skills"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Loaded Context"
        SYSTEM["System Prompt<br/>SKILL.md content"]
    end
    
    CMD --> USER
    CMD --> PROJECT
    CMD --> PLUGIN
    AGENT --> USER
    AGENT --> PROJECT
    AGENT --> PLUGIN
    MANUAL --> USER
    MANUAL --> PROJECT
    
    USER --> SYSTEM
    PROJECT --> SYSTEM
    PLUGIN --> SYSTEM
    
    SYSTEM --> BEHAVIOR["Agent Behavior<br/>Guided by skill"]
```

**Skill Resolution Priority:** Project-level (`.claude/skills/`) overrides user-level (`~/.claude/skills/`) which overrides plugin-provided skills. This allows project-specific customizations of standard skills.

**Sources:** [README.md:569-577](), [the-shortform-guide.md:13-34]()

