## Autonomous Loop Skills

Skills for running Claude Code in autonomous, non-interactive modes.

| Skill | Purpose | Key Patterns |
|-------|---------|-------------|
| `autonomous-loops` | Loop architectures | Sequential pipeline, REPL, infinite agentic loop, continuous PR loop, DAG orchestration |

The `autonomous-loops` skill defines six progressively sophisticated patterns for autonomous execution:

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Loop Complexity Spectrum"
        SEQ["Sequential Pipeline<br/>claude -p chains"]
        NANO["NanoClaw REPL<br/>Persistent sessions"]
        INFINITE["Infinite Agentic<br/>Parallel spec-driven"]
        CONTINUOUS["Continuous Claude<br/>Iterative PR loop"]
        RALPH["Ralphinho DAG<br/>RFC-driven orchestration"]
    end
    
    SEQ -->|"Add persistence"| NANO
    NANO -->|"Add parallelism"| INFINITE
    INFINITE -->|"Add CI gates"| CONTINUOUS
    CONTINUOUS -->|"Add DAG + merge queue"| RALPH
    
    SEQ -.->|"Best for"| S1["Scripted workflows<br/>Daily dev tasks"]
    NANO -.->|"Best for"| S2["Interactive exploration<br/>Session continuity"]
    INFINITE -.->|"Best for"| S3["Content generation<br/>Spec variations"]
    CONTINUOUS -.->|"Best for"| S4["Multi-day projects<br/>Iterative refinement"]
    RALPH -.->|"Best for"| S5["Large features<br/>Parallel decomposition"]
```

**Key architectural components:**

- **Sequential Pipeline**: Chain `claude -p` calls in bash scripts, each with focused prompts [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:35-100]()
- **NanoClaw REPL**: Session-aware REPL at `scripts/claw.js` that persists history in `~/.claude/claw/{session}.md` [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:104-133]()
- **Infinite Agentic Loop**: Two-prompt orchestration system (decomposer + parallel workers) [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:137-203]()
- **Continuous Claude**: PR loop with CI gates, merge automation, cost/time limits [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:206-276]()
- **Ralphinho**: RFC decomposition into DAG, tiered quality pipelines, merge queue with eviction recovery [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:279-528]()

**De-Sloppify Pattern**: An add-on for any loop — separate cleanup pass after implementation to remove test/code slop without constraining the implementer [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:316-373]()

**Sources:** [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:1-608]()

