## Skill Organization in Filesystem

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "User-Level Skills"
        UG["~/.claude/skills/"]
        UG1["coding-standards/SKILL.md"]
        UG2["tdd-workflow/SKILL.md"]
        UG3["security-review/SKILL.md"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project-Level Skills"
        PG[".claude/skills/"]
        PG1["project-guidelines-example/SKILL.md<br/>(custom overrides)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Plugin Skills"
        PLG[".claude-plugin/skills/"]
        PLG1["continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md"]
        PLG2["autonomous-loops/SKILL.md"]
        PLG3["plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Resolution"
        RESOLVE["Skill Loader"]
    end
    
    PG --> RESOLVE
    UG --> RESOLVE
    PLG --> RESOLVE
    
    RESOLVE --> LOADED["Loaded Skill Context<br/>Priority: Project > User > Plugin"]
    
    RESOLVE -.->|"Project overrides all"| PG1
    RESOLVE -.->|"User overrides plugin"| UG1
```

**Resolution order:** When a skill name is requested, Claude Code searches in this priority:
1. `.claude/skills/{name}/SKILL.md` (project-level override)
2. `~/.claude/skills/{name}/SKILL.md` (user-level configuration)
3. Plugin-provided skills (from enabled plugins)

This allows projects to customize or extend standard skills without modifying global configuration.

**Sources:** [README.md:569-577]()

