## Command Invocation Patterns

### Plugin vs Manual Installation

The command syntax differs based on installation method:

```bash
# Plugin installation (namespaced)
/everything-claude-code:plan "Add authentication"

# Manual installation (direct)
/plan "Add authentication"
```

### Command Syntax Conventions

```bash
/command [required-arg] [optional-arg] [flags]
```

- **Required arguments** — Enclosed in angle brackets in documentation: `<name>`
- **Optional arguments** — Enclosed in square brackets: `[name]`
- **Flags** — Prefixed with `--`: `--model opus`
- **Arguments with spaces** — Quoted: `"Add user auth"`

**Sources:** [README.md:156-165](), [README.md:656-669]()

---

## Command Flow Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    User["User types /command"]
    
    subgraph "Command Layer"
        CmdFile["commands/*.md<br/>Markdown prompt file"]
        Args["$ARGUMENTS variable<br/>populated"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Execution Layer"
        Agent["Agent invocation<br/>(if specified)"]
        Skill["Skill loading<br/>(if referenced)"]
        Tools["Tool execution<br/>(Read, Edit, Bash)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Hook Layer"
        PreHooks["PreToolUse hooks<br/>Validation"]
        PostHooks["PostToolUse hooks<br/>Quality enforcement"]
    end
    
    User --> CmdFile
    CmdFile --> Args
    Args --> Agent
    Args --> Skill
    Agent --> Tools
    Skill --> Tools
    Tools --> PreHooks
    PreHooks --> Tools
    Tools --> PostHooks
    
    style CmdFile fill:#f9f9f9
    style Agent fill:#e8e8e8
    style Skill fill:#e8e8e8
    style PreHooks fill:#d8d8d8
    style PostHooks fill:#d8d8d8
```

**How command execution works:**

1. **Command file loaded** — Claude Code reads `commands/{command-name}.md`
2. **Arguments parsed** — User input after command name populates `$ARGUMENTS`
3. **Agent delegation** — If command references an agent, that agent is invoked
4. **Skill loading** — If command references skills, those workflows are loaded
5. **Tool execution** — Agent/skill executes tools (Read, Edit, Write, Bash)
6. **Hook interception** — PreToolUse and PostToolUse hooks fire on tool calls

**Sources:** [commands/checkpoint.md:1-75](), [commands/verify.md:1-60](), [commands/eval.md:1-121]()

