### `/eval`

**Purpose:** Eval-driven development workflow.

**Syntax:**
```bash
/eval [define|check|report|list|clean] [feature-name]
```

**Define evals:**
```bash
/eval define feature-name
```

Creates `.claude/evals/feature-name.md` with template:
```markdown
## EVAL: feature-name

### Capability Evals
- [ ] [Capability 1]
- [ ] [Capability 2]

### Regression Evals
- [ ] [Existing behavior 1]
- [ ] [Existing behavior 2]

### Success Criteria
- pass@3 > 90% for capability evals
- pass^3 = 100% for regression evals
```

**Check evals:**
```bash
/eval check feature-name
```

Runs evals and reports status:
```
EVAL CHECK: feature-name
========================
Capability: 2/3 passing
Regression: 3/3 passing
Status: IN PROGRESS
```

**Report evals:**
```bash
/eval report feature-name
```

Comprehensive report with pass@k metrics:
```
EVAL REPORT: feature-name
=========================
CAPABILITY EVALS
[eval-1]: PASS (pass@1)
[eval-2]: PASS (pass@2)
[eval-3]: FAIL

METRICS
Capability pass@1: 67%
Capability pass@3: 100%
Regression pass^3: 100%

RECOMMENDATION
SHIP / NEEDS WORK / BLOCKED
```

**List evals:**
```bash
/eval list
```

**Pass@k vs Pass^k:**
- **pass@k** — At least ONE of k attempts succeeds (good for capability)
- **pass^k** — ALL k attempts must succeed (good for regression)

**Sources:** [commands/eval.md:1-121](), [README.md:317]()

