## Purpose and Scope

This page documents the rules system in Everything Claude Code — the "always-follow" guidelines that constrain Claude's behavior across all sessions. Rules are markdown files loaded automatically by Claude Code that define coding standards, workflows, security requirements, and best practices.

For information about skills (workflow definitions), see [Skills Reference](#5.2). For commands that execute specific tasks, see [Command Reference](#5.3).

---

## Rules System Architecture

### How Rules Work

Rules are markdown files stored in `~/.claude/rules/` (user-level) or `.claude/rules/` (project-level) that Claude Code loads on every session start. Unlike skills which are invoked explicitly, rules apply continuously throughout the session.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Rules Storage"
        UserRules["~/.claude/rules/\n(user-level)"]
        ProjectRules[".claude/rules/\n(project-level)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Rules Organization"
        Common["common/\n8 language-agnostic files"]
        TypeScript["typescript/\n5 TS/JS files"]
        Python["python/\n5 Python files"]
        Golang["golang/\n5 Go files"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Claude Code Session"
        SessionStart["Session Start"]
        RulesLoader["Rules Loader"]
        SystemPrompt["System Prompt"]
        AgentExecution["Agent Execution"]
    end
    
    UserRules --> RulesLoader
    ProjectRules --> RulesLoader
    
    Common --> UserRules
    TypeScript --> UserRules
    Python --> UserRules
    Golang --> UserRules
    
    SessionStart --> RulesLoader
    RulesLoader --> SystemPrompt
    SystemPrompt --> AgentExecution
    
    style SystemPrompt fill:#f9f9f9
    style RulesLoader fill:#f9f9f9
```

**Rules Loading Priority**

Sources: [README.md:320-336](), [rules/README.md](), [.claude-plugin/plugin.json]()

