## Common Rules

Common rules apply regardless of programming language. These establish universal principles for all Claude Code sessions.

| Rule File | Purpose | Key Constraints |
|-----------|---------|----------------|
| `coding-style.md` | Code organization and style | Immutability preferences, file size limits, module structure |
| `git-workflow.md` | Git and version control | Conventional commits format, PR process, branch naming |
| `testing.md` | Test requirements | TDD workflow, 80%+ coverage mandate, test organization |
| `performance.md` | Token and context optimization | Model selection (Haiku/Sonnet/Opus), context window management |
| `patterns.md` | Design patterns and architecture | Skeleton projects, API response formats, abstraction layers |
| `hooks.md` | Hook system documentation | TodoWrite pattern, hook lifecycle, when to create hooks |
| `agents.md` | Agent delegation rules | When to delegate to subagents, scoping, tool permissions |
| `security.md` | Security requirements | Mandatory security checks, input validation, secrets handling |

