## Rules Installation

### Manual Installation Requirement

**Important:** Claude Code plugins cannot distribute rules automatically due to platform limitations. Rules must be installed manually even when using the plugin.

### Installation Methods

#### Method 1: Installation Script (Recommended)

The `install.sh` script handles both common and language-specific rules safely:

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git
cd everything-claude-code

# Install common + specific language(s)
./install.sh typescript        # Common + TypeScript
./install.sh python golang     # Common + Python + Go
./install.sh typescript python golang swift  # Multiple languages

# Target specific platform
./install.sh --target cursor typescript
```

**Installation script behavior:**
- Always installs common rules first
- Flat-copies language-specific rules into the same directory
- Detects and warns about existing files (merge vs overwrite)
- Validates cross-references between files

Sources: [README.md:136-150](), [install.sh]()

#### Method 2: Manual Copy

```bash
# User-level installation (all projects)
mkdir -p ~/.claude/rules
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* ~/.claude/rules/   # if needed
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/python/* ~/.claude/rules/       # if needed
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/golang/* ~/.claude/rules/       # if needed

# Project-level installation (current project only)
mkdir -p .claude/rules
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/common/* .claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* .claude/rules/     # pick stack
```

**Critical:** Language-specific rules extend common rules. Installing language-specific rules without common rules results in incomplete coverage.

Sources: [README.md:525-544](), [skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md:183-196]()

