## Rules and Development Workflows

### Research-First Pattern

The `development-workflow.md` rule mandates research before implementation:

```markdown
0. Research & Reuse (mandatory before any new implementation)
   - GitHub code search first
   - Exa MCP for research
   - Check package registries
   - Search for adaptable implementations
   - Prefer adopting/porting over writing net-new code
```

This integrates with the `search-first` skill:

```mermaid
graph TD
    Task["New feature requested"]
    
    CheckRule["development-workflow.md:\nResearch & Reuse mandatory"]
    
    InvokeSkill["Invoke search-first skill"]
    
    Search["Parallel search:\nnpm/PyPI, MCP, GitHub, docs"]
    
    Decide{Found\nsolution?}
    
    Adopt["Adopt:\nInstall package"]
    Extend["Extend:\nInstall + wrapper"]
    Build["Build:\nWrite custom\n(informed by research)"]
    
    Implement["Proceed to\nstep 1: Plan First"]
    
    Task --> CheckRule
    CheckRule --> InvokeSkill
    InvokeSkill --> Search
    Search --> Decide
    
    Decide -->|Exact match| Adopt
    Decide -->|Partial match| Extend
    Decide -->|Nothing suitable| Build
    
    Adopt --> Implement
    Extend --> Implement
    Build --> Implement
```

Sources: [rules/common/development-workflow.md:9-15](), [skills/search-first/SKILL.md:12-61]()

### TDD Enforcement

The `testing.md` rule requires TDD with 80%+ coverage. This is enforced through:

1. **Rules layer:** `testing.md` sets the requirement
2. **Skills layer:** `tdd-workflow/SKILL.md` defines RED-GREEN-IMPROVE process
3. **Commands layer:** `/tdd` command invokes `tdd-guide` agent with the skill
4. **Agents layer:** `tdd-guide.md` enforces the workflow
5. **Hooks layer:** PostToolUse hooks run coverage checks

Sources: [rules/common/testing.md](), [skills/tdd-workflow/](), [agents/tdd-guide.md]()

