## Rules and Cross-Platform Support

### Cursor IDE

Cursor rules use YAML frontmatter with `description`, `globs`, and `alwaysApply` fields:

```yaml
---
description: "TypeScript coding style extending common rules"
globs: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# TypeScript Patterns

(rule content)
```

The installer automatically converts ECC rules to Cursor format when using `--target cursor`.

Sources: [README.md:847-856](), [.cursor/rules/]()

### OpenCode

OpenCode rules use a similar structure to Claude Code and can be copied directly.

### Codex CLI

Codex supplements rules with an `AGENTS.md` file that includes rule references. Rules are stored in `.agents/` directory.

Sources: [README.md:862-878](), [.codex/config.toml]()

