## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| Rules not being applied | Not installed in correct directory | Verify `~/.claude/rules/` or `.claude/rules/` exists and contains .md files |
| Language-specific rules incomplete | Missing common rules | Always install common rules first: `./install.sh common typescript` |
| Path references broken | Project-level install references `~/.claude/` | Run configure-ecc wizard Step 4 verification to find and fix |
| Rules conflict with skills | Overlapping directives | Rules take precedence; adjust skills to complement rules |
| Installation script fails | File permissions | Run with sudo or check directory permissions |

### Verification Checklist

```bash
# 1. Check rules directory exists
test -d ~/.claude/rules && echo "✓ User-level rules directory exists"
test -d .claude/rules && echo "✓ Project-level rules directory exists"

# 2. Count rules files
echo "User-level rules: $(find ~/.claude/rules -name '*.md' 2>/dev/null | wc -l)"
echo "Project-level rules: $(find .claude/rules -name '*.md' 2>/dev/null | wc -l)"

# 3. Check for common rules
test -f ~/.claude/rules/coding-style.md && echo "✓ Common rules installed"

# 4. Check for language-specific rules
test -f ~/.claude/rules/typescript-patterns.md && echo "✓ TypeScript rules installed"
test -f ~/.claude/rules/python-patterns.md && echo "✓ Python rules installed"
test -f ~/.claude/rules/golang-patterns.md && echo "✓ Go rules installed"

# 5. Verify cross-references
grep -r "See \[common/" ~/.claude/rules/ || echo "✓ No broken common/ references"
```

Sources: [skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md:200-244](), [skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md:315-327]()

