## Summary

The hooks system provides 8 event interception points across the Claude Code lifecycle, enabling validation (PreToolUse blocking), quality enforcement (PostToolUse auto-fix/warn), observation (continuous learning capture), and context management (session persistence). Hooks communicate via stdin/stdout JSON protocol, use exit codes for control flow, and can run synchronously (blocking) or asynchronously (background).

**Key Integration Points:**
- Session management: Load/save context across invocations ([Session Management System](#7))
- Continuous learning: Capture observations for instinct generation ([Continuous Learning System](#8))
- Quality pipeline: Auto-format, type-check, console.log detection (Diagram 6 in prompt)
- Package management: Detect environment on SessionStart ([Package Manager System](#11.5))

