## Stdin JSON Protocol

PostToolUse hooks receive JSON on stdin with both input and output:

```json
{
  "tool_input": {
    "file_path": "src/auth.ts",
    "instructions": "Add input validation",
    "line_range": [45, 60]
  },
  "tool_output": {
    "output": "Successfully edited src/auth.ts",
    "status": "success"
  }
}
```

**For Bash tools:**

```json
{
  "tool_input": {
    "command": "gh pr create --title 'Add auth' --body '...'"
  },
  "tool_output": {
    "output": "Creating pull request...\nhttps://github.com/owner/repo/pull/123",
    "exit_code": 0
  }
}
```

**Input parsing pattern** (all hooks follow this):

```javascript
let data = '';
process.stdin.on('data', chunk => {
  if (data.length < MAX_STDIN) {
    data += chunk.substring(0, MAX_STDIN - data.length);
  }
});

process.stdin.on('end', () => {
  try {
    const input = JSON.parse(data);
    const filePath = input.tool_input?.file_path;
    const output = input.tool_output?.output;
    // ... process ...
  } catch {
    // Invalid input - pass through
  }
  process.stdout.write(data); // Always pass through
  process.exit(0); // Always exit 0
});
```

Sources: [scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js:17-26](), [scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js:16-29](), [scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js:14-24]()

