## Hook 2: post-edit-typecheck.js

**Purpose:** Run TypeScript type checking after editing .ts/.tsx files, reporting only errors in the edited file.

**Matcher:** `Edit` only

**Registration:**
```json
{
  "matcher": "Edit",
  "hooks": [{
    "type": "command",
    "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\""
  }],
  "description": "TypeScript check after editing .ts/.tsx files"
}
```

### Type Checking Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["Edit src/auth.ts completes"]
    CheckExt{"File matches<br/>.ts or .tsx?"}
    Resolve["path.resolve(filePath)"]
    FileExists{"fs.existsSync()?"}
    
    FindConfig["Walk up from dirname<br/>max 20 levels"]
    CheckTsconfig{"tsconfig.json<br/>exists in dir?"}
    MoveUp["dir = path.dirname(dir)"]
    FoundConfig{"Found tsconfig?"}
    
    RunTsc["execFileSync(<br/>npxBin, ['tsc', '--noEmit',<br/>'--pretty', 'false']<br/>)"]
    CatchError["Catch: tsc exits non-zero<br/>when errors exist"]
    
    ComputePaths["candidates = Set([<br/>filePath,<br/>resolvedPath,<br/>path.relative(dir, resolvedPath)<br/>])"]
    FilterLines["output.split('\\n')<br/>.filter(line => candidates.includes)"]
    SliceTop10["relevantLines.slice(0, 10)"]
    
    OutputStderr["console.error(<br/>'[Hook] TypeScript errors'<br/>)"]
    Exit["stdout.write(data)<br/>exit(0)"]
    
    Start --> CheckExt
    CheckExt -->|No| Exit
    CheckExt -->|Yes| Resolve
    Resolve --> FileExists
    FileExists -->|No| Exit
    FileExists -->|Yes| FindConfig
    
    FindConfig --> CheckTsconfig
    CheckTsconfig -->|No| MoveUp
    MoveUp --> CheckTsconfig
    CheckTsconfig -->|Yes| FoundConfig
    FoundConfig -->|No| Exit
    FoundConfig -->|Yes| RunTsc
    
    RunTsc --> CatchError
    CatchError --> ComputePaths
    ComputePaths --> FilterLines
    FilterLines --> SliceTop10
    SliceTop10 --> OutputStderr
    OutputStderr --> Exit
```

### Path Matching Strategy

**Problem:** TypeScript outputs errors with paths relative to `tsconfig.json` directory, but hook receives original file path from tool input.

**Solution:** Check multiple path representations:

```javascript
const relPath = path.relative(dir, resolvedPath);
const candidates = new Set([
  filePath,        // "src/auth.ts" (original input)
  resolvedPath,    // "/home/user/project/src/auth.ts" (absolute)
  relPath          // "src/auth.ts" (relative to tsconfig dir)
]);

const relevantLines = output.split('\n').filter(line => {
  for (const candidate of candidates) {
    if (line.includes(candidate)) return true;
  }
  return false;
});
```

**Why not basename matching?**

Causes false positives when multiple files share the same name (e.g., `src/utils.ts` vs `tests/utils.ts`). Line 68 comment explains this explicitly.

### Example Output

```
[Hook] TypeScript errors in auth.ts:
src/auth.ts(47,5): error TS2322: Type 'string | undefined' is not assignable to type 'string'.
src/auth.ts(52,10): error TS2339: Property 'email' does not exist on type 'User'.
```

**Characteristics:**
- Max 10 lines shown (line 79 `.slice(0, 10)`)
- Only errors in edited file
- `--pretty false` prevents ANSI color codes
- Timeout: 30 seconds [line 59]

Sources: [scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js:1-97](), [hooks/hooks.json:125-134]()

