## Hook 4: gh pr create Detector (Inline)

**Purpose:** Extract and log PR URL after `gh pr create` command completes, providing a `gh pr review` command for quick review.

**Matcher:** `Bash` only

**Registration:**
```json
{
  "matcher": "Bash",
  "hooks": [{
    "type": "command",
    "command": "node -e \"let d='';process.stdin.on('data',c=>d+=c);process.stdin.on('end',()=>{try{const i=JSON.parse(d);const cmd=i.tool_input?.command||'';if(/gh pr create/.test(cmd)){const out=i.tool_output?.output||'';const m=out.match(/https:\\/\\/github.com\\/[^/]+\\/[^/]+\\/pull\\/\\d+/);if(m){console.error('[Hook] PR created: '+m[0]);const repo=m[0].replace(/https:\\/\\/github.com\\/([^/]+\\/[^/]+)\\/pull\\/\\d+/,'$1');const pr=m[0].replace(/.+\\/pull\\/(\\d+)/,'$1');console.error('[Hook] To review: gh pr review '+pr+' --repo '+repo)}}}catch{}console.log(d)})\""
  }],
  "description": "Log PR URL and provide review command after PR creation"
}
```

### Inline Hook Pattern

**Why inline?** Single-purpose, simple logic doesn't justify a separate file.

**Readable version:**

```javascript
let d = '';
process.stdin.on('data', c => d += c);
process.stdin.on('end', () => {
  try {
    const i = JSON.parse(d);
    const cmd = i.tool_input?.command || '';
    
    if (/gh pr create/.test(cmd)) {
      const out = i.tool_output?.output || '';
      const m = out.match(/https:\/\/github.com\/[^/]+\/[^/]+\/pull\/\d+/);
      
      if (m) {
        console.error('[Hook] PR created: ' + m[0]);
        
        const repo = m[0].replace(
          /https:\/\/github.com\/([^/]+\/[^/]+)\/pull\/\d+/, 
          '$1'
        );
        const pr = m[0].replace(/.+\/pull\/(\d+)/, '$1');
        
        console.error('[Hook] To review: gh pr review ' + pr + ' --repo ' + repo);
      }
    }
  } catch {}
  console.log(d);
});
```

### Example Output

```
[Hook] PR created: https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/123
[Hook] To review: gh pr review 123 --repo owner/repo
```

Sources: [hooks/hooks.json:93-102]()

