## SessionStart Hook

The `SessionStart` hook executes when a new Claude Code session initializes. It loads persisted context from previous sessions and detects the project's package manager configuration.

### Execution Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Claude as "Claude Session"
    participant Hook as "SessionStart Hook"
    participant Script as "session-start.js"
    participant FS as "~/.claude/sessions/"
    participant PM as "Package Manager"
    
    Claude->>Hook: "Session initialized"
    Hook->>Script: "Execute node script"
    Script->>FS: "Read session files"
    FS-->>Script: "Previous context (if exists)"
    Script->>PM: "Detect package manager"
    PM-->>Script: "npm|pnpm|yarn|bun"
    Script->>Claude: "Output to stderr: Session info"
    Script->>Claude: "Package manager detected"
    Note over Claude: "Session ready with context"
```

Sources: [hooks/hooks.json:68-79](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:88-102]()

### Implementation

The hook is configured to execute `session-start.js` on any session start:

```json
"SessionStart": [
  {
    "matcher": "*",
    "hooks": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/session-start.js\""
      }
    ],
    "description": "Load previous context and detect package manager on new session"
  }
]
```

Sources: [hooks/hooks.json:68-79]()

### session-start.js Implementation Details

The `session-start.js` script performs four operations:

#### Session Context Discovery

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["session-start.js"]
    GetDirs["getSessionsDir()<br/>getLearnedSkillsDir()"]
    EnsureDirs["ensureDir(): Create if missing"]
    FindRecent["findFiles('*-session.tmp', maxAge: 7)"]
    FindSkills["findFiles('*.md')"]
    ListAliases["listAliases(limit: 5)"]
    DetectPM["getPackageManager()"]
    LogOutput["log() to stderr"]
    
    Start --> GetDirs
    GetDirs --> EnsureDirs
    EnsureDirs --> FindRecent
    FindRecent --> FindSkills
    FindSkills --> ListAliases
    ListAliases --> DetectPM
    DetectPM --> LogOutput
```

Sources: [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:1-72]()

#### Code Entity Map

| Function | Source | Purpose |
|----------|--------|---------|
| `getSessionsDir()` | [scripts/lib/utils.js:32-35]() | Returns `~/.claude/sessions/` path |
| `getLearnedSkillsDir()` | [scripts/lib/utils.js:45-49]() | Returns `~/.claude/skills/learned/` path |
| `ensureDir()` | [scripts/lib/utils.js:61-66]() | Creates directory if missing |
| `findFiles()` | [scripts/lib/utils.js:139-186]() | Cross-platform file search with age filter |
| `listAliases()` | [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js]() | Loads named session mappings |
| `getPackageManager()` | [scripts/lib/package-manager.js]() | Detects npm/pnpm/yarn/bun |
| `log()` | [scripts/lib/utils.js:219-221]() | Writes to stderr for user visibility |

Sources: [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:11-17](), [scripts/lib/utils.js:32-49,61-66,139-186,219-221]()

#### Operations Performed

1. **Session File Discovery**: Searches `~/.claude/sessions/` for `*-session.tmp` files modified within last 7 days
2. **Learned Skills Check**: Counts available learned skills in `~/.claude/skills/learned/`
3. **Session Aliases**: Lists up to 5 named sessions for `/sessions load <alias>` command
4. **Package Manager Detection**: Identifies project package manager and configuration source

The script outputs all findings to stderr for user visibility but does not block session initialization if context loading fails.

Sources: [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:21-72]()

### Session Context Persistence

Session state is stored in `~/.claude/sessions/` with the filename pattern:

```
YYYY-MM-DD-{sessionId}-session.tmp
```

Where `{sessionId}` is derived from `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` environment variable (last 8 characters) or defaults to `"default"`.

| Environment Variable | Purpose | Default |
|---------------------|---------|---------|
| `CLAUDE_SESSION_ID` | Unique session identifier | `"default"` |
| `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` | Plugin installation directory | Required |

Sources: [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:113-143]()

## Stop Hook

The `Stop` hook executes after each assistant response completes. It performs lightweight validation checks on modified files.

### Purpose

The `Stop` hook enables post-response quality checks without blocking the response itself. The primary use case is warning developers about code quality issues (e.g., leftover `console.log` statements).

### Implementation: check-console-log.js

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Stop["Stop Event Fired"]
    ReadStdin["Read stdin (hook data)"]
    CheckGit{"In git<br/>repository?"}
    GetModified["Get modified files<br/>git diff --name-only HEAD"]
    FilterFiles["Filter .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx files"]
    CheckEach["Check each file for console.log"]
    WarnFound["console.error: WARNING messages"]
    PassThrough["console.log: Pass through stdin"]
    
    Stop --> ReadStdin
    ReadStdin --> CheckGit
    CheckGit -->|No| PassThrough
    CheckGit -->|Yes| GetModified
    GetModified --> FilterFiles
    FilterFiles --> CheckEach
    CheckEach --> WarnFound
    WarnFound --> PassThrough
```

Sources: [scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js:1-62]()

### Code Entity Map

The `check-console-log.js` script interacts with:

- **Git**: `git diff --name-only HEAD` to identify modified files [scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js:34-38]()
- **File System**: `fs.existsSync()` and `fs.readFileSync()` to read file contents [scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js:39,45]()
- **Stdin Protocol**: Reads JSON hook data from stdin, passes through to stdout [scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js:18-20,60]()

### Hook Configuration

```json
"Stop": [
  {
    "matcher": "*",
    "hooks": [
      {
        "type": "command",
        "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\""
      }
    ],
    "description": "Check for console.log in modified files after each response"
  }
]
```

The `Stop` hook runs on every response (`matcher: "*"`) and provides warnings via stderr without blocking execution.

Sources: [hooks/hooks.json:134-145](), [scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js:1-62]()

