## Hook Validation Schema

The CI validation enforces these rules:

```mermaid
graph TB
    hookEntry["Hook Entry"] --> checkType{"Has 'type'<br/>field?"}
    checkType -->|No| failType["❌ FAIL:<br/>Missing 'type'"]
    checkType -->|Yes| checkCommand{"Has 'command'<br/>field?"}
    
    checkCommand -->|No| failCommand["❌ FAIL:<br/>Missing 'command'"]
    checkCommand -->|Yes| checkAsync{"Has 'async'<br/>field?"}
    
    checkAsync -->|Yes| validateAsync{"Is boolean?"}
    validateAsync -->|No| failAsync["❌ FAIL:<br/>'async' must be boolean"]
    validateAsync -->|Yes| checkTimeout
    checkAsync -->|No| checkTimeout
    
    checkTimeout{"Has 'timeout'<br/>field?"} -->|Yes| validateTimeout{"Is number >= 0?"}
    validateTimeout -->|No| failTimeout["❌ FAIL:<br/>'timeout' must be >= 0"]
    validateTimeout -->|Yes| checkInline
    checkTimeout -->|No| checkInline
    
    checkInline{"Is inline JS<br/>(node -e)?"}
    checkInline -->|Yes| validateJS{"Valid JS<br/>syntax?"}
    validateJS -->|No| failJS["❌ FAIL:<br/>Invalid inline JS"]
    validateJS -->|Yes| pass
    checkInline -->|No| pass["✅ PASS"]
```

**Sources:** [tests/ci/validators.test.js:239-354](), [scripts/ci/validate-hooks.js:1-200+]()

**Validation rules:**
1. `type` field required (must be `"command"`)
2. `command` field required (non-empty string)
3. `async` field optional (must be boolean if present)
4. `timeout` field optional (must be number >= 0 if present)
5. Inline JS (node -e "...") must have valid syntax

