### Session Metadata Structure

The `parseSessionMetadata()` function extracts structured data from markdown session files using regex patterns:

| Field | Pattern | Example |
|-------|---------|---------|
| `title` | `^#\s+(.+)$` (first H1) | `"Authentication Refactor"` |
| `date` | `\*\*Date:\*\*\s*(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})` | `"2026-02-01"` |
| `started` | `\*\*Started:\*\*\s*([\d:]+)` | `"10:30"` |
| `lastUpdated` | `\*\*Last Updated:\*\*\s*([\d:]+)` | `"14:45"` |
| `completed` | `### Completed\n...- \[x\]\s*(.+)` | `["Set up project", "Write tests"]` |
| `inProgress` | `### In Progress\n...- \[ \]\s*(.+)` | `["Fix bug"]` |
| `notes` | `### Notes for Next Session\n([\s\S]*?)` | `"Remember to check logs"` |
| `context` | `### Context to Load\n\`\`\`\n([\s\S]*?)\`\`\`` | `"src/main.ts\nlib/utils.js"` |

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:76-149]()

