    end
    
    subgraph "Sorting & Pagination"
        Sort["Sort by mtime<br/>(newest first)"]
        Slice["slice(offset, offset+limit)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Output"
        Result["Return:<br/>{sessions[], total, offset, limit, hasMore}"]
    end
    
    Limit --> ValidateLimit
    Offset --> ValidateOffset
    ValidateOffset --> DateFilter
    ValidateLimit --> Slice
    Date --> DateFilter
    Search --> SearchFilter
    DateFilter --> SearchFilter
    SearchFilter --> Sort
    Sort --> Slice
    Slice --> Result
```

**Pagination Robustness:** The function clamps `NaN`, negative, and `Infinity` offset/limit values to prevent unexpected slice behavior [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:204-207]().

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:184-271](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:368-816]()

### Session ID Resolution

The `getSessionById()` function supports multiple lookup methods:

| Lookup Type | Example Input | Match Strategy |
|-------------|---------------|----------------|
| Short ID prefix | `"abc"` or `"abcd1234"` | `metadata.shortId.startsWith(sessionId)` |
| Full filename | `"2026-02-01-abcd1234-session.tmp"` | Exact filename match |
| Filename without extension | `"2026-02-01-abcd1234-session"` | Add `.tmp` and match |
| Legacy filename (no ID) | `"2026-02-10-session"` | Match legacy format |

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:274-332](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:428-480]()

