## Session Aliases System

The aliases system provides human-readable names for sessions, stored in `~/.claude/session-aliases.json` with atomic write operations.

### Aliases Storage Format

```json
{
  "version": "1.0",
  "aliases": {
    "my-session": {
      "sessionPath": "/path/to/2026-02-01-abc12345-session.tmp",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-01T10:30:00.000Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-02-01T14:45:00.000Z",
      "title": "Authentication Refactor"
    }
  },
  "metadata": {
    "totalCount": 1,
    "lastUpdated": "2026-02-01T14:45:00.000Z"
  }
}
```

### Alias Resolution Flow

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Input Validation"
        Input["Input: alias string"]
        ValidateEmpty["Check: !alias → return null"]
        ValidateChars["Check: /^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/<br/>→ return null if invalid"]
        ValidateReserved["Check: ['list', 'help', 'remove', ...]<br/>→ return error if reserved"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Alias Lookup"
        LoadFile["loadAliases()<br/>→ parse session-aliases.json"]
        CheckExists["aliases[alias]<br/>→ aliasData or undefined"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Resolution Result"
        Found["Return:<br/>{alias, sessionPath, createdAt, title}"]
        NotFound["Return: null"]
    end
    
    Input --> ValidateEmpty
    ValidateEmpty --> ValidateChars
    ValidateChars --> ValidateReserved
    ValidateReserved --> LoadFile
    LoadFile --> CheckExists
    CheckExists -->|exists| Found
    CheckExists -->|not exists| NotFound
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js:154-179](), [tests/lib/session-aliases.test.js:148-174]()

### Alias API Functions

| Function | Signature | Purpose |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| `setAlias` | `(alias, sessionPath, title?) → {success, isNew, alias, ...}` | Create or update alias |
| `resolveAlias` | `(alias) → {alias, sessionPath, createdAt, title} \| null` | Get session path from alias |
| `listAliases` | `(options?) → [{name, sessionPath, createdAt, ...}]` | List all aliases with search/limit |
| `deleteAlias` | `(alias) → {success, alias, deletedSessionPath}` | Remove alias |
| `renameAlias` | `(oldAlias, newAlias) → {success, oldAlias, newAlias, ...}` | Rename with validation |
| `updateAliasTitle` | `(alias, title) → {success, alias, title}` | Update title field |
| `getAliasesForSession` | `(sessionPath) → [{name, createdAt, title}]` | Find all aliases for a path |
| `cleanupAliases` | `(sessionExistsFn) → {totalChecked, removed, removedAliases[]}` | Remove stale aliases |

**Validation Rules:**
- Alias name: 1-128 characters, `/^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$/`
- Reserved names: `'list'`, `'help'`, `'remove'`, `'delete'`, `'create'`, `'set'`
- Session path: non-empty string

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js:188-457](), [tests/lib/session-aliases.test.js:88-580]()

### Atomic Write Operations

The `saveAliases()` function implements atomic writes with backup/restore:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Caller
    participant SaveFn as "saveAliases()"
    participant FS as "File System"
    
    Caller->>SaveFn: aliases object
    SaveFn->>SaveFn: Update metadata<br/>(totalCount, lastUpdated)
    SaveFn->>FS: copyFileSync(aliases.json → aliases.json.bak)
    SaveFn->>FS: writeFileSync(aliases.json.tmp, content)
    
    alt Windows Platform
        SaveFn->>FS: unlinkSync(aliases.json)<br/>(delete before rename)
    end
    
    SaveFn->>FS: renameSync(aliases.json.tmp → aliases.json)
    SaveFn->>FS: unlinkSync(aliases.json.bak)
    SaveFn->>Caller: return true
    
    Note over SaveFn,FS: On error: restore from backup
```

**Platform Differences:** Windows requires deleting the destination before `rename()` due to EEXIST behavior, while Unix/macOS atomically replaces [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js:116-119]().

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js:83-151](), [tests/lib/session-aliases.test.js:519-544]()

