## Session Lifecycle and Persistence

Session hooks bridge context across independent Claude invocations by loading previous session content and saving session summaries.

### Session Lifecycle Hooks Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Claude as "Claude Code Instance"
    participant StartHook as "session-start.js"
    participant EndHook as "session-end.js"
    participant PreCompact as "pre-compact.js"
    participant SessionMgr as "Session Manager"
    participant Aliases as "Aliases System"
    
    User->>Claude: Start session (claude -p)
    Claude->>StartHook: SessionStart hook
    StartHook->>SessionMgr: getAllSessions({limit: 1})<br/>(get most recent)
    StartHook->>StartHook: Check for template content:<br/>"[Session context goes here]"
    alt Real session content
        StartHook->>Claude: Inject previous session summary<br/>to stdout
    else Template content
        StartHook->>Claude: Skip injection
    end
    StartHook->>StartHook: Detect package manager<br/>(via package-manager.js)
    StartHook->>StartHook: Count learned skills<br/>(~/.claude/skills/learned/*.md)
    StartHook->>Claude: Log session info to stderr
    
    Note over User,Claude: User works with Claude
    
    User->>Claude: /compact command
    Claude->>PreCompact: PreCompact hook
    PreCompact->>SessionMgr: getAllSessions({limit: 1})
    PreCompact->>PreCompact: Append compaction marker<br/>to session file
    PreCompact->>PreCompact: Write compaction log<br/>(compaction-log.txt)
    
    User->>Claude: End session or timeout
    Claude->>EndHook: SessionEnd hook
    EndHook->>EndHook: Read transcript.jsonl
    EndHook->>EndHook: Extract user messages<br/>Extract tool uses<br/>Extract file modifications
    EndHook->>SessionMgr: writeSessionContent()<br/>(YYYY-MM-DD-shortid-session.tmp)
```

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:1-167](), [scripts/hooks/session-end.js:1-230](), [scripts/hooks/pre-compact.js:1-130]()

### SessionStart Hook: Previous Session Loading

The `session-start.js` hook loads the most recent session file and injects it as context:

**Template Content Detection:** Sessions with placeholder text `"[Session context goes here]"` are skipped to avoid injecting empty templates [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:129-152]().

**Context Injection Format:**
```markdown
Previous session summary:
<session content>

Continue from where the previous session left off.
```

**Package Manager Detection:** Uses the 6-level priority cascade from `package-manager.js` to detect and report the current package manager [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:65-74]().

**Learned Skills Count:** Counts `*.md` files in `~/.claude/skills/learned/` and reports to stderr [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:77-91]().

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:1-167](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:87-204]()

### SessionEnd Hook: Summary Extraction

The `session-end.js` hook reads `transcript.jsonl` and extracts structured summaries:

**Extraction Logic:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Transcript Parsing"
        ReadTranscript["Read transcript.jsonl<br/>(if CLAUDE_TRANSCRIPT_PATH set)"]
        ParseLines["Parse JSONL lines"]
        FilterUser["Filter: type === 'user'"]
        FilterToolUse["Filter: type === 'tool_use'"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Content Extraction"
        UserMessages["Extract user messages:<br/>- content string<br/>- content[].text array"]
        ToolUses["Extract tool uses:<br/>- tool_name<br/>- tool_input.file_path"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Summary Generation"
        FormatDate["Format: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM"]
        BuildMarkdown["Build markdown:<br/>## Session: {date}<br/>**Started:** {time}<br/><br/>### User Messages<br/>{messages}<br/><br/>### Tools Used<br/>{tools}<br/><br/>### Files Modified<br/>{files}"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Persistence"
        SessionId["getSessionIdShort()<br/>(last 8 chars of CLAUDE_SESSION_ID)"]
        FilePath["~/.claude/sessions/<br/>YYYY-MM-DD-{shortId}-session.tmp"]
        WriteFile["writeSessionContent()"]
    end
    
    ReadTranscript --> ParseLines
    ParseLines --> FilterUser
    ParseLines --> FilterToolUse
    FilterUser --> UserMessages
    FilterToolUse --> ToolUses
    UserMessages --> BuildMarkdown
    ToolUses --> BuildMarkdown
    BuildMarkdown --> FormatDate
    FormatDate --> SessionId
    SessionId --> FilePath
