## Strategic Compaction System

The strategic compaction system suggests manual `/compact` invocations at logical workflow boundaries instead of auto-compacting at arbitrary points.

### Compaction Strategy Rationale

**Why Manual Over Auto-Compact:**
- Auto-compact happens mid-task at arbitrary tool call counts
- Strategic compaction preserves context through logical phases
- Compact after exploration, before execution
- Compact after milestone completion, before starting next task

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js:6-13]()

### Threshold Algorithm

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Initialization"
        SessionId["sessionId = CLAUDE_SESSION_ID<br/>|| 'default'"]
        CounterFile["counterFile = /tmp/claude-tool-count-{sessionId}"]
        Threshold["threshold = COMPACT_THRESHOLD<br/>|| 50<br/>(clamped: 1-10000)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Counter Management"
        ReadCount["Read counter file<br/>using fs.openSync('a+')"]
        ParseCount["Parse count:<br/>parseInt(buf, 10)"]
        ValidateCount["Validate:<br/>isFinite && > 0 && <= 1000000"]
        IncrementCount["count = parsed + 1<br/>or 1 if invalid"]
        WriteCount["Truncate and write:<br/>fs.ftruncateSync(fd, 0)<br/>fs.writeSync(fd, count)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Suggestion Logic"
        CheckThreshold{"count === threshold?"}
        CheckInterval{"count > threshold<br/>&&<br/>(count - threshold) % 25 === 0?"}
        SuggestInitial["Log: '{threshold} tool calls reached -<br/>consider /compact if transitioning phases'"]
        SuggestInterval["Log: '{count} tool calls -<br/>good checkpoint for /compact if context is stale'"]
    end
    
    SessionId --> CounterFile
    CounterFile --> ReadCount
    ReadCount --> ParseCount
    ParseCount --> ValidateCount
    ValidateCount --> IncrementCount
    IncrementCount --> WriteCount
    WriteCount --> CheckThreshold
    CheckThreshold -->|Yes| SuggestInitial
    CheckThreshold -->|No| CheckInterval
    CheckInterval -->|Yes| SuggestInterval
```

**Threshold Behavior:**
1. **First suggestion:** Exactly at threshold (default 50)
2. **Subsequent suggestions:** Every 25 tool calls after threshold (75, 100, 125, ...)

**Counter Persistence:** Uses `fs.openSync()` with `'a+'` mode and `ftruncateSync()` to reduce (but not eliminate) race conditions between concurrent hook invocations [scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js:40-58]().

**Counter Validation:** Clamps parsed values to `1-1000000` range to prevent corrupted files with huge values from causing issues [scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js:49-51]().

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js:1-81](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:340-478]()

### Counter File Robustness

The counter file handling includes fallback logic:

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Primary Path (fd-based)"
        Open["fs.openSync(counterFile, 'a+')"]
        Read["fs.readSync(fd, buf)"]
        Parse["parseInt(buf)"]
        Truncate["fs.ftruncateSync(fd, 0)"]
        Write["fs.writeSync(fd, count)"]
        Close["fs.closeSync(fd)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Fallback Path"
        WriteFileFallback["writeFile(counterFile, count)"]
    end
    
    Open -->|success| Read
    Read --> Parse
    Parse --> Truncate
    Truncate --> Write
    Write --> Close
    Open -->|error| WriteFileFallback
```

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js:40-62]()

