</details>



This document describes the file naming convention, markdown structure, and metadata format used by session files in Everything Claude Code. Session files persist conversation state and project context across independent Claude Code invocations, enabling cross-session memory and continuity.

For information about programmatic access to session files, see [Session Manager API](#7.2). For human-readable aliases for session identification, see [Session Aliases System](#7.3). For session creation and persistence behavior, see [Session Lifecycle & Persistence](#7.4).

---

## File Naming Convention

Session files follow a strict naming convention with date validation and optional session identification:

### Format Specification

```
YYYY-MM-DD-shortid-session.tmp
```

**Components:**
- `YYYY-MM-DD`: ISO 8601 date (validated for calendar correctness)
- `shortid`: 8+ character lowercase alphanumeric identifier
- Extension: `.tmp`

**Examples:**
- New format: `2026-02-01-a1b2c3d4-session.tmp`
- Legacy format: `2026-01-17-session.tmp` (no short ID)

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:51-86](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:617-654]()

### Short ID Specification

```mermaid
graph LR
    EnvVar["CLAUDE_SESSION_ID<br/>env variable"]
    Extract["Extract last<br/>8 characters"]
    Validate["Validate:<br/>• 8+ chars<br/>• Lowercase a-z<br/>• Digits 0-9"]
    ShortID["shortid field"]
    Fallback["Fallback:<br/>'no-id'"]
    
    EnvVar --> Extract
    Extract --> Validate
    Validate -->|Valid| ShortID
    Validate -->|Invalid/Missing| Fallback
```

**Validation Rules:**
- Minimum length: 8 characters
- Character set: `[a-z0-9]` only (no uppercase, no special characters)
- Rejection cases: `< 8 chars`, contains uppercase, contains special characters

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:77-86](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:581-589]()

### Date Validation

The filename parser validates calendar correctness to prevent malformed session files:

| Validation | Rule | Examples |
|------------|------|----------|
| Month range | 01-12 | Rejects: `00`, `13` |
| Day range | 01-31 | Rejects: `00`, `32` |
| 30-day months | Apr, Jun, Sep, Nov | Rejects: `2026-04-31`, `2026-09-31` |
| February leap year | 29 days in leap years only | Accepts: `2024-02-29`, Rejects: `2025-02-29` |
| February non-leap | 28 days max | Rejects: `2025-02-29`, `2026-02-30` |

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:591-648]()

---

## Session File Structure

Session files use markdown format with structured sections for tasks, notes, and context. The structure enables both human readability and programmatic parsing.

### Markdown Template

```markdown
# Session Title

**Date:** 2026-02-01
**Started:** 10:30
**Last Updated:** 14:45

### Completed
- [x] Set up project structure
- [x] Write initial tests

### In Progress
- [ ] Implement authentication
- [ ] Add error handling

### Notes for Next Session
Remember to check the database migration logs before proceeding.

### Context to Load
```
src/main.ts
lib/auth.ts
```
```

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:92-123]()

