## Metadata Fields

Session metadata is extracted by `parseSessionMetadata()` function from markdown content. All fields are optional.

### Field Specification

| Field | Format | Example | Extraction Rule |
|-------|--------|---------|-----------------|
| `title` | H1 heading | `# My Session Title` | First H1 heading in file |
| `date` | `**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD` | `**Date:** 2026-02-01` | Matches `**Date:**` pattern |
| `started` | `**Started:** HH:MM` | `**Started:** 10:30` | Matches `**Started:**` pattern |
| `lastUpdated` | `**Last Updated:** HH:MM` | `**Last Updated:** 14:45` | Matches `**Last Updated:**` pattern |
| `completed` | Array of strings | `['Task 1', 'Task 2']` | Extracts text from `- [x]` items |
| `inProgress` | Array of strings | `['Task 3']` | Extracts text from `- [ ]` items |
| `notes` | String | `'Remember to test'` | Content after `### Notes for Next Session` |
| `context` | String | `'src/main.ts\nlib/utils.js'` | Content inside ` ``` ` block after `### Context to Load` |

### Code Entity Mapping

```mermaid
graph TB
    parseSessionMetadata["parseSessionMetadata(content)"]
    
    TitleExtract["RegExp: /^# (.+)$/m"]
    DateExtract["RegExp: /\*\*Date:\*\* (.+)/"]
    StartedExtract["RegExp: /\*\*Started:\*\* (.+)/"]
    UpdatedExtract["RegExp: /\*\*Last Updated:\*\* (.+)/"]
    
    CompletedExtract["RegExp: /^- \[x\] (.+)$/gm"]
    InProgressExtract["RegExp: /^- \[ \] (.+)$/gm"]
    
    NotesExtract["Section: ### Notes for Next Session"]
    ContextExtract["Section: ### Context to Load<br/>Inside ``` block"]
    
    MetadataObj["{<br/>  title,<br/>  date,<br/>  started,<br/>  lastUpdated,<br/>  completed: [],<br/>  inProgress: [],<br/>  notes,<br/>  context<br/>}"]
    
    parseSessionMetadata --> TitleExtract
    parseSessionMetadata --> DateExtract
    parseSessionMetadata --> StartedExtract
    parseSessionMetadata --> UpdatedExtract
    parseSessionMetadata --> CompletedExtract
    parseSessionMetadata --> InProgressExtract
    parseSessionMetadata --> NotesExtract
    parseSessionMetadata --> ContextExtract
    
    TitleExtract --> MetadataObj
    DateExtract --> MetadataObj
    StartedExtract --> MetadataObj
    UpdatedExtract --> MetadataObj
    CompletedExtract --> MetadataObj
    InProgressExtract --> MetadataObj
    NotesExtract --> MetadataObj
    ContextExtract --> MetadataObj
```

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:89-143](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:482-527]()

### Special Cases

**Title Extraction:**
- Takes first H1 heading only (ignores subsequent H1s)
- Whitespace is trimmed from title text
- Returns `null` if no H1 heading found

**Context Block Extraction:**
- Content must be inside triple-backtick fenced code block
- Extracts raw text between backticks (no language identifier expected)
- Preserves line breaks in file path lists

**Checkbox Items:**
- Completed tasks: `- [x] Task text` (matches `[x]` only, case-sensitive)
- In-progress tasks: `- [ ]` with single space inside brackets
- Inline backticks in task text are preserved (e.g., `Fix \`app.js\` bug`)

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:494-527](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:516-520](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:821-843]()

---

## Task Tracking Sections

The `### Completed` and `### In Progress` sections enable persistent task state across sessions. Statistics are computed by `getSessionStats()`.

### Statistics Schema

```javascript
{
  totalItems: number,        // completed + inProgress
  completedItems: number,    // count of [x] items
  inProgressItems: number,   // count of [ ] items
  lineCount: number,         // total lines in file
  hasNotes: boolean,         // presence of Notes section
  hasContext: boolean        // presence of Context section
}
```

### Statistics Computation Diagram

```mermaid
graph LR
    Input["Session file content"]
    
    CountCompleted["Count: - [x]<br/>RegExp matches"]
    CountInProgress["Count: - [ ]<br/>RegExp matches"]
    CountLines["content.split('\\n').length"]
    
    CheckNotes["content.includes('<br/>### Notes for Next Session')"]
    CheckContext["content.includes('<br/>### Context to Load')"]
    
    StatsObj["{<br/>  totalItems,<br/>  completedItems,<br/>  inProgressItems,<br/>  lineCount,<br/>  hasNotes,<br/>  hasContext<br/>}"]
    
    Input --> CountCompleted
    Input --> CountInProgress
    Input --> CountLines
    Input --> CheckNotes
    Input --> CheckContext
    
    CountCompleted --> StatsObj
    CountInProgress --> StatsObj
    CountLines --> StatsObj
    CheckNotes --> StatsObj
    CheckContext --> StatsObj
```

**Empty Content Handling:**
- Empty string (`''`) returns all counts as 0, booleans as `false`
- Null/undefined content returns same defaults as empty string
- Whitespace-only content is treated as content, not empty

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:145-176](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:531-555]()

---

## Legacy Format Support

The system maintains backward compatibility with session files created before the short ID convention was introduced.

### Format Comparison

| Aspect | Legacy Format | Current Format |
|--------|---------------|----------------|
| Filename | `2026-01-17-session.tmp` | `2026-02-01-a1b2c3d4-session.tmp` |
| Short ID | `'no-id'` (sentinel value) | 8+ character alphanumeric |
| Parsing | Via `parseSessionFilename()` | Via `parseSessionFilename()` |
| Resolution | Searchable by filename prefix | Searchable by short ID prefix |

### parseSessionFilename() Behavior

```mermaid
graph TB
    Input["Filename string"]
    
    CheckFormat{"Matches:<br/>YYYY-MM-DD-<br/>shortid-<br/>session.tmp?"}
    
    CheckLegacy{"Matches:<br/>YYYY-MM-DD-<br/>session.tmp?"}
    
    ValidateDate["Calendar validation<br/>(month 01-12,<br/>day 01-31,<br/>leap year)"]
    
    ValidateShortID["Short ID validation<br/>(8+ chars,<br/>lowercase,<br/>alphanumeric)"]
    
    NewFormat["{<br/>  shortId: string,<br/>  date: 'YYYY-MM-DD',<br/>  filename: string,<br/>  datetime: Date<br/>}"]
    
    LegacyFormat["{<br/>  shortId: 'no-id',<br/>  date: 'YYYY-MM-DD',<br/>  filename: string,<br/>  datetime: Date<br/>}"]
    
    ReturnNull["return null"]
    
    Input --> CheckFormat
    CheckFormat -->|Yes| ValidateDate
    ValidateDate -->|Valid| ValidateShortID
    ValidateShortID -->|Valid| NewFormat
    ValidateShortID -->|Invalid| ReturnNull
    
    CheckFormat -->|No| CheckLegacy
    CheckLegacy -->|Yes| ValidateDate
    ValidateDate -->|Invalid| ReturnNull
    CheckLegacy -->|No| ReturnNull
    
    ValidateDate -.->|Legacy path| LegacyFormat
```

**Legacy File Discovery:**
- `getAllSessions()` returns both legacy and new format files
- `getSessionById()` accepts full legacy filename for lookup
- Legacy files sort by modification time like new format files

**Migration Note:** Legacy files are not automatically renamed. They remain valid and fully functional in the system.

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:59-70](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:463-467]()

---

## File Location & Storage

Session files are stored in a standardized directory within the Claude configuration hierarchy:

**Primary Location:**
```
~/.claude/sessions/
```

**Path Resolution:**
- `getSessionsDir()` from utils.js returns absolute path
- Cross-platform (Windows: `%USERPROFILE%\.claude\sessions\`, Unix: `~/.claude/sessions/`)
- Directory is created automatically if missing (via `ensureDir()`)

**File Operations:**
- `writeSessionContent(path, content)` - create or overwrite
- `appendSessionContent(path, content)` - append to existing
- `getSessionContent(path)` - read file content
- `deleteSession(path)` - remove file
- `sessionExists(path)` - check existence

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:181-264]()

---

## Parsing Workflow

The complete flow from filename to structured metadata:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Client
    participant parseSessionFilename
    participant Validator["Date/ID Validator"]
    participant parseSessionMetadata
    participant getSessionStats
    participant FileSystem
    
    Client->>parseSessionFilename: "2026-02-01-a1b2c3d4-session.tmp"
    parseSessionFilename->>Validator: Validate date & shortId
    Validator-->>parseSessionFilename: Valid
    parseSessionFilename-->>Client: {shortId, date, filename, datetime}
    
    Client->>FileSystem: Read session file
    FileSystem-->>Client: Markdown content
    
    Client->>parseSessionMetadata: content
    parseSessionMetadata->>parseSessionMetadata: Extract title (H1)
    parseSessionMetadata->>parseSessionMetadata: Extract date/time fields
    parseSessionMetadata->>parseSessionMetadata: Extract task arrays
    parseSessionMetadata->>parseSessionMetadata: Extract notes & context
    parseSessionMetadata-->>Client: {title, date, started, completed[], ...}
    
    Client->>getSessionStats: content
    getSessionStats->>getSessionStats: Count tasks
    getSessionStats->>getSessionStats: Count lines
    getSessionStats->>getSessionStats: Check sections
    getSessionStats-->>Client: {totalItems, completedItems, lineCount, ...}
```

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:48-143](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:145-169]()

