## Edge Cases & Robustness

The parsing system handles various edge cases gracefully:

### Line Ending Formats

| Format | Support | Example Test |
|--------|---------|--------------|
| Unix LF (`\n`) | ✓ Primary format | Standard markdown |
| Windows CRLF (`\r\n`) | ✓ Fully supported | [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:485-492]() |
| Mixed line endings | ✓ Handled correctly | Normalized during parsing |
| BOM prefix (`\uFEFF`) | ✓ Stripped automatically | [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:184-192]() |

### Content Variations

**Empty Sections:**
- Sections with headers but no items return empty arrays
- Does not cause parsing errors

**Missing Sections:**
- Optional sections return `null` or empty arrays when absent
- Metadata object always returns complete structure with defaults

**Special Characters:**
- Colons in values (e.g., description fields) are handled correctly
- Backticks in task text are preserved
- HTML-like content in notes is not escaped

**Whitespace:**
- Leading/trailing whitespace in title is trimmed
- Whitespace-only content is distinguished from empty content
- Tab characters in content are preserved

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:485-527](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:821-852]()

