## Integration Points

Session file format integrates with multiple system components:

**SessionStart Hook:** Loads previous session content via `getSessionContent()` → `parseSessionMetadata()` to inject context into new conversation ([Session Lifecycle & Persistence](#7.4))

**SessionEnd Hook:** Writes session summary via `writeSessionContent()` with standardized markdown structure ([Session Lifecycle & Persistence](#7.4))

**Session Aliases:** Maps human-readable names to session file paths via `session-aliases.json` ([Session Aliases System](#7.3))

**Session Manager API:** Provides programmatic access to all parsing and I/O operations ([Session Manager API](#7.2))

**Compaction System:** Tracks tool call count per session using short ID for counter file naming ([Strategic Compaction](#7.5))

**Sources:** [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:1-12](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:86-180]()

