## Metadata Extraction

### Session Content Structure

Session files use markdown format with specific sections:

```mermaid
graph TB
    SessionFile["Session File<br/>YYYY-MM-DD-shortid-session.tmp"]
    
    subgraph "Parsed Metadata"
        Title["title: from # heading"]
        DateMeta["date: from **Date:** field"]
        Started["started: from **Started:** field"]
        LastUpdated["lastUpdated: from **Last Updated:** field"]
        Completed["completed[]: from ### Completed<br/>- [x] items"]
        InProgress["inProgress[]: from ### In Progress<br/>- [ ] items"]
        Notes["notes: from ### Notes for Next Session"]
        Context["context: from ### Context to Load"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Computed Statistics"
        TotalItems["totalItems: completed + inProgress count"]
        LineCount["lineCount: total lines"]
        HasNotes["hasNotes: boolean"]
        HasContext["hasContext: boolean"]
    end
    
    SessionFile --> Title
    SessionFile --> DateMeta
    SessionFile --> Started
    SessionFile --> LastUpdated
    SessionFile --> Completed
    SessionFile --> InProgress
    SessionFile --> Notes
    SessionFile --> Context
    
    Completed --> TotalItems
    InProgress --> TotalItems
    SessionFile --> LineCount
    Notes --> HasNotes
    Context --> HasContext
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:80-149](), [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:157-181]()

---

### `parseSessionMetadata(content)`

Extracts structured metadata from session markdown content using regex patterns.

**Parameters:**
- `content` (string): Session markdown content

**Returns:** Metadata object with fields:

| Field | Type | Description | Extraction Pattern |
|-------|------|-------------|-------------------|
| `title` | string\|null | First `#` heading | `/^#\s+(.+)$/m` |
| `date` | string\|null | Date in YYYY-MM-DD format | `/\*\*Date:\*\*\s*(\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2})/` |
| `started` | string\|null | Start time (HH:MM) | `/\*\*Started:\*\*\s*([\d:]+)/` |
| `lastUpdated` | string\|null | Last update time (HH:MM) | `/\*\*Last Updated:\*\*\s*([\d:]+)/` |
| `completed` | string[] | Checked items | `### Completed` section with `- [x]` |
| `inProgress` | string[] | Unchecked items | `### In Progress` section with `- [ ]` |
| `notes` | string | Notes text | `### Notes for Next Session` section |
| `context` | string | Files to load | `### Context to Load` code block |

**Handles edge cases:**
- CRLF line endings (`\r\n`)
- BOM (Byte Order Mark) at file start
- Colons in field values
- Multiple headings (takes first)
- Empty sections
- Inline backticks in task items

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:80-149](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:89-526]()

---

### `getSessionStats(sessionPathOrContent)`

Calculates session statistics. Accepts either a file path or pre-read content string to avoid redundant disk reads.

**Parameters:**
- `sessionPathOrContent` (string): Full path to session file OR pre-read content

**Path detection heuristic:**
- Treats as path if: no newlines, ends with `.tmp`, starts with `/` or drive letter
- Otherwise treats as content

**Returns:** Statistics object:

```javascript
{
  totalItems: 5,           // completed + inProgress count
  completedItems: 3,       // completed count
  inProgressItems: 2,      // inProgress count
  lineCount: 42,           // total lines
  hasNotes: true,          // has notes section
  hasContext: true         // has context section
}
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:157-181](), [tests/lib/session-manager.test.js:144-176]()

