## Purpose and Scope

The Continuous Learning System automatically extracts reusable patterns from Claude Code sessions and converts them into persistent knowledge structures. This page provides an architectural overview of both the v1 (skills-based) and v2 (instinct-based) learning systems, their observation mechanisms, and storage patterns.

For detailed implementation guides, see:
- v1 implementation details: [Continuous Learning v1](#9.1)
- v2 architecture and instincts: [Continuous Learning v2](#9.2)
- Observer agent mechanics: [Observer Agent & Pattern Detection](#9.3)
- Instinct lifecycle: [Instinct Management](#9.4)
- Evolution algorithms: [Evolution Pipeline](#9.5)

## System Architecture Overview

Both learning systems operate as parallel pipelines that observe session activity and generate reusable artifacts. v1 uses a probabilistic skill-based approach, while v2 uses deterministic hook-based observation.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Session Activity"
        USER["User Prompts"]
        CLAUDE["Claude Responses"]
        TOOLS["Tool Executions"]
    end
    
    subgraph "v1: Skills-Based Learning"
        STOP_HOOK["Stop Hook"]
        EVAL_SESSION["evaluate-session.js"]
        LEARNED_SKILLS["~/.claude/skills/learned/"]
    end
    
    subgraph "v2: Instinct-Based Learning"
        PRE_HOOK["PreToolUse Hook"]
        POST_HOOK["PostToolUse Hook"]
        OBS_LOG["observations.jsonl"]
        OBSERVER["Background Observer<br/>(Haiku)"]
        INSTINCTS["~/.claude/homunculus/instincts/"]
        EVOLVE["Evolution Engine"]
        ARTIFACTS["evolved/<br/>commands/skills/agents/"]
    end
    
    USER --> CLAUDE
    CLAUDE --> TOOLS
    TOOLS --> STOP_HOOK
    
    STOP_HOOK -->|"50-80% fire rate"| EVAL_SESSION
    EVAL_SESSION -->|"generates"| LEARNED_SKILLS
    
    TOOLS --> PRE_HOOK
    TOOLS --> POST_HOOK
    PRE_HOOK -->|"100% reliable"| OBS_LOG
    POST_HOOK -->|"100% reliable"| OBS_LOG
    
    OBS_LOG -->|"periodic scan"| OBSERVER
    OBSERVER -->|"creates/updates"| INSTINCTS
    INSTINCTS -->|"cluster threshold"| EVOLVE
    EVOLVE -->|"generates"| ARTIFACTS
```

**Diagram: Parallel Learning Pipelines**

Both systems run simultaneously during the migration period. v1 extracts full skills at session end, while v2 continuously builds atomic instincts from tool observations.

Sources: [README.md:279-290](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:52-89](), [skills/continuous-learning/SKILL.md:10-16]()

## Version Comparison: v1 vs v2

| Feature | v1 (Skills-Based) | v2 (Instinct-Based) |
|---------|-------------------|---------------------|
| **Observation Reliability** | ~50-80% (Stop hook) | 100% (PreToolUse/PostToolUse) |
| **Analysis Context** | Main Claude context | Background Haiku agent |
| **Knowledge Unit** | Complete SKILL.md file | Atomic instinct (single behavior) |
| **Confidence Tracking** | None | 0.3-0.9 weighted scoring |
| **Evolution Path** | Direct session → skill | Instincts → cluster → skill/command/agent |
| **Sharing Mechanism** | Copy SKILL.md files | Export/import instinct collections |
| **Storage Location** | `~/.claude/skills/learned/` | `~/.claude/homunculus/instincts/` |
| **Background Processing** | No | Yes (non-blocking) |

Sources: [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:13-20](), [skills/continuous-learning/SKILL.md:84-97]()

## Observation Mechanisms

### v1: Stop Hook Architecture

v1 uses a single `Stop` hook that fires after each Claude response. The hook invokes `evaluate-session.js`, which analyzes the accumulated session context.

```mermaid
graph LR
    SESSION["Session Messages"]
    STOP["Stop Hook<br/>(after response)"]
    EVAL["evaluate-session.js"]
    CHECK{"Session length<br/>> threshold?"}
    PATTERNS["Pattern Detection"]
    SKILL["SKILL.md Generation"]
    LEARNED["~/.claude/skills/learned/"]
    
    SESSION --> STOP
    STOP -->|"fires ~50-80%"| EVAL
    EVAL --> CHECK
    CHECK -->|"yes"| PATTERNS
    CHECK -->|"no"| SESSION
    PATTERNS --> SKILL
    SKILL --> LEARNED
```

**Diagram: v1 Stop Hook Flow**

The Stop hook is probabilistic—Claude's judgment determines whether patterns are significant enough to extract. This results in 50-80% observation coverage.

Sources: [hooks/hooks.json:134-166](), [skills/continuous-learning/SKILL.md:12-16](), [the-longform-guide.md:96-102]()

### v2: Hook-Based Observation

v2 uses deterministic `PreToolUse` and `PostToolUse` hooks that capture 100% of tool executions. The `observe.sh` script appends structured observations to a JSONL log.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Tool Execution Lifecycle"
        PRE["PreToolUse Event"]
        TOOL["Tool Execution"]
        POST["PostToolUse Event"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Observation Capture"
        OBSERVE_SH["observe.sh"]
        JSONL["observations.jsonl"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Background Analysis"
        OBSERVER["Observer Agent<br/>(Haiku model)"]
        PARSE["Parse JSONL"]
        DETECT["Pattern Detection"]
        INSTINCT["Create/Update Instinct"]
    end
    
    PRE -->|"matcher: *"| OBSERVE_SH
    POST -->|"matcher: *"| OBSERVE_SH
    OBSERVE_SH -->|"append"| JSONL
    
    JSONL -->|"periodic read"| PARSE
    PARSE --> OBSERVER
    OBSERVER --> DETECT
    DETECT -->|"user corrections"| INSTINCT
    DETECT -->|"error resolutions"| INSTINCT
    DETECT -->|"repeated workflows"| INSTINCT
    
    INSTINCT --> PERSONAL["~/.claude/homunculus/instincts/personal/"]
```

**Diagram: v2 Hook-Based Observation Flow**

The hooks are configured with `matcher: "*"` to capture all tool usage. The observer runs in the background without blocking the main session.

Sources: [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:94-118](), [the-longform-guide.md:254-260]()

## Storage Architecture

### File System Layout

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "v1 Storage"
        V1_ROOT["~/.claude/skills/learned/"]
        V1_SKILL1["error-handling-pattern.md"]
        V1_SKILL2["database-query-optimization.md"]
        V1_SKILL3["typescript-validation.md"]
        
        V1_ROOT --> V1_SKILL1
        V1_ROOT --> V1_SKILL2
        V1_ROOT --> V1_SKILL3
    end
    
    subgraph "v2 Storage"
        V2_ROOT["~/.claude/homunculus/"]
        
        OBS["observations.jsonl"]
        ARCHIVE["observations.archive/"]
        
        INSTINCTS["instincts/"]
        PERSONAL["instincts/personal/"]
        INHERITED["instincts/inherited/"]
        
        EVOLVED["evolved/"]
        EV_AGENTS["evolved/agents/"]
        EV_SKILLS["evolved/skills/"]
        EV_COMMANDS["evolved/commands/"]
        
        V2_ROOT --> OBS
        V2_ROOT --> ARCHIVE
        V2_ROOT --> INSTINCTS
        V2_ROOT --> EVOLVED
        
        INSTINCTS --> PERSONAL
        INSTINCTS --> INHERITED
        
        EVOLVED --> EV_AGENTS
        EVOLVED --> EV_SKILLS
        EVOLVED --> EV_COMMANDS
    end
```

**Diagram: Storage Directory Structure**

v1 stores complete skills as markdown files. v2 maintains a separation between raw observations, atomic instincts, and evolved artifacts.

### Observation Log Format

The `observations.jsonl` file stores one JSON object per line:

```json
{
  "timestamp": "2025-01-15T14:32:05Z",
  "event": "PreToolUse",
  "tool": "Edit",
  "tool_input": {"file_path": "src/utils.ts"},
  "context": "user requested functional refactor"
}
```

When the file exceeds 10MB (configurable in `config.json`), it rotates to `observations.archive/YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl`.

Sources: [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:208-222](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:172-206]()

### Instinct File Structure

Each instinct is a markdown file with YAML frontmatter:

```markdown
---
id: prefer-functional-style
trigger: "when writing new functions"
confidence: 0.7
domain: "code-style"
source: "session-observation"
created: "2025-01-15"
last_updated: "2025-01-18"
---

# Prefer Functional Style

## Action
Use functional patterns over classes when appropriate.

## Evidence
- Observed 5 instances of functional pattern preference
- User corrected class-based approach to functional on 2025-01-15
- Similar pattern in 3 different sessions
```

The frontmatter enables programmatic filtering by confidence, domain, and trigger conditions.

Sources: [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:22-43]()

## Command Integration

### Available Commands

| Command | Purpose | System |
|---------|---------|--------|
| `/learn` | Manual pattern extraction mid-session | v1 |
| `/instinct-status` | Show learned instincts with confidence scores | v2 |
| `/instinct-import <file>` | Import instincts from teammate or repo | v2 |
| `/instinct-export` | Export instincts for sharing | v2 |
| `/evolve` | Cluster related instincts into skills/commands/agents | v2 |
| `/skill-create` | Generate skills from git history | Both |

### Command Implementations

```mermaid
