## Phase 1: Observation

### Hook Registration and Invocation

The observation system hooks into Claude Code's tool execution pipeline through `hooks.json` registration:

```json
{
  "PreToolUse": [{
    "matcher": "*",
    "hooks": [{
      "type": "command",
      "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh",
      "async": true,
      "timeout": 10
    }]
  }],
  "PostToolUse": [{
    "matcher": "*",
    "hooks": [{
      "type": "command",
      "command": "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh",
      "async": true,
      "timeout": 10
    }]
  }]
}
```

The hook runs **twice per tool use**: once before execution (PreToolUse) and once after completion (PostToolUse). This dual-phase capture enables tracking of both intent and outcome.

**Sources:** [hooks/hooks.json:56-66](), [hooks/hooks.json:146-156]()

### Observation Capture Process

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant CC as "Claude Code"
    participant Hook as "observe.sh"
    participant Detect as "detect-project.sh"
    participant File as "observations.jsonl"
    participant Observer as "start-observer.sh<br/>(PID from .observer.pid)"
    
    CC->>Hook: stdin JSON<br/>{tool_name, tool_input, cwd}
    Hook->>Hook: Parse stdin (python3)
    Hook->>Detect: Extract cwd, detect project
    Detect-->>Hook: PROJECT_ID, PROJECT_NAME
    Hook->>Hook: Build observation record
    Hook->>File: Append JSONL<br/>(atomic write)
    Hook->>Observer: kill -USR1 $pid<br/>(signal new data)
    Hook-->>CC: exit 0
```

**Observation record structure:**

```jsonl
{"timestamp":"2025-01-22T10:30:00Z","event":"tool_start","tool":"Edit","session":"abc123","input":"...truncated...","project_id":"a1b2c3d4e5f6","project_name":"my-react-app"}
{"timestamp":"2025-01-22T10:30:01Z","event":"tool_complete","tool":"Edit","session":"abc123","output":"...truncated...","project_id":"a1b2c3d4e5f6","project_name":"my-react-app"}
```

**Key implementation details:**

| Aspect | Implementation | Location |
|--------|---------------|----------|
| Input parsing | Python stdin reader, truncates to 5KB | [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:77-122]() |
| Project detection | `detect-project.sh` via `source` | [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:55-60]() |
| Archival | Rotate at 10MB → `observations.archive/` | [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:140-147]() |
| Signaling | `kill -USR1` to observer PID | [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:178-185]() |
| Async execution | `async: true`, `timeout: 10` in hooks.json | [hooks/hooks.json:61-62]() |

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:1-188](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:80-91]()

