## Phase 3: Codification

### Instinct File Structure

Instincts are stored as markdown files with YAML frontmatter in project-scoped or global directories:

```
~/.claude/homunculus/
├── instincts/
│   └── personal/                     # Global instincts
│       ├── always-validate-input.md  # scope: global
│       └── grep-before-edit.md       # scope: global
└── projects/
    └── a1b2c3d4e5f6/                  # Project hash
        └── instincts/
            └── personal/              # Project instincts
                ├── use-react-hooks.md # scope: project
                └── prefer-functional.md # scope: project
```

**Instinct file anatomy:**

```markdown
---
id: prefer-functional-style
trigger: "when writing new functions"
confidence: 0.7
domain: "code-style"
source: "session-observation"
scope: project
project_id: "a1b2c3d4e5f6"
project_name: "my-react-app"
---

# Prefer Functional Style

## Action
Use functional patterns over classes when appropriate.

## Evidence
- Observed 5 instances of functional pattern preference
- User corrected class-based approach to functional on 2025-01-15
```

**Domain taxonomy:**

| Domain | Purpose | Typical Scope |
|--------|---------|---------------|
| `code-style` | Language/framework conventions | project |
| `testing` | Test writing strategies | project or global |
| `git` | Git workflow preferences | global |
| `debugging` | Debugging approaches | project or global |
| `workflow` | Tool usage sequences | global |
| `file-patterns` | File organization | project |
| `security` | Security practices | global |

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:48-79](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/observer.md:68-149]()

