## Phase 5: Usage

### Agent Context Injection

When agents are invoked, they load instincts from both project-scoped and global directories to inform their behavior:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Agent Invocation"
        AgentLoad["Agent loads context"]
        DetectProj["Detect current project"]
        LoadProject["Load project instincts"]
        LoadGlobal["Load global instincts"]
        FilterConf{"confidence ≥ 0.5?"}
        InjectCtx["Inject into system prompt"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Storage"
        ProjInst["projects/{hash}/instincts/personal/"]
        GlobalInst["instincts/personal/"]
        EvolvedSkills["evolved/skills/"]
    end
    
    AgentLoad --> DetectProj
    DetectProj --> LoadProject
    DetectProj --> LoadGlobal
    LoadProject --> ProjInst
    LoadGlobal --> GlobalInst
    LoadGlobal --> EvolvedSkills
    
    ProjInst --> FilterConf
    GlobalInst --> FilterConf
    EvolvedSkills --> FilterConf
    
    FilterConf -->|Yes| InjectCtx
    FilterConf -->|No| AgentLoad
```

**Confidence-based filtering:**

| Confidence Range | Behavior in Agent Context |
|------------------|---------------------------|
| 0.3-0.4 | Suggested only (not enforced) |
| 0.5-0.6 | Applied when trigger matches |
| 0.7-0.8 | Auto-approved for application |
| 0.9+ | Core behavior (always enforced) |

The closed-loop effect: Each session generates observations → instincts → better future sessions.

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:311-330](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:1-9]()

