## Project Scoping Architecture

### Project Detection Priority Cascade

The `detect-project.sh` script implements a 4-level priority cascade:

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start["Project Detection Start"]
    Check1{"CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR<br/>env var set?"}
    Check2{"git remote get-url origin<br/>succeeds?"}
    Check3{"git rev-parse --show-toplevel<br/>succeeds?"}
    Fallback["Global Fallback<br/>(no project context)"]
    
    Hash1["Hash remote URL<br/>→ 12-char project ID"]
    Hash2["Hash repo path<br/>→ 12-char project ID"]
    
    Registry["Update projects.json<br/>{id → name/path/remote}"]
    
    SetVars["Set environment:<br/>PROJECT_ID<br/>PROJECT_NAME<br/>PROJECT_ROOT<br/>PROJECT_DIR"]
    
    Start --> Check1
    Check1 -->|Yes| Hash1
    Check1 -->|No| Check2
    Check2 -->|Yes| Hash1
    Check2 -->|No| Check3
    Check3 -->|Yes| Hash2
    Check3 -->|No| Fallback
    
    Hash1 --> Registry
    Hash2 --> Registry
    Registry --> SetVars
    
    Fallback --> SetVars
```

**Project ID calculation:**

```bash
# Priority 1: Environment variable
PROJECT_ID="${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}"

# Priority 2: Git remote URL (portable across machines)
REMOTE_URL=$(git remote get-url origin 2>/dev/null)
PROJECT_ID=$(echo -n "$REMOTE_URL" | sha256sum | cut -c1-12)

# Priority 3: Git repo path (machine-specific)
REPO_PATH=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null)
PROJECT_ID=$(echo -n "$REPO_PATH" | sha256sum | cut -c1-12)

# Priority 4: Global fallback
PROJECT_ID="global"
```

**Project directory structure:**

```bash
~/.claude/homunculus/projects/{project_id}/
├── observations.jsonl                # Raw observations
├── observations.archive/             # Rotated observations (>10MB)
│   └── processed-20250122-143022-1234.jsonl
├── instincts/
│   ├── personal/                     # Auto-learned
│   └── inherited/                    # Imported
├── evolved/                          # Generated from instincts
│   ├── skills/
│   ├── commands/
│   └── agents/
├── .observer.pid                     # Observer daemon PID
└── observer.log                      # Observer output
```

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:126-135](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:52-60](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/start-observer.sh:22-29]()

