## Observation Archival Strategy

After successful analysis, the observer archives processed observations to prevent re-analysis and manage file size growth.

**Archival Process:**

```mermaid
graph TD
    Analysis["analyze_observations()"]
    ClaudeComplete["Claude analysis complete"]
    ArchiveDir["mkdir -p observations.archive/"]
    Timestamp["date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S"]
    UniqueID["$$ (process ID)"]
    Move["mv observations.jsonl<br/>→ observations.archive/processed-TIMESTAMP-PID.jsonl"]
    NewFile["Next observation creates fresh observations.jsonl"]
    
    Analysis --> ClaudeComplete
    ClaudeComplete --> ArchiveDir
    ArchiveDir --> Timestamp
    Timestamp --> UniqueID
    UniqueID --> Move
    Move --> NewFile
```

**Implementation:**

[skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/start-observer.sh:226-231]():

```bash
if [ -f "$OBSERVATIONS_FILE" ]; then
  archive_dir="${PROJECT_DIR}/observations.archive"
  mkdir -p "$archive_dir"
  mv "$OBSERVATIONS_FILE" "$archive_dir/processed-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)-$$.jsonl" 2>/dev/null || true
fi
```

**Size-Based Pre-Archival:**

The `observe.sh` hook also archives observations proactively when file size exceeds 10MB to prevent performance degradation [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:140-147]():

```bash
if [ -f "$OBSERVATIONS_FILE" ]; then
  file_size_mb=$(du -m "$OBSERVATIONS_FILE" 2>/dev/null | cut -f1)
  if [ "${file_size_mb:-0}" -ge "$MAX_FILE_SIZE_MB" ]; then
    archive_dir="${PROJECT_DIR}/observations.archive"
    mkdir -p "$archive_dir"
    mv "$OBSERVATIONS_FILE" "$archive_dir/observations-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)-$$.jsonl" 2>/dev/null || true
  fi
fi
```

**File Naming Convention:**
- **Pre-analysis archival**: `observations-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-PID.jsonl`
- **Post-analysis archival**: `processed-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-PID.jsonl`
- **PID suffix**: Ensures unique filenames in concurrent scenarios

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/start-observer.sh:226-231](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/hooks/observe.sh:140-147]()

