## Confidence Scoring System

### Initial Confidence Assignment

Confidence is calculated based on observation frequency when an instinct is first created:

| Observations | Confidence | Meaning |
|--------------|-----------|---------|
| 1-2 | 0.3 | Tentative |
| 3-5 | 0.5 | Moderate |
| 6-10 | 0.7 | Strong |
| 11+ | 0.85 | Very strong |

**Diagram: Confidence Evolution Over Time**

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Tentative: 1-2 observations
    Tentative --> Moderate: 3-5 observations
    Moderate --> Strong: 6-10 observations
    Strong --> VeryStrong: 11+ observations
    
    Tentative: 0.3 (tentative)
    Moderate: 0.5 (moderate)
    Strong: 0.7 (strong)
    VeryStrong: 0.85-0.9 (very strong)
    
    Moderate --> Tentative: -0.1 (contradiction)
    Strong --> Moderate: -0.1 (contradiction)
    VeryStrong --> Strong: -0.1 (contradiction)
    
    Tentative --> Moderate: +0.05 (confirmation)
    Moderate --> Strong: +0.05 (confirmation)
    Strong --> VeryStrong: +0.05 (confirmation)
    
    note right of Tentative
        Suggested but not enforced
    end note
    
    note right of Strong
        Auto-approved for application
    end note
```

### Confidence Adjustment Rules

| Event | Adjustment | Reason |
|-------|-----------|--------|
| Confirming observation | +0.05 | Pattern repeated |
| User correction | -0.1 | Pattern contradicted |
| Time decay (per week) | -0.02 | Pattern not observed |
| Similar instinct imported | +0.03 | External validation |

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:310-330](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/observer.md:137-148]()

---

## Scope Decision System

### Scope Types

Instincts have two possible scopes:

1. **Project scope** (`scope: project`): Pattern applies only within the specific project where it was observed
2. **Global scope** (`scope: global`): Universal pattern that applies across all projects

**Diagram: Scope Decision Flowchart**

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["New Pattern Detected"]
    
    Check1{"Is pattern<br/>language/framework-<br/>specific?"}
    Check2{"Is pattern<br/>project file<br/>structure?"}
    Check3{"Is pattern<br/>code style<br/>preference?"}
    Check4{"Is pattern<br/>security or<br/>best practice?"}
    Check5{"Is pattern<br/>tool workflow<br/>preference?"}
    Check6{"Is pattern<br/>git practice?"}
    
    ProjectScope["scope: project<br/>+ project_id<br/>+ project_name"]
    GlobalScope["scope: global<br/>(no project fields)"]
    
    Start --> Check1
    Check1 -->|Yes| ProjectScope
    Check1 -->|No| Check2
    Check2 -->|Yes| ProjectScope
    Check2 -->|No| Check3
    Check3 -->|Yes| ProjectScope
    Check3 -->|No| Check4
    Check4 -->|Yes| GlobalScope
    Check4 -->|No| Check5
    Check5 -->|Yes| GlobalScope
    Check5 -->|No| Check6
    Check6 -->|Yes| GlobalScope
    Check6 -->|No| ProjectScope
    
    ProjectScope -.->|Default<br/>when unsure| ProjectScope
```

### Scope Decision Criteria

| Pattern Type | Scope | Examples |
|-------------|-------|---------|
| Language/framework conventions | **project** | "Use React hooks", "Follow Django REST patterns" |
| File structure preferences | **project** | "Tests in `__tests__`/", "Components in src/components/" |
| Code style | **project** | "Use functional style", "Prefer dataclasses" |
| Error handling strategies | **project** (usually) | "Use Result type for errors" |
| Security practices | **global** | "Validate user input", "Sanitize SQL" |
| General best practices | **global** | "Write tests first", "Always handle errors" |
| Tool workflow preferences | **global** | "Grep before Edit", "Read before Write" |
| Git practices | **global** | "Conventional commits", "Small focused commits" |

**Default rule**: When in doubt, use `scope: project` — it's safer to be project-specific and promote later than to contaminate the global space.

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:274-285](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/observer.md:120-136]()

