## Instinct Lifecycle

**Diagram: Instinct State Machine**

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Observed: Pattern detected (3+ observations)
    
    Observed --> Created: Observer agent creates<br/>instinct file
    Created --> ProjectScoped: scope: project<br/>(default)
    Created --> GlobalScoped: scope: global<br/>(universal pattern)
    
    ProjectScoped --> HighConfidence: Confidence >= 0.8
    HighConfidence --> Promoted: /promote command<br/>(appears in 2+ projects)
    Promoted --> GlobalScoped: Moved to global scope
    
    GlobalScoped --> Evolved: /evolve clusters<br/>related instincts
    ProjectScoped --> Evolved: /evolve clusters<br/>related instincts
    
    Evolved --> Skill: Generated SKILL.md
    Evolved --> Command: Generated command.md
    Evolved --> Agent: Generated agent.md
    
    Skill --> [*]
    Command --> [*]
    Agent --> [*]
    
    note right of ProjectScoped
        personal/ subdirectory
        per-project isolation
    end note
    
    note right of GlobalScoped
        instincts/personal/
        applies everywhere
    end note
    
    note right of Promoted
        Cross-project validation
        Average confidence >= 0.8
    end note
```

### Lifecycle Stages

1. **Observation**: Pattern detected from 3+ tool use observations in [observe.sh:156-175]()
2. **Creation**: Observer agent creates instinct file in [start-observer.sh:168-232]()
3. **Scoping**: Assigned `project` or `global` scope based on pattern type
4. **Refinement**: Confidence adjusts based on confirming/contradicting observations
5. **Promotion**: Project instinct promoted to global when seen in 2+ projects
6. **Evolution**: Clustered with related instincts into skills/commands via `/evolve`

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:80-124](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/observer.md:30-65]()

