## Instinct Promotion Rules

### Auto-Promotion Criteria

An instinct is eligible for promotion from project scope to global scope when:

1. **Cross-project presence**: Same instinct ID exists in **2+ different projects**
2. **High confidence**: Average confidence across all instances **>= 0.8**
3. **Domain compatibility**: Domain is in global-friendly list (`security`, `general-best-practices`, `workflow`, `git`)

### Promotion Commands

```bash
# Auto-detect and promote all qualifying instincts
/promote

# Preview candidates without changes
/promote --dry-run

# Promote specific instinct from current project
/promote prefer-explicit-errors

# Force promotion without confirmation
/promote --force
```

**Diagram: Promotion Process**

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph "Project A"
        InstA["instinct-id.md<br/>confidence: 0.85"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project B"
        InstB["instinct-id.md<br/>confidence: 0.82"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project C"
        InstC["instinct-id.md<br/>confidence: 0.78"]
    end
    
    Check{"Cross-project check"}
    Avg{"Average<br/>confidence<br/>>= 0.8?"}
    Domain{"Global-friendly<br/>domain?"}
    
    subgraph "Global"
        GlobalInst["instincts/personal/<br/>instinct-id.md<br/>scope: global"]
    end
    
    InstA --> Check
    InstB --> Check
    InstC --> Check
    
    Check -->|2+ projects| Avg
    Avg -->|Yes: 0.817| Domain
    Domain -->|Yes| GlobalInst
    Domain -->|No| Rejected["Keep project-scoped"]
    Avg -->|No| Rejected
```

The `/evolve` command also suggests promotion candidates as part of its analysis.

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md:287-308](), [commands/promote.md:26-42](), [skills/continuous-learning-v2/agents/observer.md:150-157]()

