## MCP Server Configuration

MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers are configured in `~/.claude.json`, separate from settings.json.

### MCP Configuration File Structure

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "~/.claude.json"
        Root["Root object"]
        MCPServers["mcpServers: {}"]
        Server1["github: {command, args, env}"]
        Server2["supabase: {command, args, env}"]
        Server3["memory: {command, args, env}"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Per-Server Schema"
        Command["command: 'npx'"]
        Args["args: ['-y', '@modelcontextprotocol/server-github']"]
        Env["env: {GITHUB_TOKEN: 'xxx'}"]
    end
    
    Root --> MCPServers
    MCPServers --> Server1
    MCPServers --> Server2
    MCPServers --> Server3
    
    Server1 --> Command
    Server1 --> Args
    Server1 --> Env
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:313-341](), [README.md:574-588]()

### Example ~/.claude.json

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_TOKEN": "ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxx"
      }
    },
    "supabase": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest", "--project-ref=YOUR_REF"],
      "env": {
        "SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN": "sbp_xxxxxxxxxxxxx"
      }
    },
    "memory": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory"]
    }
  }
}
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:313-341]()

### API Key Replacement

Replace `YOUR_*_HERE` placeholders with actual credentials before use.

**Sources:** [README.md:574-588]()

### Disabling MCPs Per-Project

Use `.claude/settings.json` to disable specific MCPs for a project:

```json
{
  "disabledMcpServers": ["supabase", "railway", "vercel"]
}
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:139-153]()

---

## Context Window Management

MCP servers consume context window space by injecting tool descriptions. Excessive MCPs degrade the effective context window from 200k tokens to ~70k.

### MCP Context Impact Diagram

```mermaid
graph LR
    Base["Base Context: 200k tokens"]
    
    subgraph "MCP Tool Descriptions"
        MCP1["GitHub MCP: ~15k tokens<br/>(20 tools)"]
        MCP2["Supabase MCP: ~12k tokens<br/>(15 tools)"]
        MCP3["Vercel MCP: ~8k tokens<br/>(10 tools)"]
        MCP4["Railway MCP: ~6k tokens<br/>(8 tools)"]
        MCP5["5 more MCPs: ~30k tokens<br/>(40 tools)"]
    end
    
    Base --> Consumed["71k tokens consumed<br/>by tool descriptions"]
    MCP1 --> Consumed
    MCP2 --> Consumed
    MCP3 --> Consumed
    MCP4 --> Consumed
    MCP5 --> Consumed
    
    Consumed --> Effective["Effective Context: ~129k tokens<br/>(200k - 71k)"]
    
    style Effective fill:#fff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:139-153](), [README.md:714-729]()

### MCP Discipline Guidelines

| Metric | Recommendation | Rationale |
|--------|---------------|-----------|
| Total configured | 20-30 | Have options available |
| Total enabled | ≤10 | Keep context window usable |
| Total active tools | ≤80 | Avoid degradation |
| Per-project enabled | 5-7 | Project-specific needs |

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:139-153]()

### Checking Enabled MCPs

```bash
/mcp
```

Or inspect settings:
```bash
cat ~/.claude/settings.json | jq '.disabledMcpServers'
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:148-153]()

### Context Optimization via mgrep

The `mgrep` plugin (by @mixedbread-ai) reduces search token usage by ~50% compared to traditional grep/ripgrep.

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:135-139](), [the-shortform-guide.md:222-229]()

---

## Continuous Learning Configuration

Continuous Learning v2 uses a configuration file at `~/.claude/homunculus/config.json` to control pattern detection and skill generation.

### Continuous Learning File Structure

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "~/.claude/homunculus/"
        Config["config.json<br/>(observer settings)"]
        Observations["observations.jsonl<br/>(captured events)"]
        InstinctsDir["instincts/<br/>(learned patterns)"]
        ProjectsDir["projects/<br/>(project-scoped learning)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "config.json Schema"
        Observer["observer: {}"]
        Enabled["enabled: true/false"]
        Interval["run_interval_minutes: 30"]
        MinObs["min_observations_to_analyze: 20"]
        SkillsPath["learned_skills_path: '~/.claude/skills/learned'"]
    end
    
    Config --> Observer
    Observer --> Enabled
    Observer --> Interval
    Observer --> MinObs
    Observer --> SkillsPath
    
    Config -.controls.-> ObserverAgent["start-observer.sh daemon"]
    ObserverAgent -.reads.-> Observations
    ObserverAgent -.generates.-> InstinctsDir
    InstinctsDir -.evolves into.-> SkillsPath
```

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md](), [the-longform-guide.md:88-103]()

### Example config.json

```json
{
  "observer": {
    "enabled": true,
    "run_interval_minutes": 30,
    "min_observations_to_analyze": 20,
    "learned_skills_path": "~/.claude/skills/learned"
  },
  "min_session_length": 10
}
```

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md]()

### Configuration Parameters

| Parameter | Type | Default | Purpose |
|-----------|------|---------|---------|
| `observer.enabled` | boolean | `true` | Enable/disable observer daemon |
| `observer.run_interval_minutes` | integer | `30` | Analysis interval (minutes) |
| `observer.min_observations_to_analyze` | integer | `20` | Observation threshold for pattern detection |
| `observer.learned_skills_path` | string | `~/.claude/skills/learned` | Output directory for generated skills |
| `min_session_length` | integer | `10` | Minimum user messages before evaluation |

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:480-524]()

### Observation Capture

The `observe.sh` hook (PreToolUse + PostToolUse) appends to `observations.jsonl`:

```jsonl
{"timestamp":"2026-02-01T10:30:00Z","tool":"Edit","file":"src/auth.ts","result":"success"}
{"timestamp":"2026-02-01T10:31:00Z","tool":"Bash","command":"npm test","result":"failed"}
```

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md]()

### Observer Daemon Signals

The observer daemon (`start-observer.sh`) responds to:
- **USR1**: Trigger immediate analysis (sent by PostToolUse hooks)
- **TERM**: Graceful shutdown

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md]()

---

## Project-Specific Configuration

Projects can override user-level settings via `.claude/` directory at the project root.

### Project Configuration Precedence

```mermaid
graph TD
    UserLevel["User-Level Config<br/>~/.claude/"]
    ProjectLevel["Project-Level Config<br/>.claude/"]
    
    UserSettings["~/.claude/settings.json"]
    UserPM["~/.claude/package-manager.json"]
    UserRules["~/.claude/rules/*.md"]
    
    ProjSettings[".claude/settings.json"]
    ProjPM[".claude/package-manager.json"]
    ProjRules[".claude/rules/*.md"]
    
    UserLevel --> UserSettings
    UserLevel --> UserPM
    UserLevel --> UserRules
    
    ProjectLevel --> ProjSettings
    ProjectLevel --> ProjPM
    ProjectLevel --> ProjRules
    
    UserSettings -->|merged with| ProjSettings
    UserPM -->|overridden by| ProjPM
    UserRules -->|augmented by| ProjRules
    
    ProjSettings --> FinalSettings["Effective Settings"]
    ProjPM --> FinalPM["Effective Package Manager"]
    ProjRules --> FinalRules["Combined Rules"]
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:78-127](), [README.md:534-544]()

### Project Package Manager Override

Create `.claude/package-manager.json`:
```json
{
  "packageManager": "bun",
  "setAt": "2026-02-01T14:00:00.000Z"
}
```

This overrides global config when running Claude Code in this project.

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:78-127](), [tests/lib/package-manager.test.js:356-374]()

### Project-Scoped Rules

Add `.claude/rules/` directory with project-specific rules:

```
.claude/rules/
  project-patterns.md    # Project-specific coding patterns
  api-conventions.md     # API design rules for this project
  deployment.md          # Deployment guidelines
```

These **augment** (not replace) user-level rules in `~/.claude/rules/`.

**Sources:** [README.md:534-544]()

### Project-Scoped MCP Disabling

Create `.claude/settings.json`:
```json
{
  "disabledMcpServers": ["github", "supabase", "vercel"]
}
```

Only disables these MCPs when running Claude Code in this project directory.

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:139-153]()

### Project Detection for Continuous Learning

The `detect-project.sh` script generates a project ID hash from the git remote URL:

```bash
# For git remote: https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git
# Project ID: e4c7b9a2 (SHA-256 of URL, truncated to 8 chars)
```

Observations and instincts are stored under `~/.claude/homunculus/projects/{project-id}/`.

**Sources:** [skills/continuous-learning-v2/SKILL.md]()

---

