# Page: Context Window Management

# Context Window Management

<details>
<summary>Relevant source files</summary>

The following files were used as context for generating this wiki page:

- [README.md](README.md)
- [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md](skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md)
- [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md](skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md)
- [the-longform-guide.md](the-longform-guide.md)
- [the-shortform-guide.md](the-shortform-guide.md)

</details>



This document covers strategies for preserving and maximizing Claude's available context window through MCP server management, tool limitation, and lazy loading. The focus is on preventing the 200k → 70k context degradation that occurs when too many tools are enabled simultaneously.

For general settings configuration, see [Settings Configuration](#10.2). For individual MCP server setup and API key management, see [MCP Server Configuration](#10.4). For understanding what MCPs are and their tradeoffs, see [MCPs (Model Context Protocol)](#3.7). For broader optimization strategies including model selection and code architecture, see [Token Optimization Strategies](#12.2).

---

## The Context Window Problem

Claude Code's context window degrades significantly when too many MCP servers and tools are enabled. A session that starts with 200,000 tokens of available context can shrink to 70,000 tokens or less when 15+ MCP servers are active with 100+ tools exposed.

### Context Degradation Pattern

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Baseline Context Window"
        BASE["200k tokens available<br/>No MCPs loaded"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Progressive Degradation"
        FEW["150k-180k tokens<br/>5-8 MCPs enabled<br/>40-60 tools"]
        MODERATE["120k-150k tokens<br/>10-12 MCPs enabled<br/>60-80 tools"]
        MANY["70k-100k tokens<br/>15+ MCPs enabled<br/>80-120 tools"]
    end
    
    BASE -->|"Load MCPs"| FEW
    FEW -->|"Add more MCPs"| MODERATE
    MODERATE -->|"Enable all MCPs"| MANY
    
    MANY -.->|"Compaction triggered earlier<br/>More frequent context loss"| COMPACT["PreCompact Hook fires<br/>Critical state may be lost"]
```

**Sources:** [README.md:510-520](), [the-shortform-guide.md:137-153]()

The degradation is not linear. Each MCP server registers:
- Tool definitions (schema, parameters, descriptions)
- Server metadata and capabilities
- Connection overhead for HTTP-based servers
- Persistent tool availability context

### Measured Impact

| MCPs Enabled | Tools Active | Available Context | Effective Reduction |
|--------------|--------------|-------------------|---------------------|
| 0-3          | 0-20         | 180k-200k         | 0-10%              |
| 5-8          | 40-60        | 150k-180k         | 10-25%             |
| 10-12        | 60-80        | 120k-150k         | 25-40%             |
| 15+          | 80-120       | 70k-100k          | 50-65%             |

**Sources:** [README.md:510-520](), [the-shortform-guide.md:143-146]()

---

## MCP Discipline: The 20-30/5-10 Rule

The critical thresholds for maintaining context window health:

- **20-30 MCPs configured** in `~/.claude.json` (user-level MCP library)
- **5-10 MCPs enabled** per project (via `disabledMcpServers` in project `.claude.json`)
- **<80 tools active** across all enabled servers

This is not a hard limit enforced by Claude Code, but a practical guideline derived from production usage. Exceeding these thresholds leads to:
- Earlier compaction triggers (see [Memory & Context Preservation](#11.3))
- Reduced ability to hold long conversation threads
- More aggressive context pruning
- Decreased effectiveness of session memory

**MCP Discipline: Configuration vs Enablement**

```mermaid
graph TB
    USER_CONFIG["~/.claude.json<br/>mcpServers object<br/>20-30 total MCPs"]
    
    PROJECT_A["Project A<br/>.claude.json<br/>disabledMcpServers: [...]<br/>5-7 enabled"]
    PROJECT_B["Project B<br/>.claude.json<br/>disabledMcpServers: [...]<br/>5-7 enabled"]
    PROJECT_C["Project C<br/>.claude.json<br/>disabledMcpServers: [...]<br/>8-10 enabled"]
    
    CONTEXT_A["Context: 160k-170k tokens<br/>~40-50 tools active"]
    CONTEXT_B["Context: 155k-165k tokens<br/>~35-45 tools active"]
    CONTEXT_C["Context: 140k-155k tokens<br/>~60-70 tools active"]
    
    USER_CONFIG -->|"projects.'.'.disabledMcpServers"| PROJECT_A
    USER_CONFIG -->|"projects.'.'.disabledMcpServers"| PROJECT_B
    USER_CONFIG -->|"projects.'.'.disabledMcpServers"| PROJECT_C
    
    PROJECT_A --> CONTEXT_A
    PROJECT_B --> CONTEXT_B
    PROJECT_C --> CONTEXT_C
```

**Anti-Pattern: All MCPs Enabled**

```mermaid
graph LR
    ALL_ENABLED["~/.claude.json<br/>20+ MCPs<br/>No disabledMcpServers"]
    DEGRADED["Context: 70k-100k tokens<br/>120+ tools active<br/>Early compaction"]
    
    ALL_ENABLED --> DEGRADED
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:145-146](), [README.md:512-518]()

