## Configuration Hierarchy

MCP enablement can be controlled at multiple levels with specific precedence rules:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Configuration Layers"
        USER_CONFIG["~/.claude.json<br/>User-level MCP definitions<br/>All available servers"]
        SETTINGS["~/.claude/settings.json<br/>extraKnownMarketplaces<br/>enabledPlugins"]
        PROJECT_CONFIG["project/.claude.json<br/>Project-level overrides<br/>disabledMcpServers array"]
        ENV["Environment Variables<br/>CLAUDE_DISABLE_MCPS"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Effective Configuration"
        AVAILABLE["Available MCPs<br/>From user config"]
        DISABLED["Disabled List<br/>Project-specific"]
        ACTIVE["Active MCPs<br/>available - disabled"]
    end
    
    USER_CONFIG -->|"Defines all servers"| AVAILABLE
    PROJECT_CONFIG -->|"Selective disabling"| DISABLED
    ENV -->|"Override all"| DISABLED
    
    AVAILABLE --> ACTIVE
    DISABLED --> ACTIVE
```

**Sources:** [README.md:510-520](), [the-shortform-guide.md:152-153]()

### User-Level MCP Configuration

Location: `~/.claude.json`

Defines all MCP servers you have available. This is your "MCP library" - all servers configured here are available for use.

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"],
      "env": {
        "GITHUB_TOKEN": "ghp_xxxxx"
      }
    },
    "supabase": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest"],
      "env": {
        "SUPABASE_URL": "https://xxx.supabase.co",
        "SUPABASE_KEY": "xxx"
      }
    },
    "vercel": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.vercel.com",
      "env": {
        "VERCEL_TOKEN": "xxx"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Sources:** [README.md:313-337](), [the-shortform-guide.md:313-337]()

### Project-Level Disabling

Location: `project/.claude.json` or `project/.claude/config.json`

Each project can selectively disable MCPs that aren't needed for that codebase:

```json
{
  "projects": {
    ".": {
      "disabledMcpServers": [
        "supabase",
        "vercel",
        "railway",
        "cloudflare-docs",
        "clickhouse"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

**Configuration Resolution Flow**

```mermaid
graph TB
    MCP_DEFS["~/.claude.json mcpServers<br/>{github, supabase, vercel, railway, ...}"]
    PROJECT_DISABLED["project/.claude.json<br/>projects.'.'.disabledMcpServers<br/>[supabase, vercel, railway, cloudflare-docs, clickhouse]"]
    EFFECTIVE["Effective MCPs<br/>{github, memory, sequential-thinking}"]
    
    MCP_DEFS -->|"Filter out disabled"| PROJECT_DISABLED
    PROJECT_DISABLED --> EFFECTIVE
```

**Common project-specific patterns:**

| Project Type | Keep Enabled (5-7 MCPs) | Typically Disable |
|--------------|--------------------------|-------------------|
| Frontend-only | github, vercel, memory, filesystem | supabase, railway, clickhouse, cloudflare-workers-bindings |
| Backend API | github, supabase, railway, memory, filesystem | vercel, cloudflare-docs, cloudflare-workers-bindings |
| Documentation | github, memory, sequential-thinking, firecrawl | supabase, vercel, railway, clickhouse, cloudflare-workers-bindings |
| CLI Tool | github, filesystem, memory | supabase, vercel, railway, cloudflare-docs, clickhouse |

**Sources:** [README.md:510-520](), [the-shortform-guide.md:313-337]()

