## mgrep Optimization

`mgrep` (by @mixedbread-ai) is a semantic search tool that reduces token usage by ~50% compared to `grep` or `ripgrep` for codebase navigation. It operates as both a plugin and an MCP server.

### Token Reduction Mechanism

```mermaid
graph TB
    QUERY["Search query:<br/>handleSubmit function"]
    
    GREP_PATH["grep/ripgrep approach"]
    MGREP_PATH["mgrep approach"]
    
    GREP_RESULTS["Returns all matching lines<br/>+ surrounding context<br/>~2k-5k tokens per search"]
    MGREP_RESULTS["Returns semantic matches only<br/>ranked by relevance<br/>~1k-2k tokens per search"]
    
    GREP_CONTEXT["Agent must filter results<br/>Additional reasoning tokens"]
    MGREP_CONTEXT["Pre-filtered by relevance<br/>Immediate actionable results"]
    
    QUERY --> GREP_PATH
    QUERY --> MGREP_PATH
    
    GREP_PATH --> GREP_RESULTS
    MGREP_PATH --> MGREP_RESULTS
    
    GREP_RESULTS --> GREP_CONTEXT
    MGREP_RESULTS --> MGREP_CONTEXT
```

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:135-139](), [the-shortform-guide.md:221-229]()

### Installation and Usage

```bash
# Install via plugin marketplace
/plugin marketplace add https://github.com/mixedbread-ai/mgrep
# Then install from /plugins UI

# Usage in Claude Code
/mgrep "function handleSubmit"  # Local search
/mgrep --web "Next.js 15 app router changes"  # Web search
```

**Impact on Context Window:**

| Search Pattern | grep tokens | mgrep tokens | Reduction |
|----------------|-------------|--------------|-----------|
| Function name in large codebase | 3k-5k | 1k-2k | ~50% |
| API endpoint across services | 4k-7k | 2k-3k | ~50% |
| Configuration pattern | 2k-4k | 1k-2k | ~50% |

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:135-139](), [the-shortform-guide.md:221-229]()

### Integration with MCP Discipline

`mgrep` adds one MCP server (or plugin) but saves more tokens than it consumes through reduced search results:

```mermaid
graph LR
    BASELINE["Baseline: 5 MCPs enabled<br/>160k context available"]
    ADD_MGREP["Add mgrep MCP<br/>155k context available<br/>(-5k overhead)"]
    USAGE["10 searches per session<br/>Save ~30k tokens vs grep"]
    NET["Net gain: +25k tokens<br/>vs grep approach"]
    
    BASELINE --> ADD_MGREP
    ADD_MGREP --> USAGE
    USAGE --> NET
```

**Recommendation:** Include `mgrep` in the 5-10 enabled MCPs for projects with large codebases (>50 files).

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:135-139](), [the-shortform-guide.md:221-229]()

