## MCP Server Management with disabledMcpServers

Projects can selectively disable MCP servers to optimize context window usage. This is critical because having too many MCPs enabled can reduce your context window from 200k tokens to 70k tokens.

### Configuration Pattern

In your project's configuration (either in a project-specific `~/.claude.json` section or via project settings), use `disabledMcpServers`:

```json
{
  "projects": {
    "/path/to/project": {
      "disabledMcpServers": [
        "github",
        "supabase",
        "vercel",
        "railway",
        "clickhouse"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### Context Window Optimization Strategy

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "User-Level MCP Configuration"
        TOTAL["20-30 MCPs Configured<br/>~/.claude.json"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project A: Frontend"
        PROJ_A_ENABLED["Enabled MCPs:<br/>- vercel<br/>- github<br/>- sequential-thinking"]
        PROJ_A_DISABLED["Disabled:<br/>- supabase<br/>- railway<br/>- clickhouse<br/>- etc."]
        PROJ_A_CTX["Context Window:<br/>~180k tokens<br/><10 MCPs<br/><80 tools"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project B: Backend API"
        PROJ_B_ENABLED["Enabled MCPs:<br/>- supabase<br/>- clickhouse<br/>- railway<br/>- github"]
        PROJ_B_DISABLED["Disabled:<br/>- vercel<br/>- sequential-thinking<br/>- etc."]
        PROJ_B_CTX["Context Window:<br/>~180k tokens<br/><10 MCPs<br/><80 tools"]
    end
    
    TOTAL -->|Project-specific filter| PROJ_A_ENABLED
    TOTAL -->|Project-specific filter| PROJ_B_ENABLED
    
    PROJ_A_ENABLED --> PROJ_A_CTX
    PROJ_B_ENABLED --> PROJ_B_CTX
    
    style TOTAL fill:#f9f9f9
    style PROJ_A_CTX fill:#e8f5e8
    style PROJ_B_CTX fill:#e8f5e8
```

**Diagram: Per-Project MCP Enablement Strategy**

### Rule of Thumb

| Metric | Target | Why |
|--------|--------|-----|
| Configured MCPs | 20-30 | Full ecosystem available |
| Enabled MCPs per project | <10 | Maintain context window |
| Active tools | <80 | Prevent context degradation |
| Context window | >150k tokens | Productive sessions |

Sources: [README.md:509-520](), [the-shortform-guide.md:138-154](), [the-longform-guide.md:24-33]()

