## Configuration Precedence Rules

When Claude Code loads configuration, it follows this precedence hierarchy:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Configuration Loading Order"
        BUILTIN["1. Built-in Defaults<br/>(Lowest priority)"]
        USER_GLOBAL["2. User-Level Config<br/>~/.claude/"]
        PROJECT_LOCAL["3. Project-Level Config<br/>.claude/"]
        RUNTIME["4. Runtime Overrides<br/>CLI flags, environment vars<br/>(Highest priority)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Example: Rules Loading"
        USER_RULES["User Rules:<br/>~/.claude/rules/security.md<br/>~/.claude/rules/coding-style.md"]
        PROJ_RULES["Project Rules:<br/>.claude/rules/security.md<br/>.claude/rules/api-format.md"]
        LOADED["Loaded Rules:<br/>security.md (project version)<br/>coding-style.md (user version)<br/>api-format.md (project only)"]
    end
    
    BUILTIN --> USER_GLOBAL
    USER_GLOBAL --> PROJECT_LOCAL
    PROJECT_LOCAL --> RUNTIME
    
    USER_RULES -->|merged with| PROJ_RULES
    PROJ_RULES --> LOADED
    
    style RUNTIME fill:#e8f5e8
    style LOADED fill:#e8f5e8
```

**Diagram: Configuration Precedence and Merging**

### Merging Behavior

| Component Type | Behavior | Example |
|----------------|----------|---------|
| **Rules** | Project overrides user file with same name | `.claude/rules/security.md` overrides `~/.claude/rules/security.md` |
| **Agents** | Project extends user agents | Both user and project agents available |
| **Commands** | Project extends user commands | Both user and project commands available |
| **Skills** | Project extends user skills | Both user and project skills available |
| **MCPs** | Project can disable user MCPs | `disabledMcpServers` filters user config |
| **Package Manager** | Project overrides completely | `.claude/package-manager.json` takes precedence |

Sources: [README.md:353-367](), [the-longform-guide.md:54-62]()

