## System Prompt Injection

Projects can use dynamic system prompt injection to load context conditionally:

### Method 1: CLI Flags

```bash
# Load project-specific context
claude --system-prompt "$(cat .claude/context.md)"

# Create project-specific aliases
alias claude-dev='cd /path/to/project && claude --system-prompt "$(cat .claude/dev.md)"'
alias claude-review='cd /path/to/project && claude --system-prompt "$(cat .claude/review.md)"'
```

### Method 2: Context Directory Pattern

```
.claude/contexts/
  dev.md           # Development mode context
  review.md        # Code review mode context
  deploy.md        # Deployment mode context
  research.md      # Research/exploration mode
```

```bash
# Switch contexts based on task
claude --system-prompt "$(cat .claude/contexts/dev.md)"
```

### Precedence Order

System prompt content has higher authority than user messages, which have higher authority than tool results:

```
System Prompt > User Messages > Tool Results
```

This allows project-specific system prompts to enforce critical project conventions.

Sources: [the-longform-guide.md:54-76](), [README.md:227-231]()

---

## Session Persistence

Projects automatically persist session state in `.claude/sessions/`:

### Session File Pattern

```
.claude/sessions/
  2025-01-15-abc123-session.tmp
  2025-01-15-def456-session.tmp
  2025-01-16-ghi789-session.tmp
```

Each session file contains:
- What approaches worked (with evidence)
- Which approaches were attempted but failed
- What approaches have not been attempted
- Current state and next steps

### Session Management Flow

```mermaid
graph LR
    SESSION_START["SessionStart Hook"]
    ACTIVE["Active Session<br/>Work in progress"]
    SESSION_END["SessionEnd Hook"]
    PERSIST["Persist to<br/>.claude/sessions/<br/>YYYY-MM-DD-ID-session.tmp"]
    NEXT_SESSION["Next Session Start"]
    LOAD["Load previous<br/>session.tmp file"]
    
    SESSION_START --> ACTIVE
    ACTIVE --> SESSION_END
    SESSION_END --> PERSIST
    NEXT_SESSION --> LOAD
    LOAD --> SESSION_START
    
    style PERSIST fill:#e8f5e8
    style LOAD fill:#e8f5e8
```

**Diagram: Session Persistence Lifecycle**

Session files enable context continuity across sessions without manually summarizing progress.

Sources: [the-longform-guide.md:39-50](), [README.md:214]()

