    TDDAgent --> TDDWorkflowSkill
    
    VerifyCmd --> VerificationLoop
    VerifyCmd --> TDDAgent
    
    EvalCmd --> EvalHarness
    
    ReviewerAgent --> SecurityReview
```

Skills act as shared knowledge between commands and agents. Multiple entry points (commands, agents, direct skill invocation) can access the same workflow definition.

Sources: [README.md:288-321](), [commands/]() (directory), [skills/]() (directory), [agents/]() (directory)

### Cross-Skill Dependencies

Some workflows compose multiple skills:

| Primary Skill | Dependent Skills | Workflow |
|---------------|------------------|----------|
| `search-first` | `iterative-retrieval` | Research-First [#10.2](#10.2) |
| `tdd-workflow` | `coding-standards`, `verification-loop` | TDD [#10.3](#10.3) |
| `verification-loop` | `tdd-workflow`, `eval-harness` | Verification [#10.5](#10.5) |
| `continuous-learning-v2` | All skills (learns from usage) | Background learning |
| `eval-harness` | `verification-loop`, `checkpoint` | Eval-Driven [#10.6](#10.6) |

Sources: [skills/]() (directory), [skills/configure-ecc/SKILL.md:226-232]()

