## Context Persistence Across Workflow Phases

### Session Files for Multi-Step Workflows

Workflows that span multiple Claude invocations use session files for context continuity:

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Day 1: Planning + Initial Implementation"
        Start1["Session Start"]
        SessionStartHook1["SessionStart Hook<br/>(scripts/hooks/session-start.js)"]
        LoadPrev1["Load previous session<br/>~/.claude/sessions/"]
        Work1["Workflow Steps:<br/>Plan → Implement"]
        SessionEndHook1["SessionEnd Hook<br/>(scripts/hooks/session-end.js)"]
        Extract1["Extract summary:<br/>- Tasks completed<br/>- Files modified<br/>- Tools used"]
        SessionFile1["2025-01-15-abc123-session.tmp"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Day 2: Continue Implementation + Review"
        Start2["Session Start"]
        SessionStartHook2["SessionStart Hook"]
        LoadPrev2["Load session from Day 1"]
        Work2["Workflow Steps:<br/>Continue impl → Review"]
        SessionEndHook2["SessionEnd Hook"]
        Extract2["Update summary"]
        SessionFile2["2025-01-16-def456-session.tmp"]
    end
    
    Start1 --> SessionStartHook1
    SessionStartHook1 --> LoadPrev1
    LoadPrev1 --> Work1
    Work1 --> SessionEndHook1
    SessionEndHook1 --> Extract1
    Extract1 --> SessionFile1
    
    SessionFile1 -.->|"Loaded by"| SessionStartHook2
    Start2 --> SessionStartHook2
    SessionStartHook2 --> LoadPrev2
    LoadPrev2 --> Work2
    Work2 --> SessionEndHook2
    SessionEndHook2 --> Extract2
    Extract2 --> SessionFile2
```

Session files enable:
- **Cross-session continuity**: Pick up where you left off with full context
- **Autonomous loop context**: `claude -p` invocations can access prior work
- **Multi-day workflows**: Long-running features maintain state across days

Sources: [the-longform-guide.md:36-75](), [scripts/hooks/session-start.js]() (referenced), [scripts/hooks/session-end.js]() (referenced), [README.md:315-317]()

### SHARED_TASK_NOTES.md Pattern

For autonomous workflows (Continuous Claude PR Loop), a dedicated notes file bridges context:

[skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:262-274]() documents this pattern:

```markdown
## Progress
- [x] Added tests for auth module (iteration 1)
- [x] Fixed edge case in token refresh (iteration 2)
- [ ] Still need: rate limiting tests, error boundary tests

## Next Steps
- Focus on rate limiting module next
- The mock setup in tests/helpers.ts can be reused
```

Each `claude -p` iteration reads this file at start and updates it at end.

Sources: [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:262-274](), [the-longform-guide.md:36-86]()

