## Phase 4: Verification with `/verify`

The `/verify` command runs comprehensive checks to ensure deployment readiness.

### Verification Execution Order

The command executes checks in this exact sequence (from [commands/verify.md:7-33]()):

```mermaid
graph TD
    Start["Verification Start"]
    
    Build["1. Build Check"]
    BuildFail["STOP: Report Errors"]
    
    Types["2. Type Check<br/>(tsc --noEmit)"]
    
    Lint["3. Lint Check"]
    
    Tests["4. Test Suite<br/>(Coverage Report)"]
    
    ConsoleLog["5. Console.log Audit<br/>(grep for console.log)"]
    
    GitStatus["6. Git Status<br/>(Uncommitted Changes)"]
    
    Report["Generate Verification Report"]
    
    Start --> Build
    Build -->|FAIL| BuildFail
    Build -->|PASS| Types
    Types --> Lint
    Lint --> Tests
    Tests --> ConsoleLog
    ConsoleLog --> GitStatus
    GitStatus --> Report
```

### Verification Report Format

```
VERIFICATION: [PASS/FAIL]

Build:    [OK/FAIL]
Types:    [OK/X errors]
Lint:     [OK/X issues]
Tests:    [X/Y passed, Z% coverage]
Secrets:  [OK/X found]
Logs:     [OK/X console.logs]

Ready for PR: [YES/NO]
```

### Verification Modes

The `/verify` command accepts mode arguments (from [commands/verify.md:54-60]()):

| Mode | Checks | Use Case |
|------|--------|----------|
| `quick` | Build + Types only | Fast iteration feedback |
| `full` | All checks (default) | Pre-commit verification |
| `pre-commit` | Build + Types + Lint + Tests | Git pre-commit hook |
| `pre-pr` | Full + Security scan | Before creating pull request |

### Integration with Spring Boot Verification Loop

For Spring Boot projects, verification includes additional checks documented in [Spring Boot Development Workflow](#11.4):
- Multi-phase build verification
- JPA entity validation
- 80%+ test coverage enforcement
- Spring Boot-specific linting

**Sources:** [commands/verify.md](), [README.md:186-189](), [the-longform-guide.md:149-172]()

