## Phase 5: Checkpointing with `/checkpoint`

The `/checkpoint` command creates named snapshots of verified states for progress tracking.

### Checkpoint Creation Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant CheckpointCmd as "/checkpoint create"
    participant Verify as "/verify quick"
    participant Git
    participant Log as ".claude/checkpoints.log"
    
    User->>CheckpointCmd: /checkpoint create "feature-auth-complete"
    CheckpointCmd->>Verify: Run quick verification
    Verify-->>CheckpointCmd: PASS/FAIL status
    
    alt Verification PASS
        CheckpointCmd->>Git: git rev-parse --short HEAD
        Git-->>CheckpointCmd: e.g., "a3f2c1b"
        CheckpointCmd->>Log: Append checkpoint entry
        Note over Log: 2025-01-15-14:30 | feature-auth-complete | a3f2c1b
        CheckpointCmd-->>User: Checkpoint created
    else Verification FAIL
        CheckpointCmd-->>User: Cannot checkpoint: verification failed
    end
```

### Checkpoint Log Format

Checkpoints are stored in `.claude/checkpoints.log` (from [commands/checkpoint.md:16-19]()):

```
2025-01-15-10:00 | feature-start | d4e5f6a
2025-01-15-11:30 | tests-passing | g7h8i9j
2025-01-15-14:30 | review-complete | a3f2c1b
```

### Checkpoint Verification

The `/checkpoint verify <name>` command compares current state to a saved checkpoint:

**Comparison Metrics** (from [commands/checkpoint.md:25-42]()):
- Files added/modified since checkpoint
- Test pass rate delta
- Coverage percentage delta
- Build status change

**Example Output:**
```
CHECKPOINT COMPARISON: feature-start
============================
Files changed: 12
Tests: +15 passed / -2 failed
Coverage: +8.5% (now 87%)
Build: PASS
```

### Typical Checkpoint Workflow

From [commands/checkpoint.md:55-66]():

```
[Start] --> /checkpoint create "feature-start"
   |
[Implement] --> /checkpoint create "core-done"
   |
[Test] --> /checkpoint verify "core-done"
   |
[Refactor] --> /checkpoint create "refactor-done"
   |
[PR] --> /checkpoint verify "feature-start"
```

**Sources:** [commands/checkpoint.md](), [the-longform-guide.md:149-172]()

