## Quality Gates via Hooks

Hooks automatically enforce quality standards during the workflow without manual intervention.

### Hook Execution Points

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "PreToolUse Hooks"
        PreBash["Before Bash Tool"]
        PreWrite["Before Write Tool"]
        PreEdit["Before Edit Tool"]
        
        PreBash --> TmuxCheck["Check if tmux running<br/>(suggest for long commands)"]
        PreWrite --> BlockDocs["Block arbitrary .md writes<br/>(allow README, CLAUDE.md)"]
        PreEdit --> GitPushReminder["Remind to review before push"]
    end
    
    subgraph "PostToolUse Hooks"
        PostEdit["After Edit Tool"]
        
        PostEdit --> Prettier["prettier --write<br/>(auto-format)"]
        PostEdit --> TSC["tsc --noEmit<br/>(type check)"]
        PostEdit --> ConsoleLogCheck["grep console.log<br/>(warn if found)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Stop Hooks"
        StopHook["After Claude Response"]
        StopHook --> CheckLogs["Scan modified files<br/>for console.log"]
    end
    
    subgraph "PreCompact Hooks"
        PreCompact["Before Context Compaction"]
        PreCompact --> SaveState["Save critical state<br/>to session file"]
    end
    
    style PreToolUse fill:#fff4e1
    style PostToolUse fill:#e8f5e8
    style StopHooks fill:#ffe1e1
    style PreCompactHooks fill:#f0e1ff
```

### Hook Configuration Location

All hooks are defined in `hooks/hooks.json` (from [README.md:206-209]()):

```json
{
  "PreToolUse": [...],
  "PostToolUse": [...],
  "Stop": [...],
  "PreCompact": [...]
}
```

### Automatic Quality Enforcement

During the TDD phase, when the `tdd-guide` agent uses the Edit tool:

1. **PostToolUse hook fires** (from [the-shortform-guide.md:349-359]()):
   - Runs `prettier --write` on edited files
   - Runs `tsc --noEmit` for type errors
   - Searches for `console.log` statements

2. **Feedback is immediate**:
   ```
   [Hook] Formatted 3 files with prettier
   [Hook] Type check: 2 errors found in src/auth.ts
   [Hook] Warning: console.log found at src/utils.ts:42
   ```

This provides a continuous verification loop during implementation, catching issues before the formal `/verify` phase.

**Sources:** [hooks/hooks.json](), [the-shortform-guide.md:38-72](), [Diagram 7 from architecture]()

