This page documents the Test-Driven Development (TDD) workflow implementation in the Everything Claude Code plugin, including the RED-GREEN-REFACTOR methodology, command orchestration, and coverage enforcement patterns.

**Scope**: This page covers the TDD workflow methodology and tooling. For general feature development workflows, see [Complete Feature Development](#11.1). For language-specific development patterns without TDD focus, see [Go Development Workflow](#11.5) and [Spring Boot Development Workflow](#11.4). For comprehensive verification patterns, see [Eval-Driven Development Workflow](#11.7).

---

## Overview

The plugin enforces TDD through specialized commands (`/tdd`, `/go-test`) that delegate to the `tdd-guide` agent. The workflow mandates writing tests before implementation, verifying 80%+ code coverage, and following language-specific testing patterns.

**Sources**: [README.md:176-179](), [the-shortform-guide.md:13-35]()

---

## TDD Methodology: RED-GREEN-REFACTOR

The core TDD cycle consists of three phases executed iteratively:

```mermaid
graph TB
    RED["RED<br/>Write Failing Test"]
    GREEN["GREEN<br/>Implement Minimal Code"]
    REFACTOR["REFACTOR<br/>Improve Code"]
    VERIFY["Verify Coverage<br/>go test -cover"]
    NEXT["Next Requirement"]
    
    RED -->|"Test fails for<br/>right reason"| GREEN
    GREEN -->|"All tests pass"| REFACTOR
    REFACTOR -->|"Tests still pass"| VERIFY
    VERIFY -->|"Coverage >= 80%"| NEXT
    VERIFY -->|"Coverage < 80%"| RED
    NEXT --> RED
    
    RED -.->|"Tool: go test ./..."| RED
    GREEN -.->|"Tool: Edit"| GREEN
    REFACTOR -.->|"Tool: Edit"| REFACTOR
    VERIFY -.->|"Tool: Bash"| VERIFY
```

**Diagram**: TDD cycle phases and verification checkpoints

**Sources**: [skills/golang-testing/SKILL.md:19-69](), [commands/go-test.md:27-35]()

---

