## Coverage Enforcement

The workflow enforces minimum coverage thresholds based on code type:

| Code Type | Coverage Target | Enforcement |
|-----------|----------------|-------------|
| Critical business logic | 100% | Blocking |
| Public APIs | 90%+ | Warning |
| General code | 80%+ | Standard |
| Generated code | Excluded | N/A |

### Coverage Verification Commands

```bash
# Basic coverage check
go test -cover ./...

# Generate coverage profile
go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...

# View in browser
go tool cover -html=coverage.out

# Coverage by function
go tool cover -func=coverage.out

# With race detection
go test -race -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...
```

**Sources**: [skills/golang-testing/SKILL.md:522-559](), [commands/go-test.md:215-233]()

### Coverage Workflow

```mermaid
graph TB
    RUN_TESTS["go test -coverprofile=coverage.out ./..."]
    PARSE["go tool cover -func=coverage.out"]
    EXTRACT["Extract total coverage %"]
    CHECK_CRITICAL["Check if critical path"]
    CHECK_PUBLIC["Check if public API"]
    CHECK_GENERAL["Check if general code"]
    
    FAIL_100["Fail: Require 100%"]
    FAIL_90["Fail: Require 90%+"]
    FAIL_80["Fail: Require 80%+"]
    PASS["Pass: Coverage sufficient"]
    
    RUN_TESTS --> PARSE
    PARSE --> EXTRACT
    EXTRACT --> CHECK_CRITICAL
    CHECK_CRITICAL -->|"Critical logic"| FAIL_100
    CHECK_CRITICAL -->|"Not critical"| CHECK_PUBLIC
    CHECK_PUBLIC -->|"Public API"| FAIL_90
    CHECK_PUBLIC -->|"Not public"| CHECK_GENERAL
    CHECK_GENERAL -->|"< 80%"| FAIL_80
    CHECK_GENERAL -->|">= 80%"| PASS
```

**Diagram**: Coverage threshold enforcement flow

**Sources**: [skills/golang-testing/SKILL.md:543-559](), [commands/go-test.md:234-242]()

