## TDD Session Example

A typical TDD session follows this pattern:

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant tdd_guide as "tdd-guide agent"
    participant Editor as "Edit Tool"
    participant Shell as "Bash Tool"
    
    User->>tdd_guide: /go-test "implement email validator"
    
    Note over tdd_guide: Step 1: Define interface
    tdd_guide->>Editor: Write validator/email.go with panic("not implemented")
    
    Note over tdd_guide: Step 2: Write tests (RED)
    tdd_guide->>Editor: Write validator/email_test.go with table-driven tests
    
    Note over tdd_guide: Step 3: Verify FAIL
    tdd_guide->>Shell: go test ./validator/...
    Shell-->>tdd_guide: FAIL (panic: not implemented)
    
    Note over tdd_guide: Step 4: Implement (GREEN)
    tdd_guide->>Editor: Replace panic with regex validation
    
    Note over tdd_guide: Step 5: Verify PASS
    tdd_guide->>Shell: go test ./validator/...
    Shell-->>tdd_guide: PASS
    
    Note over tdd_guide: Step 6: Check coverage
    tdd_guide->>Shell: go test -cover ./validator/...
    Shell-->>tdd_guide: coverage: 100.0% of statements
    
    tdd_guide-->>User: TDD Complete! All tests pass, 100% coverage.
```

**Diagram**: Sequence of operations in a TDD session

