## Common Workflows

### Workflow 1: Feature → Review → Fix → Ship

```bash
# Implement with TDD
/tdd "Add OAuth2 login"

# Review
/code-review

# Address critical issues
claude -p "Fix the 3 critical security issues from review-comments.md"

# Re-review
/code-review

# Security audit
/security-scan

# Ship
git commit -m "feat: add OAuth2 login"
git push
```

### Workflow 2: Autonomous Loop with Review

```bash
#!/bin/bash
for feature in "${features[@]}"; do
  # Implement
  claude -p "Implement $feature with TDD" --model sonnet
  
  # Review (separate context, higher model)
  claude -p "Review changes for $feature. Report critical issues only." --model opus
  
  # Auto-fix if critical issues found
  if [ -f review-comments.md ] && grep -q "Critical" review-comments.md; then
    claude -p "Fix critical issues in review-comments.md" --model sonnet
  fi
  
  # Verify
  claude -p "Run test suite" --model haiku
  
  # Commit
  git commit -m "feat: $feature"
done
```

### Workflow 3: Pre-PR Review Checklist

```bash
# 1. Run all quality checks
/verify

# 2. Run code review
/code-review

# 3. Run security scan
/security-scan

# 4. Check review outputs
cat review-comments.md  # Manual review
cat security-report.json | jq '.grade'  # Should be A, B, or C

# 5. Fix any critical issues
# ... (address findings) ...

# 6. Create PR
gh pr create --title "feat: add authentication" --body "$(cat review-comments.md)"
```

