## Plankton Code Quality System

Plankton (credit: @alxfazio) is a write-time code quality enforcement system that runs formatters and linters via PostToolUse hooks, then spawns Claude subprocesses to fix violations.

### Three-Phase Architecture

**Phase 1: Auto-Format (Silent)**

Runs formatters on every file edit:
- Python: `ruff format`
- TypeScript/JS: `biome format`
- Shell: `shfmt`
- TOML: `taplo`
- Markdown: `markdownlint`

Fixes 40-50% of issues silently. No output to main agent.

**Phase 2: Collect Violations (JSON)**

Runs linters and collects unfixable violations as structured JSON:

```json
{
  "file": "src/auth.ts",
  "violations": [
    {
      "line": 42,
      "column": 10,
      "code": "E501",
      "message": "Line too long (120 > 100 characters)",
      "linter": "ruff"
    }
  ]
}
```

**Phase 3: Delegate + Verify**

Spawns `claude -p` subprocess with violations JSON. Routes to model tier based on complexity:

| Violation Type | Model | Timeout | Examples |
|----------------|-------|---------|----------|
| Simple style/formatting | Haiku | 120s | E/W/F codes, import ordering |
| Complexity/refactoring | Sonnet | 300s | C901 (too complex), PLR codes |
| Type system/deep reasoning | Opus | 600s | unresolved-attribute, type mismatches |

After subprocess completes, re-runs Phase 1+2 to verify. Exit 0 if clean, Exit 2 if violations remain.

Sources: [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md:18-55]()

### Config Protection

LLMs will modify linter configs to disable rules rather than fix code. Plankton blocks this:

**PreToolUse Hook**: `protect_linter_configs.sh`

Blocks edits to `.ruff.toml`, `biome.json`, `.shellcheckrc`, `.yamllint`, `.hadolint.yaml` before they happen.

**Stop Hook**: `stop_config_guardian.sh`

Detects config changes via `git diff` at session end. Fails the session if configs were modified.

Sources: [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md:57-63]()

### Model Routing Logic

```mermaid
graph TB
    Violations["Violations Collected"] --> Count{"Count > 5?"}
    
    Count -->|"Yes"| Escalate["Auto-escalate<br/>to higher tier"]
    Count -->|"No"| CheckType{"Violation Type?"}
    
    CheckType -->|"E/W/F codes"| Haiku["Haiku<br/>120s timeout<br/>10 max turns"]
    CheckType -->|"C901, PLR codes"| Sonnet["Sonnet<br/>300s timeout<br/>10 max turns"]
    CheckType -->|"Type errors"| Opus["Opus<br/>600s timeout<br/>15 max turns"]
    
    Escalate --> Sonnet
    
    Haiku --> Subprocess["claude -p subprocess"]
    Sonnet --> Subprocess
    Opus --> Subprocess
    
    Subprocess --> Reverify["Re-run Phase 1+2"]
    
    Reverify --> Clean{"Violations<br/>remain?"}
    
    Clean -->|"No"| Exit0["Exit 0<br/>(silent success)"]
    Clean -->|"Yes"| Exit2["Exit 2<br/>(report to main agent)"]
```

