**Multi-Agent Orchestration Commands**

The system provides orchestration commands for coordinating multiple agents:

| Command | Purpose | Pattern |
|---------|---------|---------|
| `/multi-plan` | Task decomposition | Break features into parallel work units |
| `/multi-execute` | Orchestrated workflows | Sequential or parallel agent execution |
| `/multi-backend` | Backend services | API + DB + cache in parallel |
| `/multi-frontend` | Frontend components | UI + state + tests in parallel |
| `/multi-workflow` | General coordination | Custom multi-service patterns |

**Chief-of-Staff PostToolUse Enforcement**

The `chief-of-staff` agent runs after every tool execution via PostToolUse hooks to enforce quality standards. This pattern ensures that even when the main agent misses something, the chief-of-staff catches it.

Sources: [README.md:308-315](), [the-shortform-guide.md:76-96]()

