## Package Manager System

Cross-platform package manager detection and command generation. Supports npm, pnpm, yarn, and bun with a 6-level priority cascade.

### Detection Priority Cascade

```mermaid
graph TB
    Start["getPackageManager()"] --> Check1{"CLAUDE_PACKAGE_MANAGER<br/>env var?"}
    
    Check1 -->|"Yes"| Env["1. Environment Variable<br/>Highest priority"]
    Check1 -->|"No"| Check2{".claude/package-manager.json<br/>exists?"}
    
    Check2 -->|"Yes"| Project["2. Project Config<br/>2nd priority"]
    Check2 -->|"No"| Check3{"package.json<br/>packageManager field?"}
    
    Check3 -->|"Yes"| PkgJson["3. package.json<br/>3rd priority"]
    Check3 -->|"No"| Check4{"Lock files<br/>present?"}
    
    Check4 -->|"Yes"| Detect["detectFromLockFile()<br/>Priority: pnpm > bun > yarn > npm"]
    Detect --> Lock["4. Lock File Detection<br/>4th priority"]
    
    Check4 -->|"No"| Check5{"~/.claude/package-manager.json<br/>exists?"}
    
    Check5 -->|"Yes"| Global["5. Global Config<br/>5th priority"]
    Check5 -->|"No"| Fallback["6. npm Fallback<br/>6th priority<br/>(no spawns)"]
    
    Env --> Result["Return: {name, config, source}"]
    Project --> Result
    PkgJson --> Result
    Lock --> Result
    Global --> Result
    Fallback --> Result
```

**Why No Spawn in Fallback**

The fallback to npm does NOT check command availability via `which`/`where` (which spawns child processes). This prevents Bun spawn limit issues on Windows during SessionStart hooks. Steps 1-5 already cover all config-based detection methods.

Sources: [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:163-236]()

### Lock File Detection

`detectFromLockFile(projectDir)` scans for lock files in priority order:

```javascript
// scripts/lib/package-manager.js:92-102
function detectFromLockFile(projectDir = process.cwd()) {
  for (const pmName of DETECTION_PRIORITY) {
    const pm = PACKAGE_MANAGERS[pmName];
    const lockFilePath = path.join(projectDir, pm.lockFile);
    
    if (fs.existsSync(lockFilePath)) {
      return pmName;
    }
  }
  return null;
}
```

**DETECTION_PRIORITY**: `['pnpm', 'bun', 'yarn', 'npm']`

Sources: [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:92-102](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:56-57]()

### Command Generation

Package manager configuration includes all standard commands:

```javascript
// scripts/lib/package-manager.js:13-54
const PACKAGE_MANAGERS = {
  npm: {
    name: 'npm',
    lockFile: 'package-lock.json',
    installCmd: 'npm install',
    runCmd: 'npm run',
    execCmd: 'npx',
    testCmd: 'npm test',
    buildCmd: 'npm run build',
    devCmd: 'npm run dev'
  },
  pnpm: {
    name: 'pnpm',
    lockFile: 'pnpm-lock.yaml',
    installCmd: 'pnpm install',
    runCmd: 'pnpm',
    execCmd: 'pnpm dlx',
    testCmd: 'pnpm test',
    buildCmd: 'pnpm build',
    devCmd: 'pnpm dev'
  },
  // ... yarn, bun
};
```

**Safe Command Construction**

```javascript
// scripts/lib/package-manager.js:288-315
function getRunCommand(script, options = {}) {
  if (!SAFE_NAME_REGEX.test(script)) {
    throw new Error(`Script name contains unsafe characters: ${script}`);
  }
  const pm = getPackageManager(options);
  
  switch (script) {
    case 'install': return pm.config.installCmd;
    case 'test': return pm.config.testCmd;
    case 'build': return pm.config.buildCmd;
    case 'dev': return pm.config.devCmd;
    default: return `${pm.config.runCmd} ${script}`;
  }
}
```

Binary names and script names are validated against `SAFE_NAME_REGEX` (`/^[@a-zA-Z0-9_./-]+$/`) to prevent command injection.

Sources: [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:13-54](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:288-315]()

### Pattern Matching

`getCommandPattern(action)` generates regex patterns matching all package managers:

```javascript
// Example: pattern for "dev" command
getCommandPattern('dev')
// Returns: "(npm run dev|pnpm( run)? dev|yarn dev|bun run dev)"
```

Used in hook matchers to detect dev server commands regardless of package manager.

Sources: [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:362-416]()

