## Hook-Based Memory Preservation

Four hooks manage memory across the session lifecycle: `session-start.js`, `pre-compact.js`, `session-end.js`, and `evaluate-session.js`.

### SessionStart Hook: Context Loading

**Hook Registration:**

```json
{
  "SessionStart": [{
    "matcher": "*",
    "hooks": [{
      "type": "command",
      "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/session-start.js\""
    }]
  }]
}
```

**session-start.js Execution Flow:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    HOOK["session-start.js fires"]
    SESSIONS["getSessionsDir()"]
    FIND["findFiles('*-session.tmp',<br/>{maxAge: 7})"]
    SORT["Sort by mtime desc"]
    LATEST["latest = sessions[0]"]
    READ["getSessionContent(latest)"]
    CHECK{"isTemplateSession()?"}
    INJECT["Output to stdout:<br/>'Previous session summary:...'"]
    SKILLS["getLearnedSkillsDir()"]
    COUNT["Count .md files"]
    LOGSKILLS["Log to stderr:<br/>'N learned skill(s)'"]
    ALIASES["loadAliases()"]
    LOGALIASES["Log first 5 aliases"]
    PM["getPackageManager()"]
    LOGPM["Log to stderr:<br/>'Package manager: X'"]
    
    HOOK --> SESSIONS
    SESSIONS --> FIND
    FIND --> SORT
    SORT --> LATEST
    LATEST --> READ
    READ --> CHECK
    CHECK -->|"No"| INJECT
    CHECK -->|"Yes"| SKILLS
    INJECT --> SKILLS
    SKILLS --> COUNT
    COUNT --> LOGSKILLS
    LOGSKILLS --> ALIASES
    ALIASES --> LOGALIASES
    LOGALIASES --> PM
    PM --> LOGPM
```

**Template Session Detection:**

A session is considered a template if its content includes `[Session context goes here]` placeholder text. These are skipped to avoid injecting empty context.

**Package Manager Detection:**

The hook calls `getPackageManager()` which follows a 6-level priority cascade:
1. `CLAUDE_PACKAGE_MANAGER` environment variable
2. `.claude/package-manager.json` (project config)
3. `package.json` `packageManager` field
4. Lock file detection (`pnpm-lock.yaml` > `bun.lockb` > `yarn.lock` > `package-lock.json`)
5. `~/.claude/package-manager.json` (global config)
6. Fallback to first available manager

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:1-72](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:1-150](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:88-204]()

