## Hook-Based Memory Preservation

Three critical hooks manage memory across the session lifecycle: `SessionStart`, `PreCompact`, and `SessionEnd`.

### SessionStart Hook

Executes when a new Claude session initializes. Loads previous context and detects package manager configuration.

**Hook Configuration:**

```json
{
  "SessionStart": [{
    "matcher": "*",
    "hooks": [{
      "type": "command",
      "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/session-start.js\""
    }]
  }]
}
```

**Execution Flow:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    HOOK["SessionStart Hook Fires"]
    SESSIONS["Find recent .tmp files<br/>in ~/.claude/sessions/"]
    SKILLS["Find learned skills<br/>in ~/.claude/skills/learned/"]
    ALIASES["List session aliases<br/>from session-aliases.json"]
    PM["Detect package manager"]
    LOG["Log available context"]
    
    HOOK --> SESSIONS
    HOOK --> SKILLS
    HOOK --> ALIASES
    HOOK --> PM
    SESSIONS --> LOG
    SKILLS --> LOG
    ALIASES --> LOG
    PM --> LOG
```

**Sources:** [hooks/hooks.json:68-78](), [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:21-66]()

### SessionEnd Hook: State Persistence

Fires when a Claude Code session terminates. Extracts summary from `transcript.jsonl` and persists to session file.

**Hook Registration:**

```json
{
  "SessionEnd": [
    {
      "matcher": "*",
      "hooks": [{
        "type": "command",
        "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/session-end.js\""
      }]
    },
    {
      "matcher": "*",
      "hooks": [{
        "type": "command",
        "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/evaluate-session.js\""
      }]
    }
  ]
}
```

**session-end.js Transcript Extraction:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    HOOK["session-end.js fires"]
    STDIN["Read stdin JSON:<br/>{transcript_path}"]
    READ["Read transcript.jsonl"]
    PARSE["Parse JSONL lines"]
    USER["Filter type==='user'"]
    TOOL["Filter type==='tool_use'"]
    EXTRACT["Extract:<br/>- User messages<br/>- Tool calls<br/>- File paths"]
    SHORTID["getSessionIdShort()"]
    DATE["getDateString()"]
    PATH["getSessionsDir()/<br/>YYYY-MM-DD-shortId-session.tmp"]
    EXISTS{"File exists?"}
    APPEND["appendSessionContent()"]
    WRITE["writeSessionContent()"]
    
    HOOK --> STDIN
    STDIN --> READ
    READ --> PARSE
    PARSE --> USER
    PARSE --> TOOL
    USER --> EXTRACT
    TOOL --> EXTRACT
    EXTRACT --> SHORTID
    SHORTID --> DATE
    DATE --> PATH
    PATH --> EXISTS
    EXISTS -->|"Yes"| APPEND
    EXISTS -->|"No"| WRITE
```

**Content Array Handling:**

User messages with `content` as an array are processed recursively:

```javascript
// Handles: {"content": [null, {"text": "hello"}, null, {"text": "world"}]}
// Extracts: "hello world"
```

Null elements are filtered out before extracting text.

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/session-end.js:1-80](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:229-272](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:550-568]()

### Stop Hook: Pattern Evaluation

The `evaluate-session.js` hook runs on the `Stop` event (once per session, not per message) to evaluate if the session is significant enough for pattern learning.

**evaluate-session.js Threshold Logic:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    HOOK["evaluate-session.js fires"]
    STDIN["Read stdin JSON:<br/>{transcript_path}"]
    READ["Read transcript.jsonl"]
    COUNT["Count lines with<br/>type === 'user'"]
    THRESH{"Count >=<br/>min_session_length?"}
    SKIP["Log: 'Session too short'<br/>Exit 0"]
    PROCESS["Log: 'Processing N messages'"]
    LEARN["Trigger continuous learning<br/>(future implementation)"]
    
    HOOK --> STDIN
    STDIN --> READ
    READ --> COUNT
    COUNT --> THRESH
    THRESH -->|"No"| SKIP
    THRESH -->|"Yes"| PROCESS
    PROCESS --> LEARN
```

**Default Threshold:** `min_session_length: 10` (configurable via `config.json`)

**Whitespace Tolerance:** The hook correctly parses JSONL with extra whitespace (pretty-printed style):

```json
{ "type" : "user", "content": "..." }
```

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/evaluate-session.js:1-60](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:481-547]()

## Strategic Compaction Management

The `suggest-compact.js` hook tracks tool usage and recommends manual compaction at thresholds to avoid excessive context accumulation.

### Counter-Based Suggestion System

**Hook Registration:**

```json
{
  "PreToolUse": [{
    "matcher": "tool == \"Edit\" || tool == \"Write\"",
    "hooks": [{
      "type": "command",
      "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js\""
    }]
  }]
}
```

**suggest-compact.js Counter Logic:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    HOOK["suggest-compact.js fires"]
    ENV["CLAUDE_SESSION_ID ||<br/>COMPACT_THRESHOLD"]
    COUNTER["Read counter from:<br/>/tmp/claude-tool-count-{sessionId}"]
    CORRUPT{"Counter file<br/>valid?"}
    RESET["Reset to 0"]
    INCREMENT["counter++"]
    WRITE["Write counter back"]
    FIRST{"counter ==<br/>threshold?"}
    INTERVAL{"counter > threshold<br/>&& counter % 25 === 0?"}
    SUGGEST["Log to stderr:<br/>'N tool calls reached'"]
    SILENT["Exit 0 silently"]
    
    HOOK --> ENV
    ENV --> COUNTER
    COUNTER --> CORRUPT
    CORRUPT -->|"No (NaN)"| RESET
    CORRUPT -->|"Yes"| INCREMENT
    RESET --> INCREMENT
    INCREMENT --> WRITE
    WRITE --> FIRST
    FIRST -->|"Yes"| SUGGEST
    FIRST -->|"No"| INTERVAL
    INTERVAL -->|"Yes"| SUGGEST
    INTERVAL -->|"No"| SILENT
```

**Threshold Configuration:**

| Environment Variable | Default | Valid Range | Purpose |
|---------------------|---------|-------------|---------|
| `COMPACT_THRESHOLD` | `50` | `10-500` | Initial suggestion point |

**Suggestion Intervals:**

- At threshold: Suggest at exactly N tool calls (e.g., 50)
- Post-threshold: Suggest every 25 calls (e.g., 75, 100, 125, ...)

**Counter Persistence:**

Counter files are stored per-session in `/tmp/` to survive shell restarts but reset on system reboot. Format:

```
42
```

**Corrupted Counter Handling:**

If the counter file contains non-numeric data (e.g., `not-a-number`), the hook resets it to `1` and continues without error.

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js:1-70](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:342-478]()

