## Session Aliases System

The `session-aliases.js` module provides a named lookup system for session files, enabling human-readable references to long session IDs.

### Aliases File Structure

**File Location:** `~/.claude/session-aliases.json`

**Schema:**

```json
{
  "version": "1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "lastUpdated": "2026-02-11T14:30:00.000Z"
  },
  "aliases": {
    "feature-auth": {
      "sessionPath": "/Users/name/.claude/sessions/2026-02-01-a1b2c3d4-session.tmp",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-01T10:30:00.000Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-02-01T14:22:00.000Z",
      "title": "User authentication implementation"
    },
    "refactor-api": {
      "sessionPath": "/Users/name/.claude/sessions/2026-02-10-e5f6g7h8-session.tmp",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-10T09:00:00.000Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-02-10T15:10:00.000Z",
      "title": "API endpoint refactoring"
    }
  }
}
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js:1-50](), [tests/lib/session-aliases.test.js:17-24]()

### Alias Management API

**setAlias(alias, sessionPath, title)**

Creates or updates an alias. Returns `{success, isNew, alias}`.

**Validation Rules:**
- Alias must be 1-128 characters
- Lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens, underscores only
- Reserved names blocked: `list`, `help`, `remove`, `delete`, `create`, `set`

```mermaid
graph TB
    INPUT["setAlias('my-session',<br/>'/path/to/session.tmp',<br/>'Title')"]
    VALIDATE["Validation:<br/>- Length 1-128<br/>- Pattern /^[a-z0-9_-]+$/<br/>- Not reserved"]
    EXISTS{"Alias exists?"}
    UPDATE["Update:<br/>- sessionPath<br/>- updatedAt<br/>- title"]
    CREATE["Create:<br/>- createdAt = now<br/>- updatedAt = now"]
    SAVE["saveAliases(data)"]
    RETURN["Return {success: true,<br/>isNew: bool}"]
    ERROR["Return {success: false,<br/>error: string}"]
    
    INPUT --> VALIDATE
    VALIDATE -->|"Invalid"| ERROR
    VALIDATE -->|"Valid"| EXISTS
    EXISTS -->|"Yes"| UPDATE
    EXISTS -->|"No"| CREATE
    UPDATE --> SAVE
    CREATE --> SAVE
    SAVE --> RETURN
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js:100-180](), [tests/lib/session-aliases.test.js:87-134]()

**resolveAlias(alias)**

Looks up an alias and returns the entry. Returns `null` if not found.

```javascript
const entry = resolveAlias('feature-auth');
// Returns: {alias, sessionPath, createdAt, updatedAt, title}
```

**listAliases({search, limit})**

Returns aliases sorted by most recently updated. Supports substring search on alias name or title.

```javascript
listAliases({ search: 'auth', limit: 10 })
// Returns array sorted by updatedAt descending
```

**deleteAlias(alias)**

Removes an alias. Returns `{success, alias}` or `{success: false, error}`.

**renameAlias(oldAlias, newAlias)**

Renames an alias while preserving all metadata. Returns `{success, oldAlias, newAlias}` or error.

**cleanupAliases(sessionExistsFn)**

Removes aliases pointing to non-existent session files. Requires a callback function `(sessionPath) => boolean`.

```javascript
cleanupAliases((path) => fs.existsSync(path))
// Returns: {totalChecked, removed, removedAliases, totalRemaining}
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/session-aliases.js:200-400](), [tests/lib/session-aliases.test.js:1-500]()

### SessionStart Hook Integration

The `session-start.js` hook lists the first 5 aliases on startup:

```javascript
const aliasList = listAliases({ limit: 5 });
if (aliasList.length > 0) {
  log('[SessionStart] Available aliases:');
  aliasList.forEach(a => log(`  - ${a.name}`));
}
```

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:47-53]()

