## Memory Persistence Architecture

### Complete Session Lifecycle

**Session Memory Flow:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    START["Claude Code invocation"]
    SESSIONSTART["session-start.js:<br/>- findFiles(*-session.tmp, maxAge=7)<br/>- getSessionContent(latest)<br/>- Skip if isTemplateSession()<br/>- Inject to stdout"]
    WORK["User interaction"]
    EDITWRITE["Edit/Write tool used"]
    SUGGESTCOMPACT["suggest-compact.js:<br/>- Increment counter<br/>- Log if threshold reached"]
    USERCOMPACT{"User runs<br/>/compact?"}
    PRECOMPACT["pre-compact.js:<br/>- Append to compaction-log.txt<br/>- Annotate recent .tmp files"]
    CLAUDECOMPACT["Claude Code compacts context"]
    SESSIONEND["Session ends"]
    SAVESTATE["session-end.js:<br/>- Read transcript.jsonl<br/>- Extract summary<br/>- Write/append to .tmp"]
    EVALUATE["evaluate-session.js:<br/>- Count user messages<br/>- Skip if < min_session_length"]
    
    START --> SESSIONSTART
    SESSIONSTART --> WORK
    WORK --> EDITWRITE
    EDITWRITE --> SUGGESTCOMPACT
    SUGGESTCOMPACT --> USERCOMPACT
    USERCOMPACT -->|"Yes"| PRECOMPACT
    USERCOMPACT -->|"No"| WORK
    PRECOMPACT --> CLAUDECOMPACT
    CLAUDECOMPACT --> WORK
    WORK --> SESSIONEND
    SESSIONEND --> SAVESTATE
    SAVESTATE --> EVALUATE
```

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:1-72](), [scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js:1-70](), [scripts/hooks/pre-compact.js:1-50](), [scripts/hooks/session-end.js:1-80](), [scripts/hooks/evaluate-session.js:1-60]()

### Cross-Session Memory Bridge

Each Claude Code invocation is independent (no shared memory), but session files create continuity:

**Memory Bridge Pattern:**

```mermaid
graph LR
    INVOCATION1["claude -p 'implement auth'"]
    END1["session-end.js writes:<br/>2026-02-11-abc123-session.tmp"]
    INVOCATION2["claude -p 'write tests'<br/>(next day)"]
    START2["session-start.js reads:<br/>2026-02-11-abc123-session.tmp"]
    INJECT["Injects to stdout:<br/>'Previous session summary...'"]
    CONTEXT["Claude has full<br/>context of previous work"]
    
    INVOCATION1 --> END1
    END1 -.file persists.-> START2
    INVOCATION2 --> START2
    START2 --> INJECT
    INJECT --> CONTEXT
```

**File Retention:**

Session files persist indefinitely in `~/.claude/sessions/`. The `session-start.js` hook searches only the last 7 days (`maxAge: 7`) for performance, but older files remain accessible via `getSessionById()` or manual path references.

**Sources:** [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:29-37](), [scripts/lib/session-manager.js:350-450]()

### SHARED_TASK_NOTES.md Pattern

For autonomous loops (e.g., Continuous Claude), a `SHARED_TASK_NOTES.md` file provides cross-iteration context:

**Pattern:**

```markdown
## Progress
- [x] Added tests for auth module (iteration 1)
- [x] Fixed edge case in token refresh (iteration 2)
- [ ] Still need: rate limiting tests, error boundary tests

## Next Steps
- Focus on rate limiting module next
- The mock setup in tests/helpers.ts can be reused

## Blockers
- None currently
```

Each `claude -p` invocation reads this file at start and updates it at end, bridging context across independent CLI calls.

**Sources:** [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md:261-275](), [the-longform-guide.md:38-49]()

