## System Operations

System operation functions provide safe, cross-platform command execution and git integration.

### Command Execution

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Command Execution Flow"
        CE["commandExists(cmd)"]
        RC["runCommand(cmd, options)"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Platform Detection"
        Windows["Windows:<br/>spawnSync('where', [cmd])"]
        Unix["Unix:<br/>spawnSync('which', [cmd])"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Security"
        Validate["Input Validation:<br/>/^[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+$/"]
        SpawnSync["Use spawnSync<br/>Prevents shell injection"]
    end
    
    CE --> Validate
    Validate --> Windows
    Validate --> Unix
    
    RC --> SpawnSync
```

### Function Reference

| Function | Returns | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `commandExists(cmd)` | `boolean` | Checks if command exists in PATH; validates command name to prevent injection |
| `runCommand(cmd, options)` | `{success: boolean, output: string}` | Executes command and returns result; **use only with trusted input** |

### Security Note

`runCommand()` uses `execSync` which executes shell commands. **Only use with hardcoded, trusted commands.** For user input, use `spawnSync` with argument arrays instead.

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/utils.js:237-282]()

### Git Integration

| Function | Returns | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `isGitRepo()` | `boolean` | Checks if current directory is a git repository |
| `getGitModifiedFiles(patterns)` | `string[]` | Returns modified files matching patterns (uses `git diff --name-only HEAD`) |

**Usage example:**
```javascript
if (isGitRepo()) {
  const modifiedJS = getGitModifiedFiles(['.*\\.js$']);
  log(`Modified JS files: ${modifiedJS.length}`);
}
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/utils.js:284-312]()

