## Security Model

### Command Injection Prevention

The system validates all user-provided script names and arguments to prevent shell injection:

```javascript
// Script names: alphanumeric, dash, underscore, dot, slash, @
// Allows scoped packages (@scope/pkg) but rejects shell metacharacters
const SAFE_NAME_REGEX = /^[@a-zA-Z0-9_./-]+$/;

// Arguments: more permissive but blocks dangerous metacharacters
// Allows: alphanumeric, whitespace, common punctuation
// Rejects: ; | & ` $ ( ) { } < > ! (shell metacharacters)
const SAFE_ARGS_REGEX = /^[@a-zA-Z0-9\s_./:=,'"*+-]+$/;
```

**Validation Logic:**

```javascript
// getRunCommand validation
if (!script || typeof script !== 'string') {
  throw new Error('Script name must be a non-empty string');
}
if (!SAFE_NAME_REGEX.test(script)) {
  throw new Error(`Script name contains unsafe characters: ${script}`);
}

// getExecCommand validation
if (!binary || typeof binary !== 'string') {
  throw new Error('Binary name must be a non-empty string');
}
if (!SAFE_NAME_REGEX.test(binary)) {
  throw new Error(`Binary name contains unsafe characters: ${binary}`);
}
if (args && typeof args === 'string' && !SAFE_ARGS_REGEX.test(args)) {
  throw new Error(`Arguments contain unsafe characters: ${args}`);
}
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:285-286](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:319-320](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:288-300](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:327-337]()

### Security Rationale

The validation prevents attacks like:

```javascript
// REJECTED: Shell metacharacters
getRunCommand('dev; rm -rf /')  // Throws: unsafe characters

// REJECTED: Command substitution
getExecCommand('prettier', '--check $(whoami)')  // Throws: unsafe characters

// ALLOWED: Scoped packages
getExecCommand('@biomejs/biome', 'check')  // ✓ Valid

// ALLOWED: File paths with slashes
getRunCommand('scripts/build-prod')  // ✓ Valid
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:285-286](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:319-320]()

