## Integration Points

### Session Manager Integration

The session manager uses package manager detection during session initialization:

```javascript
// In session-start.js hook
const { getPackageManager } = require('./lib/package-manager');

const pm = getPackageManager();
log(`[Session] Using package manager: ${pm.name} (${pm.source})`);

// Commands available to session context
const installCmd = pm.config.installCmd;
const devCmd = pm.config.devCmd;
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:163-236]()

### Hook System Integration

Hooks use package manager detection for command execution:

```javascript
// In post-edit-format.js
const { getExecCommand } = require('./lib/package-manager');

const formatCmd = getExecCommand('biome', 'format --write ' + filePath);
// Executes: npx biome format --write file.ts
// or:       pnpm dlx biome format --write file.ts
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:327-340]()

### Pattern Matching Across Package Managers

The `getCommandPattern()` function generates regex patterns that match equivalent commands across all package managers:

```javascript
// Generate pattern for 'dev' command
getCommandPattern('dev')
// Returns: (npm run dev|pnpm( run)? dev|yarn dev|bun run dev)

// Generate pattern for 'install' command
getCommandPattern('install')
// Returns: (npm install|pnpm install|yarn( install)?|bun install)

// Generic script pattern
getCommandPattern('lint')
// Returns: (npm run lint|pnpm( run)? lint|yarn lint|bun run lint)
```

This is used by hooks to detect package manager commands in bash tool calls regardless of which PM is configured.

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:370-416]()

