## Eval Framework

The eval-harness framework implements formal evaluation principles for AI-assisted development, treating evals as first-class testing artifacts.

### Eval Types

#### Capability Evals

Test new functionality that Claude should be able to accomplish:

```markdown
[CAPABILITY EVAL: feature-name]
Task: Description of what Claude should accomplish
Success Criteria:
  - [ ] Criterion 1
  - [ ] Criterion 2
  - [ ] Criterion 3
Expected Output: Description of expected result
```

**Structure**: [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:21-31]()

#### Regression Evals

Ensure existing functionality remains intact:

```markdown
[REGRESSION EVAL: feature-name]
Baseline: SHA or checkpoint name
Tests:
  - existing-test-1: PASS/FAIL
  - existing-test-2: PASS/FAIL
  - existing-test-3: PASS/FAIL
Result: X/Y passed (previously Y/Y)
```

**Structure**: [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:33-43]()

Sources: [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:19-43]()

### Grader Types

The eval framework supports three grader types for validating eval results:

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Grader Types"
        CodeGrader["Code-Based Grader<br/>grep, test runners<br/>Deterministic"]
        ModelGrader["Model-Based Grader<br/>Claude evaluation<br/>Open-ended"]
        HumanGrader["Human Grader<br/>Manual review<br/>Security-critical"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Use Cases"
        C1["File exists<br/>Pattern match<br/>Tests pass<br/>Build succeeds"]
        M1["Code quality<br/>Problem solving<br/>Edge cases<br/>Structure"]
        H1["Security review<br/>Architecture<br/>Risk assessment<br/>UX evaluation"]
    end
    
    CodeGrader --> C1
    ModelGrader --> M1
    HumanGrader --> H1
    
    style CodeGrader fill:#f9f9f9
    style ModelGrader fill:#f9f9f9
    style HumanGrader fill:#f9f9f9
```

**1. Code-Based Grader** [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:47-58]()

Deterministic validation using code execution:

```bash
# Pattern matching
grep -q "export function handleAuth" src/auth.ts && echo "PASS" || echo "FAIL"

# Test execution
npm test -- --testPathPattern="auth" && echo "PASS" || echo "FAIL"

# Build verification
npm run build && echo "PASS" || echo "FAIL"
```

**2. Model-Based Grader** [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:60-72]()

Use Claude to evaluate open-ended outputs with structured prompts evaluating problem-solving, structure, edge cases, and error handling.

**3. Human Grader** [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:74-81]()

Flag for manual review with risk level classification (LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH). Used primarily for security-critical changes.

Sources: [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:45-81]()

### Reliability Metrics

The framework uses two primary metrics to measure reliability:

#### pass@k Metric

"At least one success in k attempts" [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:85-89]()

| Metric | Definition | Typical Target |
|--------|-----------|---------------|
| pass@1 | First attempt success rate | Baseline measurement |
| pass@3 | Success within 3 attempts | > 90% for capability evals |

**Usage**: Measures how reliably Claude can accomplish a task given multiple attempts.

#### pass^k Metric

"All k trials succeed" [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:91-95]()

| Metric | Definition | Use Case |
|--------|-----------|----------|
| pass^3 | 3 consecutive successes | Critical paths, regression evals |

**Usage**: Higher bar for reliability. All attempts must succeed. Required for regression evals to ensure no degradation.

Sources: [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:83-95]()

