## Eval-Driven Development Workflow

The eval-driven development (EDD) workflow treats evals as the specification that guides implementation.

### Four-Phase Workflow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Dev as Developer
    participant Claude as Claude Code
    participant EvalDef as .claude/evals/<br/>feature.md
    participant Code as Source Code
    participant Graders as Graders<br/>(Code/Model/Human)
    participant Report as Eval Report
    
    Note over Dev,Report: Phase 1: Define (Before Coding)
    Dev->>Claude: /eval define feature-name
    Claude->>EvalDef: Create eval definition<br/>- Capability evals<br/>- Regression evals<br/>- Success metrics
    
    Note over Dev,Report: Phase 2: Implement
    Dev->>Claude: Request implementation
    Claude->>Code: Write code to pass evals
    
    Note over Dev,Report: Phase 3: Evaluate
    Dev->>Claude: /eval check feature-name
    Claude->>Graders: Run capability evals
    Claude->>Graders: Run regression evals
    Graders-->>Claude: PASS/FAIL results
    
    Note over Dev,Report: Phase 4: Report
    Claude->>Report: Generate eval report<br/>- pass@k metrics<br/>- Regression status<br/>- Overall status
    Report-->>Dev: READY FOR REVIEW / NEEDS WORK
```

### Phase 1: Define

Create eval definition before writing any code [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:99-116]():

```markdown
## EVAL DEFINITION: feature-xyz

### Capability Evals
1. Can create new user account
2. Can validate email format
3. Can hash password securely

### Regression Evals
1. Existing login still works
2. Session management unchanged
3. Logout flow intact

### Success Metrics
- pass@3 > 90% for capability evals
- pass^3 = 100% for regression evals
```

**Storage Location**: `.claude/evals/feature-xyz.md` [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:177-185]()

### Phase 2: Implement

Write code to satisfy the eval criteria [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:118-119]().

### Phase 3: Evaluate

Run evals and collect results [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:121-130]():

```bash
# Run capability evals
[Execute each capability eval, record PASS/FAIL]

# Run regression evals
npm test -- --testPathPattern="existing"
```

### Phase 4: Report

Generate comprehensive eval report [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:132-155]():

```markdown
EVAL REPORT: feature-xyz
========================

Capability Evals:
  create-user:     PASS (pass@1)
  validate-email:  PASS (pass@2)
  hash-password:   PASS (pass@1)
  Overall:         3/3 passed

Regression Evals:
  login-flow:      PASS
  session-mgmt:    PASS
  logout-flow:     PASS
  Overall:         3/3 passed

Metrics:
  pass@1: 67% (2/3)
  pass@3: 100% (3/3)

Status: READY FOR REVIEW
```

Sources: [skills/eval-harness/SKILL.md:97-155]()

### Integration Commands

| Command | Purpose | Output |
|---------|---------|--------|
| `/eval define feature-name` | Create eval definition | `.claude/evals/feature-name.md` |
| `/eval check feature-name` | Run current evals | Pass/fail status |
| `/eval report feature-name` | Generate full report | Detailed eval report |

