```

**Sources:** [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md:117-143]()

### Complementary vs Overlapping Concerns

| Concern | ECC | Plankton | Recommended Resolution |
|---------|-----|----------|----------------------|
| **Code formatting** | `post-edit-format.js` (Prettier) | `multi_linter.sh` (biome/ruff format) | Disable ECC's Prettier for JS/TS when using Plankton |
| **Type checking** | `post-edit-typecheck.js` (tsc) | `multi_linter.sh` (ty, biome) | Both can run; ECC for immediate feedback, Plankton for comprehensive |
| **Linting** | (none) | 20+ linters in Phase 2 | Plankton handles comprehensively |
| **Config protection** | (none) | PreToolUse + Stop hooks | Plankton exclusive feature |
| **Security scanning** | AgentShield, security-reviewer | Bandit, Semgrep | Complementary (AgentShield for config, Plankton for code) |
| **Package manager** | Detection + `/setup-pm` | Enforcement (blocks legacy) | Complementary |
| **Session learning** | Continuous learning, evaluate-session | (none) | ECC exclusive feature |
| **Console.log detection** | `post-edit-console-warn.js`, `check-console-log.js` | (none) | ECC exclusive feature |

**Sources:** [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md:117-143]()

### Recommended Integration Pattern

```bash
# 1. Install ECC as primary plugin (agents, skills, commands, rules)
/plugin install everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code

# 2. Add Plankton hooks to .claude/hooks/ (per-project)
cp -r plankton/.claude/hooks/* .claude/hooks/

# 3. Merge hook configurations in .claude/settings.json
# - Keep ECC's PreToolUse hooks (doc-file-warning, git-push-warning)
# - Replace ECC's Prettier PostToolUse with Plankton's multi_linter.sh for JS/TS
# - Keep ECC's console.log detection hooks
# - Add Plankton's config protection hooks

# 4. Use AgentShield for security audits (ECC integration)
/security-scan

# 5. Use verification-loop as final gate before PRs (ECC skill)
/verify
```

**Sources:** [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md:129-135](), [README.md:447-449]()

