    NoHooks --> SessionStart
    NoPlugin --> DriftGuards
```

**Sources:** [README.md:861-899]()

### AGENTS.md Format

Codex uses a single `AGENTS.md` file instead of separate `.md` files per agent:

```markdown
# Agent: planner

## Description
Feature implementation planning

## Tools
Read, Grep, Glob

## Model
opus

## Instructions
You are a feature planner...

---

# Agent: tdd-guide
...
```

**Sources:** [.codex/AGENTS.md]()

### Installation

```bash
# Copy reference config
cp .codex/config.toml ~/.codex/config.toml

# Run in repo — AGENTS.md auto-detected
codex
```

**Sources:** [README.md:867-875]()

### Sandbox Permissions

Codex has a permissions model that requires explicit tool grants. The `.codex/config.toml` declares allowed tools per agent:

```toml
[agents.planner]
tools = ["Read", "Grep", "Glob"]
model = "opus"
```

**Sources:** [.codex/config.toml]()

