This document covers the native Claude Code platform integration, including plugin installation, component distribution, feature coverage, and platform-specific behaviors. For cross-platform distribution to other IDEs, see [Cursor IDE Integration](#12.2), [OpenCode Integration](#12.3), and [Codex CLI Integration](#12.4).

---

## Overview

Claude Code receives **full feature parity** with all components from the Everything Claude Code repository. The integration is delivered through the native plugin system, with automatic distribution of agents, skills, commands, and hooks.

| Component Type | Count | Distribution Method |
|---------------|-------|---------------------|
| Agents | 14 | Plugin auto-install |
| Commands | 30+ | Plugin auto-install |
| Skills | 28+ | Plugin auto-install |
| Hooks | 8 event types | Auto-load from `hooks/hooks.json` |
| Rules | 8+ | Manual installation required |
| MCP Configs | 20+ servers | Manual configuration |

**Key Limitation**: The Claude Code plugin system does not support automatic `rules/` distribution ([upstream limitation](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference)). Rules must be installed manually.

Sources: [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25](), [.claude-plugin/marketplace.json:1-49]()

---

## Plugin System Architecture

The plugin is distributed through two manifest files that define component paths and marketplace metadata.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "GitHub Repository"
        Repo["affaan-m/everything-claude-code"]
        PluginJSON[".claude-plugin/plugin.json"]
        MarketJSON[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json"]
        AgentsDir["agents/"]
        SkillsDir["skills/"]
        CommandsDir["commands/"]
        HooksJSON["hooks/hooks.json"]
        RulesDir["rules/"]
    end
    
    subgraph "User Action"
        AddMarket["/plugin marketplace add"]
        InstallCmd["/plugin install"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Claude Code Installation"
        Settings["~/.claude/settings.json"]
        AgentsDest["~/.claude/agents/"]
        SkillsDest["~/.claude/skills/"]
        CommandsDest["~/.claude/commands/"]
        HooksLoad["Hook Auto-Load"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Manual Installation"
        ManualRules["cp rules/* ~/.claude/rules/"]
        RulesDest["~/.claude/rules/"]
    end
    
    Repo --> PluginJSON
    Repo --> MarketJSON
    Repo --> AgentsDir
    Repo --> SkillsDir
    Repo --> CommandsDir
    Repo --> HooksJSON
    Repo --> RulesDir
    
    AddMarket --> Settings
    Settings --> InstallCmd
    
    InstallCmd --> AgentsDest
    InstallCmd --> SkillsDest
    InstallCmd --> CommandsDest
    InstallCmd --> HooksLoad
    
    RulesDir -.manual.-> ManualRules
    ManualRules --> RulesDest
    
    PluginJSON -.defines.-> AgentsDir
    PluginJSON -.defines.-> SkillsDir
    PluginJSON -.defines.-> CommandsDir
    MarketJSON -.catalogs.-> PluginJSON
```

**Diagram: Plugin Distribution Flow**

The plugin manifest does **not** declare a `"hooks"` field. Claude Code v2.1+ automatically loads `hooks/hooks.json` from installed plugins by convention. Explicitly declaring hooks causes duplicate loading errors.

Sources: [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25](), [README.md:332-343](), [docs/ja-JP/README.md:407-416]()

---

## Plugin Manifest Structure

### plugin.json

Defines plugin metadata and version. The manifest intentionally omits component paths—Claude Code auto-discovers standard directories.

```json
{
  "name": "everything-claude-code",
  "version": "1.7.0",
  "description": "Complete collection of battle-tested Claude Code configs...",
  "author": {
    "name": "Affaan Mustafa",
    "url": "https://x.com/affaanmustafa"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code",
  "repository": "https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code",
  "license": "MIT",
  "keywords": [...]
}
```

**Key Fields**:
- `name`: Plugin identifier used in commands (`/everything-claude-code:plan`)
- `version`: Synchronized across `plugin.json`, `marketplace.json`, `package.json`, `.opencode/package.json`
- `repository`: Source for marketplace installation
- **No `"hooks"` field**: Prevents duplicate loading in Claude Code v2.1+

Sources: [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25](), [scripts/release.sh:1-84]()

### marketplace.json

Catalogs the plugin for marketplace discovery. Includes additional metadata for the marketplace UI.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://anthropic.com/claude-code/marketplace.schema.json",
  "name": "everything-claude-code",
  "description": "Battle-tested Claude Code configurations...",
  "owner": {
    "name": "Affaan Mustafa",
    "email": "me@affaanmustafa.com"
  },
  "plugins": [
    {
      "name": "everything-claude-code",
      "source": "./",
      "version": "1.7.0",
      "category": "workflow",
      "tags": ["agents", "skills", "hooks", "commands", "tdd", "code-review"],
      "strict": false
    }
  ]
}
```

**Key Fields**:
- `source`: Path to plugin root (relative to marketplace.json)
- `category`: Marketplace categorization (`workflow`)
- `strict`: When `false`, allows execution outside declared component directories
- `tags`: Search metadata for marketplace discovery

Sources: [.claude-plugin/marketplace.json:1-49]()

---

## Installation Methods

### Method 1: Marketplace Installation (Recommended)

```bash
# Add marketplace source
/plugin marketplace add affaan-m/everything-claude-code

# Install plugin
/plugin install everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code
```

This adds the marketplace to `~/.claude/settings.json` and installs all plugin components automatically.

**Manual settings.json Configuration**:

```json
{
  "extraKnownMarketplaces": {
    "everything-claude-code": {
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "affaan-m/everything-claude-code"
      }
    }
  },
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code": true
  }
}
```

**What Gets Installed**:
- All agents from `agents/*.md` → `~/.claude/agents/`
- All skills from `skills/*/` → `~/.claude/skills/`
- All commands from `commands/*.md` → `~/.claude/commands/`
- Hooks from `hooks/hooks.json` (auto-loaded, not copied)

**What Requires Manual Installation**:
- Rules from `rules/` → `~/.claude/rules/` (platform limitation)
- MCP configurations (user must add to `~/.claude.json` with API keys)

Sources: [README.zh-CN.md:68-74](), [README.zh-CN.md:300-344]()

### Method 2: Manual Installation

```bash
# Clone repository
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git

# Copy agents
cp everything-claude-code/agents/*.md ~/.claude/agents/

# Copy skills
cp -r everything-claude-code/skills/* ~/.claude/skills/

# Copy commands
cp everything-claude-code/commands/*.md ~/.claude/commands/

# Copy rules (required, manual only)
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* ~/.claude/rules/  # Language-specific
```

Manual installation provides granular control over which components to install but requires manually copying hooks to `settings.json`.

Sources: [README.zh-CN.md:352-377](), [docs/zh-TW/README.md:298-328]()

---

## Rules Installation Requirement

The Claude Code plugin system **does not support automatic rules distribution**. This is a platform limitation, not a repository design decision.

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph "Plugin Auto-Install"
        PluginAgents["agents/"]
        PluginSkills["skills/"]
        PluginCommands["commands/"]
        PluginHooks["hooks/hooks.json"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Manual Install Required"
        RulesCommon["rules/common/"]
        RulesTS["rules/typescript/"]
        RulesPy["rules/python/"]
        RulesGo["rules/golang/"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Claude Code Directories"
        AutoAgents["~/.claude/agents/"]
        AutoSkills["~/.claude/skills/"]
        AutoCommands["~/.claude/commands/"]
        ManualRules["~/.claude/rules/"]
    end
    
    PluginAgents -->|"auto-install"| AutoAgents
    PluginSkills -->|"auto-install"| AutoSkills
    PluginCommands -->|"auto-install"| AutoCommands
    PluginHooks -.->|"auto-load"| AutoAgents
    
    RulesCommon -.->|"cp -r"| ManualRules
    RulesTS -.->|"cp -r"| ManualRules
    RulesPy -.->|"cp -r"| ManualRules
    RulesGo -.->|"cp -r"| ManualRules
```

**Diagram: Component Distribution Methods**

**Installation Command**:

```bash
# Required: Install common rules (applies to all languages)
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/common/* ~/.claude/rules/

# Optional: Install language-specific rules
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/python/* ~/.claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/golang/* ~/.claude/rules/
```

**Project-Scoped Rules** (alternative to user-level):

```bash
mkdir -p .claude/rules
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/common/* .claude/rules/
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/typescript/* .claude/rules/
```

Rules in `.claude/rules/` apply only to the current project, not globally.

Sources: [README.zh-CN.md:76-86](), [README.zh-CN.md:332-344]()

