## Hook System Integration

### Auto-Loading Behavior (Claude Code v2.1+)

Claude Code v2.1+ automatically loads `hooks/hooks.json` from installed plugins. The `plugin.json` manifest **must not** declare a `"hooks"` field, or duplicate loading errors will occur:

```
Duplicate hooks file detected: ./hooks/hooks.json resolves to already-loaded file
```

This behavior changed between Claude Code versions, causing multiple fix/revert cycles in the repository ([#29](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/29), [#52](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/52), [#103](https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code/issues/103)).

**Regression Test Enforcement**:

A CI validation ensures `plugin.json` never declares hooks:

```javascript
// scripts/ci/validate-plugin-json.js (conceptual)
const pluginJSON = require('./.claude-plugin/plugin.json');
if ('hooks' in pluginJSON) {
  throw new Error('plugin.json must not declare "hooks" field (Claude Code v2.1+ auto-loads hooks/hooks.json)');
}
```

Sources: [docs/ja-JP/README.md:407-416]()

### Hook Event Types

Claude Code supports 8 hook event types. The `hooks/hooks.json` file defines matchers and handlers for each.

| Event Type | Trigger | Example Use Case |
|-----------|---------|------------------|
| `PreToolUse` | Before any tool execution | Block git push, warn about console.log |
| `PostToolUse` | After any tool execution | Auto-format code, run type checking |
| `SessionStart` | New session begins | Load previous session context |
| `SessionEnd` | Session ends | Persist session summary |
| `Stop` | User stops response | Extract learned patterns |
| `PreCompact` | Before manual compaction | Save current state |
| `SessionCompact` | After compaction completes | Update session metadata |
| `SessionRestart` | Session restart triggered | Clear stale state |

**Hook Definition Structure**:

```json
{
  "matcher": "tool == \"Edit\" && tool_input.file_path matches \"\\.ts$\"",
  "hooks": [
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command": "node scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js"
    }
  ]
}
```

Hooks are executed via Node.js scripts in `scripts/hooks/`, ensuring cross-platform compatibility (Windows, macOS, Linux).

Sources: [README.zh-CN.md:369-372](), [README.zh-CN.md:208-221]()

