## Hook System Superiority

OpenCode's plugin system provides 20+ event types compared to Claude Code's 8 hook phases, enabling more granular control over the development workflow.

### Hook Event Mapping

The following table maps Claude Code hook phases to equivalent OpenCode plugin events:

| Claude Code Hook | OpenCode Event | Description |
|-----------------|----------------|-------------|
| `PreToolUse` | `tool.execute.before` | Fires before any tool execution, can block |
| `PostToolUse` | `tool.execute.after` | Fires after tool completes, advisory only |
| `SessionStart` | `session.created` | Fires when new session begins |
| `SessionEnd` | `session.deleted` | Fires when session terminates |
| `Stop` | `session.idle` | Fires once per response completion |
| `PreCompact` | `context.compact.before` | Fires before context compaction |
| *(none)* | `file.edited` | Fires when file is modified |
| *(none)* | `file.watcher.updated` | Fires when watched file changes |
| *(none)* | `message.updated` | Fires when chat message updates |
| *(none)* | `lsp.client.diagnostics` | Fires when LSP diagnostics arrive |
| *(none)* | `tui.toast.show` | Fires when toast notification displays |

### Event Flow Architecture

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant OpenCode as OpenCode Engine
    participant Plugin as ECC Plugin
    participant Tool as Tool Execution
    participant LSP as LSP Server
    
    User->>OpenCode: /plan "add authentication"
    OpenCode->>Plugin: session.created event
    Plugin->>Plugin: Load previous session<br/>Detect project type
    
    OpenCode->>Plugin: tool.execute.before event
    Plugin->>Plugin: validate-intent.js<br/>suggest-compact.js
    Plugin-->>OpenCode: Allow/Block (exit code)
    
    OpenCode->>Tool: Execute tool
    Tool->>Tool: Edit files
    
    Tool->>Plugin: file.edited event
    Plugin->>Plugin: Track changes
    
    Tool->>Plugin: tool.execute.after event
    Plugin->>Plugin: format-file.js<br/>typecheck.js
    
    LSP->>Plugin: lsp.client.diagnostics event
    Plugin->>Plugin: Capture errors
    
    OpenCode->>Plugin: message.updated event
    Plugin->>Plugin: Update observations
    
    User->>OpenCode: End session
    OpenCode->>Plugin: session.idle event
    Plugin->>Plugin: Trigger learning analysis
    
    OpenCode->>Plugin: session.deleted event
    Plugin->>Plugin: Persist session summary
```

**Sources**: [docs/ja-JP/README.md:670-680](), [README.zh-CN.md:87-89]()

