## Configuration Structure

### opencode.json Schema

```json
{
  "name": "everything-claude-code",
  "version": "1.4.1",
  "description": "Production-grade agents, skills, hooks, and tools",
  
  "agents": [
    {
      "id": "planner",
      "path": "agents/planner.md",
      "enabled": true
    }
  ],
  
  "commands": [
    {
      "id": "plan",
      "path": "commands/plan.md",
      "trigger": "/plan"
    }
  ],
  
  "skills": [
    {
      "id": "tdd-workflow",
      "path": "skills/tdd-workflow/SKILL.md",
      "category": "workflow"
    }
  ],
  
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "run-tests",
      "path": "tools/run-tests.js",
      "description": "Execute test suite with framework detection"
    }
  ],
  
  "hooks": {
    "tool.execute.before": [
      {
        "matcher": "tool == 'Edit'",
        "handler": "hooks/validate-intent.js"
      }
    ],
    "tool.execute.after": [
      {
        "matcher": "tool == 'Edit'",
        "handler": "hooks/format-file.js"
      }
    ],
    "session.created": [
      {
        "handler": "hooks/session-start.js"
      }
    ],
    "session.deleted": [
      {
        "handler": "hooks/session-end.js"
      }
    ],
    "session.idle": [
      {
        "handler": "hooks/evaluate-session.js"
      }
    ],
    "file.edited": [
      {
        "handler": "hooks/observe-edit.js"
      }
    ]
  },
  
  "rules": {
    "path": ".opencode/instructions/INSTRUCTIONS.md"
  },
  
  "mcp": {
    "servers": {
      "github": { "enabled": true },
      "supabase": { "enabled": true }
    }
  }
}
```

### Unified Instructions File

OpenCode consolidates rules into a single `INSTRUCTIONS.md` file located at `.opencode/instructions/INSTRUCTIONS.md`, which combines:

- Common rules (coding style, git workflow, testing)
- Language-specific rules (TypeScript, Python, Go)
- Agent delegation guidelines
- Performance optimization rules

This differs from Claude Code's modular `.claude/rules/*.md` structure but achieves the same functional outcome.

**Sources**: [docs/ja-JP/README.md:724-730]()

