## OpenCode Event Type Reference

OpenCode provides 20+ event types organized into categories:

### Tool Lifecycle Events

| Event | Phase | Blocking | Description |
|-------|-------|----------|-------------|
| `tool.execute.before` | Pre-execution | ✅ Yes | Fires before any tool runs, can block with exit code 2 |
| `tool.execute.after` | Post-execution | ❌ No | Fires after tool completes, advisory only |
| `tool.validate` | Validation | ✅ Yes | Fires during tool input validation |
| `tool.cancel` | Cancellation | ❌ No | Fires when tool execution is cancelled |

### Session Events

| Event | Phase | Blocking | Description |
|-------|-------|----------|-------------|
| `session.created` | Start | ❌ No | Fires when new session begins, load context |
| `session.deleted` | End | ❌ No | Fires when session terminates, persist state |
| `session.idle` | Idle | ❌ No | Fires once per response completion |
| `session.resumed` | Resume | ❌ No | Fires when existing session resumes |

### File Events

| Event | Phase | Blocking | Description |
|-------|-------|----------|-------------|
| `file.edited` | Post-edit | ❌ No | Fires after file modification via Edit tool |
| `file.created` | Post-create | ❌ No | Fires after new file creation via Write tool |
| `file.deleted` | Post-delete | ❌ No | Fires after file deletion |
| `file.watcher.updated` | External | ❌ No | Fires when watched file changes externally |
| `file.watcher.created` | External | ❌ No | Fires when new file appears in watched directory |
| `file.watcher.deleted` | External | ❌ No | Fires when watched file is removed |

### Context Events

| Event | Phase | Blocking | Description |
|-------|-------|----------|-------------|
| `context.compact.before` | Pre-compact | ❌ No | Fires before context window compaction |
| `context.compact.after` | Post-compact | ❌ No | Fires after compaction completes |
| `context.window.warning` | Warning | ❌ No | Fires when context approaches limit |

### Message Events

| Event | Phase | Blocking | Description |
|-------|-------|----------|-------------|
| `message.created` | Creation | ❌ No | Fires when new message added to conversation |
| `message.updated` | Update | ❌ No | Fires when message content updates |
| `message.deleted` | Deletion | ❌ No | Fires when message removed |

### LSP Events

| Event | Phase | Blocking | Description |
|-------|-------|----------|-------------|
| `lsp.client.diagnostics` | Diagnostics | ❌ No | Fires when LSP server reports diagnostics |
| `lsp.client.error` | Error | ❌ No | Fires when LSP encounters error |

### UI Events

| Event | Phase | Blocking | Description |
|-------|-------|----------|-------------|
| `tui.toast.show` | Notification | ❌ No | Fires when toast notification displays |
| `tui.input.submitted` | Input | ❌ No | Fires when user submits input |

### Event Handler Exit Codes

OpenCode event handlers use the same exit code convention as Claude Code hooks:

| Exit Code | Behavior | Use Case |
|-----------|----------|----------|
| `0` | Allow | Validation passed, proceed with operation |
| `1` | Error | Handler failed, log error but continue |
| `2` | Block | Validation failed, abort operation |

**Sources**: [docs/ja-JP/README.md:670-680]()

