## Migration from Claude Code

When migrating ECC configurations from Claude Code to OpenCode, the following adaptations are required:

### Hook Translation

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Claude Code Hooks"
        CCPre["PreToolUse<br/>doc-file-warning.js"]
        CCPost["PostToolUse<br/>format-file.js"]
        CCStart["SessionStart<br/>session-start.js"]
        CCEnd["SessionEnd<br/>session-end.js"]
        CCStop["Stop<br/>evaluate-session.js"]
        CCCompact["PreCompact<br/>suggest-compact.js"]
    end
    
    subgraph "OpenCode Events"
        OCPre["tool.execute.before<br/>validate-intent.js"]
        OCPost["tool.execute.after<br/>format-file.js"]
        OCFileEdit["file.edited<br/>observe-edit.js"]
        OCStart["session.created<br/>session-start.js"]
        OCEnd["session.deleted<br/>session-end.js"]
        OCIdle["session.idle<br/>evaluate-session.js"]
        OCCompact["context.compact.before<br/>suggest-compact.js"]
    end
    
    CCPre --> OCPre
    CCPost --> OCPost
    CCPost -.additional.-> OCFileEdit
    CCStart --> OCStart
    CCEnd --> OCEnd
    CCStop --> OCIdle
    CCCompact --> OCCompact
```

### Plugin Configuration Mapping

| Claude Code | OpenCode | Notes |
|-------------|----------|-------|
| `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` | `.opencode/opencode.json` | Different schema, manual translation required |
| `hooks/hooks.json` | `hooks` property in `opencode.json` | Inline vs separate file |
| `.claude/rules/*.md` | `.opencode/instructions/INSTRUCTIONS.md` | Consolidated single file |
| Commands via `/namespace:cmd` | Commands via `/cmd` | No namespace prefix needed |
| Agents via `@agent-name` | Agents via `@agent-name` | Same syntax |
| Skills in `~/.claude/skills/` | Skills in `.opencode/skills/` | Project-local only |

### Custom Tools Opportunity

When migrating, consider converting hook-based quality checks to native custom tools:

**Before (Claude Code Hook)**:
```json
{
  "matcher": "tool == 'Bash' && tool_input.command contains 'npm test'",
  "hooks": [{
    "type": "command",
    "command": "node scripts/parse-test-output.js"
  }]
}
```

**After (OpenCode Custom Tool)**:
```javascript
// .opencode/tools/run-tests.js
module.exports = {
  name: "run-tests",
  description: "Run test suite with structured output",
  parameters: { /* ... */ },
  handler: async (params) => {
    // Direct implementation, no shell parsing
    const result = await runTests(params);
    return { success: true, coverage: result.coverage };
  }
};
```

