## Advantages and Trade-offs

### Advantages of Codex

| Advantage | Benefit |
|-----------|---------|
| **Explicit permissions** | Reduced security risk from malicious agents |
| **TOML configuration** | Version-controllable, diff-friendly settings |
| **Consolidated AGENTS.md** | Reduced file system overhead |
| **Sandbox isolation** | Agents cannot exceed declared capabilities |
| **No hooks dependency** | Simpler execution model, easier debugging |

### Trade-offs

| Trade-off | Impact |
|-----------|--------|
| **Manual quality checks** | More user intervention required |
| **No auto-formatting** | Code style drift without discipline |
| **No session persistence** | Context loss between sessions |
| **No continuous learning** | Patterns not automatically extracted |
| **Limited orchestration** | No PM2/multi-service workflows |

### When to Choose Codex

**Choose Codex when**:
- Security/compliance requires explicit capability grants
- Team prefers TOML over JSON configuration
- Debugging hook issues is time-consuming
- Project uses non-standard execution environments
- Manual verification workflows are acceptable

**Choose Claude Code when**:
- Automated quality enforcement is critical
- Hooks-based workflows provide value
- Continuous learning system is required
- Multi-service orchestration is needed
- Team prioritizes convenience over explicit control

**Sources**: High-level Diagram 4 (Cross-Platform Distribution Architecture)

