## Swift 6.2 Approachable Concurrency

### Overview

The `swift-concurrency-6-2` skill documents Swift 6.2's fundamental shift in concurrency semantics: async functions now stay on the calling actor by default instead of implicitly offloading to background threads. This eliminates a major class of data-race errors in Swift 6.0/6.1 code.

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **Skill Name** | `swift-concurrency-6-2` |
| **File Location** | [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md]() |
| **Target Platform** | Swift 6.2+, Xcode 26+ |
| **Primary Use Cases** | Migrating Swift 5.x/6.0/6.1 projects, resolving data-race errors, MainActor-based architectures |
| **Key Proposals** | SE-0466 (MainActor default isolation), SE-0461 (NonisolatedNonsendingByDefault) |

**Sources:** [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:1-17]()

### Concurrency Model Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "Swift 6.1 Model (OLD)"
        OldAsync["async function called"]
        OldOffload["Implicit background offload<br/>Default: global executor"]
        OldDataRace["Data race errors<br/>with @MainActor types"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Swift 6.2 Model (NEW)"
        NewAsync["async function called"]
        NewStay["Stays on calling actor<br/>Default: no offload"]
        NewSafe["Data-race safe by default"]
        Concurrent["@concurrent annotation<br/>Explicit background offload"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Core Annotations"
        MainActor["@MainActor<br/>Single-threaded isolation"]
        MainActorInference["MainActor default inference<br/>Opt-in mode for apps"]
        IsolatedConf["Isolated conformances<br/>@MainActor protocol conformances"]
    end
    
    OldAsync --> OldOffload
    OldOffload --> OldDataRace
    
    NewAsync --> NewStay
    NewStay --> NewSafe
    NewAsync -.opt-in.-> Concurrent
    
    MainActor --> NewStay
    MainActorInference --> MainActor
    IsolatedConf --> MainActor
```

**Sources:** [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:19-51](), [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:172-181]()

### Key Code Patterns

#### Isolated Conformances

The skill documents how MainActor types can now safely conform to non-isolated protocols using isolated conformances:

```swift
extension StickerModel: @MainActor Exportable {
    func export() {
        photoProcessor.exportAsPNG()
    }
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:53-92]()

**Key Entity:** `@MainActor` attribute on conformance declaration (line 64)

#### Global State Protection

Global and static variables must be protected with `@MainActor`:

```swift
@MainActor
final class StickerLibrary {
    static let shared: StickerLibrary = .init()  // OK
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:94-109]()

**Key Entity:** `@MainActor` attribute on class declaration (line 105)

#### Explicit Background Offloading with @concurrent

When actual parallelism is needed, use `@concurrent` to explicitly offload work:

```swift
nonisolated final class PhotoProcessor {
    @concurrent
    static func extractSubject(from data: Data) async -> Sticker { /* ... */ }
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:136-169]()

**Key Entity:** `@concurrent` attribute (line 156), `nonisolated` on containing type (line 142)

### Migration Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["Legacy Swift 5.x/6.0/6.1 project"]
    
    EnableSettings["Enable Approachable Concurrency<br/>in Build Settings"]
    CheckSPM{"Using<br/>Swift Package<br/>Manager?"}
    XcodeSetting["Xcode: Swift Compiler ><br/>Concurrency section"]
    SPMSetting["SPM: SwiftSettings API<br/>in Package.swift"]
    
    Migration["Use swift.org/migration<br/>Automatic code changes"]
    
    MainActorMode["Enable MainActor<br/>default inference mode"]
    CompileErrors["Fix data-race<br/>compiler errors"]
    
    AddConcurrent["Add @concurrent for<br/>CPU-intensive work"]
    Profile["Profile with Instruments<br/>to find bottlenecks"]
    
    Test["Test thoroughly<br/>Data races now compile-time errors"]
    
    Start --> EnableSettings
    EnableSettings --> CheckSPM
    CheckSPM -->|Yes| SPMSetting
    CheckSPM -->|No| XcodeSetting
    SPMSetting --> Migration
    XcodeSetting --> Migration
    
    Migration --> MainActorMode
    MainActorMode --> CompileErrors
    CompileErrors --> AddConcurrent
    AddConcurrent --> Profile
    Profile --> Test
```

**Sources:** [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:182-189](), [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:191-199]()

### Design Decisions Table

| Decision | Rationale | Code Construct |
|----------|-----------|----------------|
| Single-threaded by default | Most natural code is data-race free; concurrency is opt-in | Default async behavior (line 40-51) |
| Async stays on calling actor | Eliminates implicit offloading that caused data-race errors | Removed implicit executor hopping |
| Isolated conformances | MainActor types can conform to protocols without unsafe workarounds | `@MainActor` on `extension` (line 64) |
| `@concurrent` explicit opt-in | Background execution is a deliberate performance choice | `@concurrent` attribute (line 156) |
| MainActor default inference | Reduces boilerplate `@MainActor` annotations for app targets | Opt-in build setting (line 113-134) |

**Sources:** [skills/swift-concurrency-6-2/SKILL.md:172-181]()

