**Sources:** [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:19-68](), [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:109-153]()

### Core API Patterns

#### Availability Check Pattern

All code must check `model.availability` before creating sessions:

```swift
switch model.availability {
case .available:
    ContentView()
case .unavailable(.deviceNotEligible):
    Text("Device not eligible for Apple Intelligence")
case .unavailable(.appleIntelligenceNotEnabled):
    Text("Please enable Apple Intelligence in Settings")
case .unavailable(.modelNotReady):
    Text("Model is downloading or not ready")
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:19-42]()

**Key Entities:** `SystemLanguageModel.default` (line 25), `model.availability` (line 28), `.available` and `.unavailable(reason)` cases (lines 29-38)

#### Guided Generation with @Generable

The `@Generable` macro generates structured output types:

```swift
@Generable(description: "Basic profile information about a cat")
struct CatProfile {
    var name: String
    
    @Guide(description: "The age of the cat", .range(0...20))
    var age: Int
    
    @Guide(description: "A one sentence profile about the cat's personality")
    var profile: String
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:69-105]()

**Key Entities:** `@Generable` macro (line 76), `@Guide` attribute (lines 79, 82), `CatProfile.PartiallyGenerated` (auto-generated, referenced line 171)

#### Tool Protocol Pattern

Custom tools implement the `Tool` protocol:

```swift
struct RecipeSearchTool: Tool {
    let name = "recipe_search"
    let description = "Search for recipes matching a given term..."
    
    @Generable
    struct Arguments {
        var searchTerm: String
        var numberOfResults: Int
    }
    
    func call(arguments: Arguments) async throws -> ToolOutput {
        let recipes = await searchRecipes(term: arguments.searchTerm, limit: arguments.numberOfResults)
        return .string(recipes.map { "- \($0.name): \($0.description)" }.joined(separator: "\n"))
    }
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:109-153]()

**Key Entities:** `Tool` protocol (line 115), `Arguments` nested type with `@Generable` (lines 119-122), `call(arguments:)` method (line 125), `ToolOutput.string()` (line 129)

#### Snapshot Streaming Pattern

Streaming provides partial results as generation progresses:

```swift
let stream = session.streamResponse(to: "What are some exciting trip ideas?", generating: TripIdeas.self)

for try await partial in stream {
    // partial: TripIdeas.PartiallyGenerated (all properties Optional)
    partialResult = partial
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:155-202]()

**Key Entities:** `streamResponse(to:generating:)` method (line 166), `TripIdeas.PartiallyGenerated` type (line 171), `AsyncThrowingStream` iteration (line 171)

### Session Lifecycle

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant App
    participant SystemLM as "SystemLanguageModel.default"
    participant Session as "LanguageModelSession"
    participant Model as "On-Device Model"
    
    App->>SystemLM: Check availability
    
    alt model.availability == .available
        SystemLM-->>App: .available
        App->>Session: Create session(instructions:, tools:)
        
        loop Multi-turn conversation
            App->>Session: respond(to: prompt)
            Session->>Session: Check isResponding
            
            alt Not already responding
                Session->>Model: Generate response
                Model-->>Session: Response content
                Session-->>App: Response<String> or Response<T>
            else Already responding
                Session-->>App: Error: concurrent request
            end
        end
        
    else model unavailable
        SystemLM-->>App: .unavailable(reason)
        App->>App: Show error UI
    end
```

**Sources:** [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:44-68](), [skills/foundation-models-on-device/SKILL.md:206-215]()

