### SwiftUI Patterns

#### Basic Glass Effect

The fundamental modifier applies glass to any view:

```swift
Text("Hello, World!")
    .font(.title)
    .padding()
    .glassEffect()  // Default: regular variant, capsule shape
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:18-29]()

**Key Entity:** `.glassEffect()` modifier (line 28)

#### Customized Glass with Tint and Interactivity

```swift
Text("Hello, World!")
    .font(.title)
    .padding()
    .glassEffect(.regular.tint(.orange).interactive(), in: .rect(cornerRadius: 16.0))
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:31-45]()

**Key Entities:** `.regular` variant (line 42), `.tint(Color)` method (line 42), `.interactive()` method (line 42), `in:` shape parameter (line 42)

#### GlassEffectContainer for Performance

Multiple glass elements should be wrapped in a container:

```swift
GlassEffectContainer(spacing: 40.0) {
    HStack(spacing: 40.0) {
        Image(systemName: "scribble.variable")
            .frame(width: 80.0, height: 80.0)
            .glassEffect()
        
        Image(systemName: "eraser.fill")
            .frame(width: 80.0, height: 80.0)
            .glassEffect()
    }
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:47-74]()

**Key Entities:** `GlassEffectContainer` (line 61), `spacing:` parameter controls merge distance (line 61)

#### Morphing Transitions with Namespace

```swift
@Namespace private var namespace

GlassEffectContainer(spacing: 40.0) {
    HStack(spacing: 40.0) {
        Image(systemName: "scribble.variable")
            .glassEffect()
            .glassEffectID("pencil", in: namespace)
        
        if isExpanded {
            Image(systemName: "eraser.fill")
                .glassEffect()
                .glassEffectID("eraser", in: namespace)
        }
    }
}

Button("Toggle") {
    withAnimation { isExpanded.toggle() }
}
```

**Pattern Location:** [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:97-125]()

**Key Entities:** `@Namespace` property wrapper (line 102), `.glassEffectID(_:in:)` modifier (lines 110, 115), `withAnimation` (line 122)

