## SwiftUI Implementation Patterns

### Basic Glass Effect Application

The fundamental pattern applies the `.glassEffect()` modifier to any SwiftUI view [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:18-45]():

| Modifier | Purpose | Default Behavior |
|----------|---------|------------------|
| `.glassEffect()` | Apply glass material | Regular variant, capsule shape |
| `.glassEffect(.regular.tint(.orange).interactive(), in: .rect(cornerRadius: 16.0))` | Customized glass | Tinted, interactive, custom shape |

**Key Properties**:
- `.regular` - standard glass effect style
- `.tint(Color)` - color overlay for prominence
- `.interactive()` - enables touch/pointer reactions
- Shape parameter: `.capsule`, `.rect(cornerRadius:)`, `.circle`

Sources: [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:20-45]()

### Container Pattern for Multiple Elements

The `GlassEffectContainer` wraps multiple glass views for performance optimization and morphing capability [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:56-77]():

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant View as SwiftUI View
    participant Container as GlassEffectContainer
    participant GlassView1 as glassEffect() on View 1
    participant GlassView2 as glassEffect() on View 2
    
    View->>Container: GlassEffectContainer(spacing: 40.0)
    Container->>GlassView1: Apply glass material
    Container->>GlassView2: Apply glass material
    
    Note over Container,GlassView2: spacing parameter controls merge distance
    
    alt "Views close enough"
        Container->>Container: Blend glass shapes together
    else "Views too far"
        Container->>Container: Keep separate glass shapes
    end
```

**Container Properties**:
- `spacing: Double` - merge distance threshold for blending adjacent glass effects

Sources: [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:56-77]()

### Union and Morphing Patterns

The skill defines two advanced patterns for combining glass effects:

**glassEffectUnion** [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:78-96]():
- Combines multiple views into a single glass shape
- Requires: `@Namespace` variable, unique `id` parameter
- Use case: Group related elements under one glass surface

**glassEffectID for Morphing** [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:97-125]():
- Enables smooth transitions when glass views appear/disappear
- Requires: `@Namespace` variable, unique identifier string
- Use case: Animated expansion/collapse of glass UI

### Glass Effect Lifecycle

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start["View with .glassEffect()"]
    
    CheckContainer{Wrapped in<br/>GlassEffectContainer?}
    Standalone["Standalone rendering<br/>No morphing capability"]
    Container["Container rendering<br/>Morphing enabled"]
    
    CheckSpacing{Other glass views<br/>within spacing distance?}
    Separate["Render separate glass"]
    Merged["Merge glass shapes"]
    
    CheckUnion{Has glassEffectUnion<br/>with matching ID?}
    UniqueGlass["Individual glass shape"]
    UnionGlass["Combined glass shape"]
    
    CheckID{Has glassEffectID?}
    NoMorph["No morphing transitions"]
    MorphEnabled["Morphing transitions enabled"]
    
    Start --> CheckContainer
    CheckContainer -->|No| Standalone
    CheckContainer -->|Yes| Container
    
    Container --> CheckSpacing
    CheckSpacing -->|No| Separate
    CheckSpacing -->|Yes| Merged
    
    Merged --> CheckUnion
    CheckUnion -->|No| UniqueGlass
    CheckUnion -->|Yes| UnionGlass
    
    UniqueGlass --> CheckID
    CheckID -->|No| NoMorph
    CheckID -->|Yes| MorphEnabled
```

Sources: [skills/liquid-glass-design/SKILL.md:56-125]()

