This page provides an overview of how to contribute new components to the Everything Claude Code plugin. It covers the plugin's architecture, the contribution workflow, and the standards required for each component type.

For detailed guides on creating specific component types, see:
- [Contributing Agents](#13.1) - Creating new specialized agents
- [Contributing Skills](#13.2) - Creating domain knowledge and workflow skills
- [Contributing Commands](#13.3) - Creating slash commands
- [Contributing Hooks](#13.4) - Creating event-driven automations
- [Contribution Guidelines](#13.5) - General standards and expectations

---

## Plugin Architecture Overview

The plugin follows a modular architecture where each component type serves a distinct role. All components are declared in the plugin manifest and distributed through the Claude Code plugin system.

```mermaid
graph TB
    MANIFEST["plugin.json<br/>.claude-plugin/plugin.json"]
    
    subgraph "Distributable Components"
        AGENTS["Agents<br/>agents/*.md<br/>Specialized subagents"]
        SKILLS["Skills<br/>skills/*/<br/>Domain knowledge"]
        COMMANDS["Commands<br/>commands/*.md<br/>Slash commands"]
        HOOKS["Hooks<br/>hooks/hooks.json<br/>Event automations"]
        SCRIPTS["Scripts<br/>scripts/**/*.js<br/>Node.js utilities"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Manual Installation Only"
        RULES["Rules<br/>rules/*.md<br/>Always-follow guidelines"]
        MCPS["MCP Configs<br/>mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json<br/>External integrations"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Supporting Infrastructure"
        TESTS["Tests<br/>tests/**/*.test.js<br/>Component verification"]
        EXAMPLES["Examples<br/>examples/<br/>Sample configurations"]
        CONTEXTS["Contexts<br/>contexts/*.md<br/>Dynamic system prompts"]
    end
    
    MANIFEST -->|"declares"| AGENTS
    MANIFEST -->|"declares"| SKILLS
    MANIFEST -->|"declares"| COMMANDS
    MANIFEST -->|"auto-loads"| HOOKS
    
    AGENTS -.->|"use"| SKILLS
    COMMANDS -.->|"invoke"| AGENTS
    HOOKS -.->|"execute"| SCRIPTS
    
    RULES -.->|"constrain"| AGENTS
    RULES -.->|"constrain"| COMMANDS
    
    TESTS -.->|"verify"| AGENTS
    TESTS -.->|"verify"| SKILLS
    TESTS -.->|"verify"| HOOKS
```

**Sources:** [README.md:143-240](), [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-41]()

---

## Component Type Overview

The plugin supports five primary contribution types, each with specific structural requirements and integration patterns.

| Component Type | Location | Declared In | Distribution | Purpose |
|----------------|----------|-------------|--------------|---------|
| **Agents** | `agents/*.md` | `plugin.json:agents[]` | Automatic via plugin | Specialized subagents with tool permissions |
| **Skills** | `skills/*/` | `plugin.json:skills[]` | Automatic via plugin | Domain knowledge and workflow definitions |
| **Commands** | `commands/*.md` | `plugin.json:skills[]` | Automatic via plugin | Slash command shortcuts |
| **Hooks** | `hooks/hooks.json` | Auto-loaded (no declaration) | Automatic via plugin | Event-driven automations |
| **Rules** | `rules/*.md` | N/A | Manual copy only | Always-follow constraints |

**Key architectural constraint:** Rules cannot be distributed via plugins due to upstream Claude Code limitations. Contributors adding rules must document manual installation steps.

**Sources:** [README.md:143-240](), [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:25-40](), [README.md:78-88](), [README.md:355-367]()

