# Page: Contributing Agents

# Contributing Agents

<details>
<summary>Relevant source files</summary>

The following files were used as context for generating this wiki page:

- [README.md](README.md)
- [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md](skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md)
- [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md](skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md)
- [the-longform-guide.md](the-longform-guide.md)
- [the-shortform-guide.md](the-shortform-guide.md)

</details>



This document explains how to create new agents for the everything-claude-code plugin. Agents are specialized subagents that handle specific tasks through delegation, each with bounded contexts and restricted tool permissions.

For conceptual information about agents and their role in the plugin architecture, see [Agents](#3.2). For documentation on existing agents, see the Agent Reference section ([Planning & Architecture](#5.1), [Code Quality](#5.2), [Testing](#5.3), etc.).

---

## Agent File Structure

Agents are markdown files stored in the `agents/` directory. Each agent file consists of YAML front matter followed by markdown instructions.

### Agent File Anatomy

**Diagram: Agent File Structure**

```mermaid
graph TB
    AgentFile["agents/go-reviewer.md<br/>agents/tdd-guide.md<br/>agents/planner.md"]
    
    subgraph YAMLSection["YAML Front Matter (Lines 1-6)"]
        NameField["name: go-reviewer"]
        DescField["description: Expert Go code reviewer..."]
        ToolsField["tools: [Read, Grep, Glob, Bash]"]
        ModelField["model: opus"]
    end
    
    subgraph MarkdownBody["Markdown Body (Lines 8+)"]
        Overview["Role definition:<br/>You are a senior Go code reviewer..."]
        Diagnostics["Diagnostic commands:<br/>git diff, go vet, staticcheck"]
        Patterns["Security Checks CRITICAL<br/>Error Handling CRITICAL<br/>Code Quality HIGH"]
        OutputFormat["Review Output Format:<br/>[CRITICAL] Issue<br/>File: path:line"]
        Approval["Approval Criteria:<br/>Approve/Warning/Block"]
    end
    
    AgentFile --> NameField
    AgentFile --> DescField
    AgentFile --> ToolsField
    AgentFile --> ModelField
    AgentFile --> Overview
    AgentFile --> Diagnostics
    AgentFile --> Patterns
    AgentFile --> OutputFormat
    AgentFile --> Approval
```

**Sources:** [agents/go-reviewer.md:1-6](), [agents/go-reviewer.md:8-268](), [agents/go-build-resolver.md:1-6](), [agents/planner.md:1-6](), [agents/tdd-guide.md:1-6]()

### YAML Front Matter Fields

| Field | Required | Type | Description |
|-------|----------|------|-------------|
| `name` | Yes | string | Agent identifier matching filename |
| `description` | Yes | string | Purpose, specialization, and usage context |
| `tools` | Yes | array | Tool permissions (see Tool Permissions section) |
| `model` | Yes | string | Claude model: `opus`, `sonnet`, or `haiku` |

**Example:**
```yaml
---
name: go-reviewer
description: Expert Go code reviewer specializing in idiomatic Go, concurrency patterns, error handling, and performance. Use for all Go code changes. MUST BE USED for Go projects.
tools: ["Read", "Grep", "Glob", "Bash"]
model: opus
---
```

**Sources:** [agents/go-reviewer.md:1-6](), [agents/go-build-resolver.md:1-6]()

### Markdown Body Structure

The markdown body contains instructions that define the agent's behavior. Recommended structure:

1. **Role Definition**: Opening statement explaining the agent's expertise and mission
2. **Core Responsibilities**: Numbered list of primary tasks
3. **Diagnostic Commands**: Bash commands the agent should run to understand context
4. **Pattern Checks**: Organized by severity (CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM)
5. **Output Format**: Specification of how the agent should report findings
6. **Approval Criteria**: When to approve, warn, or block

**Sources:** [agents/go-reviewer.md:8-268](), [agents/go-build-resolver.md:8-369]()

---

## Tool Permissions

Agents have restricted access to tools based on their `tools` array in the front matter. This implements sandboxing for security and scope control.

### Available Tools

**Diagram: Tool Categories and Agent Examples**

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph ReadOnly["Read-Only Tools"]
        Read["Read<br/>Read file contents"]
        Grep["Grep<br/>Search within files"]
        Glob["Glob<br/>List files by pattern"]
    end
    
    subgraph WriteTools["Write Tools"]
        Write["Write<br/>Create/overwrite file"]
        Edit["Edit<br/>Modify existing file"]
    end
    
    subgraph ExecutionTools["Execution Tools"]
        Bash["Bash<br/>Execute shell commands"]
    end
    
    subgraph CoordinationTools["Coordination Tools"]
        Task["Task<br/>Parallel agent execution"]
    end
    
    subgraph GoReviewerExample["agents/go-reviewer.md:4"]
        GoReviewerTools["tools: [Read, Grep, Glob, Bash]<br/>Read-only + diagnostics"]
    end
    
    subgraph GoBuildExample["agents/go-build-resolver.md:4"]
        GoBuildTools["tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]<br/>Full modification access"]
    end
    
    ReadOnly --> GoReviewerTools
    ExecutionTools --> GoReviewerTools
    
    ReadOnly --> GoBuildTools
    WriteTools --> GoBuildTools
    ExecutionTools --> GoBuildTools
```

**Sources:** [agents/go-reviewer.md:4](), [agents/go-build-resolver.md:4](), [agents/code-reviewer.md:4](), [agents/tdd-guide.md:4]()

### Tool Selection Guidelines

| Agent Type | Recommended Tools | Rationale |
|------------|------------------|-----------|
| Code Reviewers | `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`, `Bash` | Read-only access prevents accidental modification |
| Build Resolvers | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Bash`, `Grep`, `Glob` | Needs write access to fix files |
| Planners | `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob` | Read-only for analysis |
| Test Runners | `Read`, `Bash`, `Grep`, `Glob` | Execute tests but don't modify code |
| Documentation | `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Grep`, `Glob` | Write access for doc updates |

**Tool Permission Patterns:**

- **Analysis-only agents**: `["Read", "Grep", "Glob", "Bash"]` (no Write/Edit)
- **Fix-it agents**: `["Read", "Write", "Edit", "Bash", "Grep", "Glob"]` (full access)
- **Orchestrator agents**: May include `["Task"]` for parallel execution

**Sources:** [agents/go-reviewer.md:4](), [agents/go-build-resolver.md:4]()

---

## Model Selection

Choose the appropriate Claude model based on task complexity and cost considerations.

### Model Comparison

| Model | Use Cases | Speed | Cost | Context |
|-------|-----------|-------|------|---------|
| `haiku` | Simple checks, pattern matching, formatting | Fastest | Lowest | 200k tokens |
| `sonnet` | General code review, moderate complexity | Medium | Medium | 200k tokens |
| `opus` | Complex analysis, architecture decisions, security | Slowest | Highest | 200k tokens |

### Selection Criteria

**Use `opus` for:**
- Security reviews with vulnerability detection ([agents/go-reviewer.md:16-49]())
- Complex architecture decisions
- Language-specific expertise requiring deep knowledge
- High-stakes approval decisions

**Use `sonnet` for:**
- General code reviews
- Test-driven development guidance
- Documentation updates
- Moderate complexity refactoring

**Use `haiku` for:**
- Quick pattern checks
- Formatting validation
- Simple linting
- Background observation analysis

**Example Model Selection:**
```yaml
# Security-critical Go review
model: opus

# General TDD guidance
model: sonnet

# Quick format check
model: haiku
```

**Sources:** [agents/go-reviewer.md:5](), [agents/go-build-resolver.md:5]()

