## Integration with Plugin System

### Plugin Registry Discovery

The plugin explicitly declares agents in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`:

```json
{
  "agents": [
    "./agents/architect.md",
    "./agents/build-error-resolver.md",
    "./agents/code-reviewer.md",
    "./agents/database-reviewer.md",
    "./agents/doc-updater.md",
    "./agents/e2e-runner.md",
    "./agents/go-build-resolver.md",
    "./agents/go-reviewer.md",
    "./agents/planner.md",
    "./agents/python-reviewer.md",
    "./agents/refactor-cleaner.md",
    "./agents/security-reviewer.md",
    "./agents/tdd-guide.md"
  ]
}
```

Each agent file listed in the `agents` array is registered and made available for delegation. 

**To add a new agent:**

1. Create the agent file in `agents/` directory
2. Add its relative path to the `agents` array in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`
3. The plugin system loads it automatically on next session

**Important:** The plugin does NOT auto-discover all `.md` files - agents must be explicitly declared in the manifest.

**Sources:** [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:26-40]()

### Agent Directory Structure

```
everything-claude-code/
├── .claude-plugin/
│   └── plugin.json                # agents: ["./agents/architect.md", ...]
└── agents/
    ├── architect.md               # System design | tools: [Read, Bash] | model: opus
    ├── build-error-resolver.md    # Build fixing | tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash]
    ├── code-reviewer.md           # General review | tools: [Read, Grep, Glob, Bash] | model: opus
    ├── database-reviewer.md       # DB optimization | tools: [Read, Grep, Bash] | model: opus
    ├── doc-updater.md             # Docs sync | tools: [Read, Write, Edit]
    ├── e2e-runner.md              # Playwright tests | tools: [Read, Bash, Grep]
    ├── go-build-resolver.md       # Go build fixes | tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]
    ├── go-reviewer.md             # Go review | tools: [Read, Grep, Glob, Bash] | model: opus
    ├── planner.md                 # Feature planning | tools: [Read, Grep, Glob] | model: sonnet
    ├── python-reviewer.md         # Python review | tools: [Read, Grep, Bash] | model: opus
    ├── refactor-cleaner.md        # Code cleanup | tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Grep, Glob]
    ├── security-reviewer.md       # Security analysis | tools: [Read, Bash] | model: opus
    └── tdd-guide.md               # TDD workflow | tools: [Edit, Bash, Grep] | model: sonnet
```

**Sources:** [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:26-40](), [agents/go-reviewer.md:1-6](), [agents/planner.md:1-6](), [agents/tdd-guide.md:1-6]()

### User Configuration Overlay

Users can add personal agents in `~/.claude/agents/` which are available alongside plugin-provided agents:

```
~/.claude/
└── agents/
    ├── custom-reviewer.md         # Personal agent
    ├── team-agent.md              # Team-shared agent
    └── project-specific.md        # Project conventions

# Plugin agents remain available:
~/.claude/plugins/everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code/agents/
```

**Agent Resolution Order:**
1. **User-level**: `~/.claude/agents/`
2. **Plugin-level**: `~/.claude/plugins/{plugin}/agents/`
3. **Project-level**: `.claude/agents/` (if supported)

Personal agents with the same `name` field as plugin agents will override the plugin version.

**Example Override:**
```yaml
# Create ~/.claude/agents/go-reviewer.md
---
name: go-reviewer
description: Custom Go reviewer with team-specific rules
tools: ["Read", "Grep", "Bash"]
model: sonnet
---
# This overrides the plugin's go-reviewer agent
```

**Sources:** [examples/user-CLAUDE.md:40-57](), [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:26-40]()

