## Contribution Checklist

Before submitting a new skill to ECC:

**Structure:**
- [ ] Directory named with kebab-case: `skills/[skill-name]/`
- [ ] File named `SKILL.md` (not `README.md`)
- [ ] YAML frontmatter at top with `name`, `description`, `origin`
- [ ] `name` field matches directory name exactly
- [ ] `origin` is `community` for contributed skills

**Content:**
- [ ] "When to Use" section with specific scenarios
- [ ] Includes both positive (apply when) and negative (avoid when) cases
- [ ] Concrete code examples for each pattern
- [ ] Anti-patterns documented with explanations
- [ ] References section linking to related skills/docs
- [ ] No always-follow rules (those belong in `rules/` directory)

**Validation:**
- [ ] Runs through `node scripts/validate-skills.js` without errors
- [ ] Tested with at least one command or agent
- [ ] Markdown is well-formed (no broken syntax)
- [ ] No duplicate content from existing skills
- [ ] Code examples use current library versions

**Documentation:**
- [ ] PR description explains what problem the skill solves
- [ ] Examples show before/after or anti-pattern/pattern comparisons
- [ ] Attribution if patterns originated from external sources

Sources: [README.md:786-795](), [README.md:356-359]()

