## Hook Execution Flow and Failure Points

Understanding where hooks can fail helps narrow down issues quickly. This diagram shows the execution flow with actual script names and exit codes:

```mermaid
graph TB
    ToolUse["Tool Use Event<br/>(Edit/Bash/Read/etc)"]
    
    ToolUse --> PreCheck{"PreToolUse Hooks<br/>in hooks.json"}
    PreCheck -->|"matcher: tool == 'Bash'"| PreExec["Execute PreToolUse Scripts:<br/>dev-server-tmux<br/>git-push-warning<br/>observe.sh (capture start)<br/>suggest-compact.js<br/>FAIL: Exit code 2 blocks tool<br/>FAIL: Script not executable"]
    
    PreExec -->|"exit 0"| ToolExec["Tool Executes"]
    PreExec -->|"exit 2"| Blocked["Tool Blocked<br/>Error reported to agent"]
    
    ToolExec --> PostCheck{"PostToolUse Hooks<br/>in hooks.json"}
    
    PostCheck -->|"matcher: tool_input.file_path"| PostExec["Execute PostToolUse Scripts:<br/>post-edit-format.js<br/>post-edit-typecheck.js<br/>post-edit-console-warn.js<br/>observe.sh (capture result)<br/>FAIL: prettier not in PATH<br/>FAIL: File path with spaces<br/>FAIL: tsc errors (exit 0, stderr only)"]
    
    PostExec --> Complete["Hook Complete<br/>Warnings → stderr<br/>Errors → stderr"]
    
    ResponseDone["Response Complete Event"]
    ResponseDone --> StopExec["Execute Stop Hooks:<br/>check-console-log.js<br/>getGitModifiedFiles()<br/>grepFile() for console.log<br/>FAIL: git not in PATH<br/>FAIL: Modified files deleted"]
    
    SessionEnd["SessionEnd Event"]
    SessionEnd --> EndExec["Execute SessionEnd Hooks:<br/>session-end.js<br/>writeSessionContent()<br/>parseSessionMetadata()<br/>FAIL: ~/.claude/sessions/ not writable<br/>FAIL: Corrupted transcript.jsonl"]
```

**Key Exit Codes:**

| Exit Code | Meaning | Hook Types | Example |
|-----------|---------|------------|---------|
| 0 | Success, proceed | All hooks | `session-start.js` loads context successfully |
| 1 | Error, but continue | PostToolUse, Stop, SessionEnd | `post-edit-typecheck.js` finds errors (warnings only) |
| 2 | Block operation | PreToolUse only | `dev-server-tmux` blocks `npm run dev` outside tmux |

**Testing Hooks in Isolation:**

```bash
# Test PreToolUse hook with stdin JSON
echo '{"tool":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"npm run dev"}}' | node scripts/hooks/dev-server-tmux.sh

# Test PostToolUse hook with file path
echo '{"tool":"Edit","tool_input":{"file_path":"test.ts"}}' | node scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js

# Test Stop hook (no stdin needed)
node scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js < /dev/null

# Test SessionStart hook
node scripts/hooks/session-start.js
```

Sources: [hooks/hooks.json:1-100](), [scripts/hooks/session-start.js:1-50](), [scripts/hooks/session-end.js:1-100](), [scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js:1-50](), [scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js:1-100](), [tests/hooks/hooks.test.js:87-273]()

