## Quick Diagnostic Checklist

Before diving into subsection troubleshooting guides, verify these prerequisites:

**Environment Checks:**
- [ ] Claude CLI version ≥ v2.1.0: `claude --version`
- [ ] Plugin installed: `/plugin list` shows `everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code`
- [ ] Rules copied to `~/.claude/rules/` (not auto-distributed by plugin system)
- [ ] Node.js available for hook scripts: `node --version`

**Configuration Checks:**
- [ ] `~/.claude/settings.json` contains `enabledPlugins` entry
- [ ] No `"hooks"` field in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` (causes duplicate detection)
- [ ] Active MCP count < 10: `/mcp` output
- [ ] Total tool count < 80: check MCP tools list

**File System Checks:**
- [ ] `hooks/hooks.json` exists in plugin directory
- [ ] `scripts/hooks/*.js` executable by Node.js
- [ ] `~/.claude/homunculus/` directory created for continuous learning v2
- [ ] Session files at `~/.claude/sessions/` if using memory persistence

