# Page: Context Window Issues

# Context Window Issues

<details>
<summary>Relevant source files</summary>

The following files were used as context for generating this wiki page:

- [README.md](README.md)
- [skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md](skills/autonomous-loops/SKILL.md)
- [skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md](skills/plankton-code-quality/SKILL.md)
- [the-longform-guide.md](the-longform-guide.md)
- [the-shortform-guide.md](the-shortform-guide.md)

</details>



This page covers troubleshooting and resolving context window degradation in Claude Code caused by excessive MCP servers, plugin overload, and improper configuration. The focus is on identifying the root causes, diagnosing the problem, and applying targeted fixes.

**Related Pages:** See [Configuration Guide](#9) for general configuration, [MCP Server Configuration](#9.4) for MCP setup details, and [Token Optimization Strategies](#11.2) for advanced optimization patterns.

---

## Understanding Context Window Budget

Claude Code provides a 200k token context window, but the usable space for active conversation varies dramatically based on how many tools, MCPs, and plugins are enabled.

### Token Allocation Breakdown

**Context Window Budget Allocation (200k tokens total):**

```mermaid
graph TB
    Total[Total200k]
    
    Total --> Rules[Rules5to10k]
    Total --> Tools[ToolsDefs]
    Total --> Active[ActiveConv]
    
    Rules --> RulesPath["~/.claude/rules/<br/>common/, typescript/, etc."]
    
    Tools --> MCPTools[MCPServerTools]
    Tools --> PluginTools[PluginTools]
    Tools --> CoreTools[CoreTools]
    
    MCPTools --> MCPEach["Per MCP:<br/>github: ~8k tokens<br/>supabase: ~6k<br/>vercel: ~7k"]
    PluginTools --> PluginEach["Per Plugin:<br/>typescript-lsp: ~10k<br/>hookify: ~3k"]
    CoreTools --> CoreList["Read, Write, Edit<br/>Bash, Grep, Glob<br/>Task: ~10k total"]
    
    MCPTools --> ScenarioA[ScenarioA]
    MCPTools --> ScenarioB[ScenarioB]
    
    ScenarioA --> ResultA["Result: ~160k usable"]
    ScenarioB --> ResultB["Result: ~90k usable"]
```

| Component | Good (5 MCPs) | Bad (14 MCPs) |
|-----------|---------------|---------------|
| Rules (always loaded) | 10k tokens | 10k tokens |
| Core tools | 10k tokens | 10k tokens |
| MCP tools | 30k tokens | 100k tokens |
| Plugin tools | 10k tokens | 10k tokens |
| **Total overhead** | **60k tokens** | **130k tokens** |
| **Usable for conversation** | **140k tokens** | **70k tokens** |

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:137-154](), [README.md:176-203]()

---

## Symptoms of Context Window Issues

| Symptom | Severity | Typical Cause |
|---------|----------|---------------|
| Context window reported as < 100k tokens | Critical | > 10 MCPs enabled or > 80 total tools |
| Claude responses become truncated mid-thought | High | Active conversation + tools exceeding 200k |
| `/compact` suggestions appear frequently | Medium | Legitimate usage, but may indicate too many tools |
| Tool execution timeouts | Medium | Large tool definitions causing overhead |
| Performance degradation (slower responses) | Medium | Tool definition parsing overhead |
| Cannot enable additional plugins/MCPs | Low | Already at practical limit |

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:144]()

---

## Root Causes

### Excessive MCP Servers

Each enabled MCP server in `~/.claude.json` adds tool definitions to the context window. The `mcpServers` object defines available MCPs, while `projects.disabledMcpServers` controls which are actually loaded.

#### MCP Tool Overhead by Server

**Common MCP servers and their overhead:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    MCPConfig[claudeJSONmcpServers]
    
    MCPConfig --> GitHub[githubMCP]
    MCPConfig --> Supabase[supabaseMCP]
    MCPConfig --> Memory[memoryMCP]
    MCPConfig --> Vercel[vercelMCP]
    MCPConfig --> Railway[railwayMCP]
    MCPConfig --> ClickHouse[clickhouseMCP]
    MCPConfig --> Firecrawl[firecrawlMCP]
    MCPConfig --> SeqThinking[seqthinkingMCP]
    MCPConfig --> Cloudflare[cloudflareMCP]
    MCPConfig --> Magic[magicMCP]
    
    GitHub --> GitHubDetails["@modelcontextprotocol/server-github<br/>Tools: create_issue, list_repos, etc.<br/>~8k tokens"]
    Supabase --> SupabaseDetails["@supabase/mcp-server-supabase<br/>Tools: query, list_tables, etc.<br/>~6k tokens"]
    Memory --> MemoryDetails["@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory<br/>Tools: store, retrieve<br/>~4k tokens"]
    Vercel --> VercelDetails["https://mcp.vercel.com<br/>Tools: deploy, logs<br/>~7k tokens"]
    Railway --> RailwayDetails["@railway/mcp-server<br/>Tools: deploy, status<br/>~6.5k tokens"]
    ClickHouse --> ClickHouseDetails["https://mcp.clickhouse.cloud/mcp<br/>Tools: query, schema<br/>~9k tokens"]
```

**Configuration file locations:**

| Location | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `~/.claude.json` | User-level MCP definitions |
| `.claude/settings.json` | Project-level `disabledMcpServers` |
| `mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json` | ECC reference configurations |

**The 80-Tool Threshold:** When total active tools exceed 80, context window degrades from 200k → ~70k usable.

**Sources:** [README.md:313-340](), [the-shortform-guide.md:127-154]()

### Excessive Plugin Installations

Plugins from `~/.claude/settings.json` `enabledPlugins` object add tool definitions:

| Plugin | Package/Source | Tool Count | Token Overhead |
|--------|----------------|------------|----------------|
| `typescript-lsp@claude-plugins-official` | Official LSP | 20-25 tools | 10,000-12,000 tokens |
| `pyright-lsp@claude-plugins-official` | Official LSP | 18-22 tools | 9,000-11,000 tokens |
| `hookify@claude-plugins-official` | Hook creator | 5-8 tools | 2,500-3,500 tokens |
| `mgrep@Mixedbread-Grep` | Search optimization | 3-5 tools | 1,500-2,500 tokens |
| `everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code` | ECC plugin | 10-15 tools | 5,000-8,000 tokens |

**Plugin configuration file:** `~/.claude/settings.json`

```json
{
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "typescript-lsp@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code": true
  }
}
```

**Sources:** [README.md:509-523](), [the-shortform-guide.md:289-308]()

### Always-Loaded Rules Overhead

Rules in `~/.claude/rules/` are loaded as system prompts in every session:

**ECC rules structure (from `rules/` directory):**

```
rules/
  common/
    coding-style.md      (~2,000 tokens)
    git-workflow.md      (~1,200 tokens)
    testing.md           (~1,800 tokens)
    performance.md       (~1,000 tokens)
    patterns.md          (~2,000 tokens)
    hooks.md             (~1,500 tokens)
    agents.md            (~2,500 tokens)
    security.md          (~1,500 tokens)
  typescript/
    typescript-*.md      (~3,000 tokens)
  python/
    python-*.md          (~2,500 tokens)
  golang/
    golang-*.md          (~2,000 tokens)
```

**Token impact:**
- Common rules only: ~12,000 tokens
- Common + TypeScript: ~15,000 tokens
- Common + Python + TypeScript + Golang: ~19,500 tokens

**Optimization:** Move rarely-used guidance to `~/.claude/skills/` (loaded on-demand) or use `claude --system-prompt "$(cat context.md)"` for dynamic injection.

**Sources:** [README.md:99-103](), [README.md:323-337](), [the-longform-guide.md:54-75]()

### Large Files in Working Set

Files read via the `Read` tool consume context proportional to their size. Repeated reads compound the problem.

**Token impact per file size:**

| File Size (LOC) | Token Cost | Read Count | Total Impact | Status |
|-----------------|------------|------------|--------------|--------|
| 100-500 | 800-4,000 | 1-3 | 2,400-12,000 | ✅ Acceptable |
| 500-1,000 | 4,000-8,000 | 1-3 | 12,000-24,000 | ⚠️ Warning |
| 1,000-2,000 | 8,000-16,000 | 1-3 | 24,000-48,000 | ❌ Refactor needed |
| > 2,000 | 16,000+ | 1-3 | 48,000+ | ❌ Critical |

**Common culprits:**
- Monolithic components (React: `src/App.tsx`, Vue: `src/views/Dashboard.vue`)
- Generated code (Prisma: `prisma/schema.prisma`, GraphQL: `src/generated/types.ts`)
- Configuration bundles (`webpack.config.js`, `vite.config.ts`)
- Data files (`data/fixtures.json`, `config/locales.yml`)

**Solution:** Modular codebase with 100-500 line files performs better in both token cost and success rate. See [Token Optimization Strategies](#11.2).

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:141-144]()

### Lazy Loading Misconception

Claude Code v2.1+ implements lazy loading for MCP tool execution, but **tool definitions are always loaded into context**.

**How lazy loading works:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    MCPConfig[claudeJSONmcpServers]
    
    MCPConfig --> DefinitionsLoaded[AllToolDefsLoaded]
    DefinitionsLoaded --> ContextImpact["Context consumed:<br/>6k-10k tokens per MCP"]
    
    ContextImpact --> FirstUse[ToolFirstUse]
    ContextImpact --> NeverUsed[ToolNeverUsed]
    
    FirstUse --> ExecutionLoaded["Execution code loaded<br/>(additional overhead)"]
    NeverUsed --> WastedTokens["Tool definition still in context<br/>(wasted tokens)"]
    
    WastedTokens --> Fix[disabledMcpServers]
    Fix --> NoDefinitions["No definitions loaded<br/>0 token overhead"]
```

**Key insight:** Lazy loading optimizes execution, not context window. Unused MCPs must be disabled via `projects.disabledMcpServers` to recover tokens.

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:26-33](), [README.md:176-203]()

---

## Diagnosing Context Window Problems

### Check Current Context Usage

The `/statusline` command displays context percentage. Custom status lines can include context tracking:

**Example custom status line:**

```
affoon:~ ctx:65% Opus 4.5 19:52
▌▌ plan mode on (shift+tab to cycle)
```

**Configuration:** Use `/statusline` to set up, then request inclusion of `{{context_percentage}}` variable.

**Red flags:**
- Context > 80% early in session (first 5-10 messages)
- Context > 90% before any code changes
- Frequent `/compact` suggestions from hooks

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:363-372]()

### List Active MCPs and Plugins

**Check MCP status:**

```bash
# In Claude Code terminal
/mcp
```

Output shows:
- All MCPs from `~/.claude.json` `mcpServers` object
- Enabled/disabled status per MCP
- Tool count per MCP (if available)

**Check plugin status:**

```bash
# In Claude Code terminal
/plugins
```

Navigate to:
1. **Marketplaces** tab - view available plugin sources
2. **Installed** tab - see enabled plugins with toggle switches

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:139-153](), [README.md:703-706]()

### Calculate Total Tool Count

**Tool count estimation formula:**

```
Total Tools = Core Tools + (MCP Count × 8) + (Plugin Count × 5)
Total Overhead = (Total Tools × 600) + Rules Overhead

Example:
- Core: 15 tools
- 6 MCPs: 48 tools
- 4 plugins: 20 tools
= 83 tools × 600 tokens = 49,800 tokens
+ 10,000 rules = 59,800 total overhead
```

**Diagnostic flow:**

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start[DiagnoseOverload]
    
    Start --> RunMCP[runMCPcommand]
    RunMCP --> CountMCP["Count enabled:<br/>github, supabase, etc."]
    
    CountMCP --> RunPlugins[runPluginsCommand]
    RunPlugins --> CountPlugins["Count enabled:<br/>typescript-lsp, etc."]
    
    CountPlugins --> Calculate[calculateFormula]
    Calculate --> EstTools["Tools = 15 + MCPs×8 + Plugins×5"]
    
    EstTools --> CheckThreshold{toolCount}
    
    CheckThreshold -->|"< 60"| Healthy["Healthy: ~180k usable"]
    CheckThreshold -->|"60-80"| Warning["Warning: ~140k usable"]
    CheckThreshold -->|"> 80"| Critical["Critical: ~70k usable"]
    
    Critical --> Actions["Disable MCPs/plugins"]
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:144-147]()

---

## Solutions

### Immediate Fix: Disable Unused MCPs

**File:** `~/.claude.json`

Add MCP names to `projects.disabledMcpServers` array:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-github"]
    },
    "supabase": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest", "--project-ref=YOUR_REF"]
    },
    "firecrawl": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "firecrawl-mcp"]
    },
    "memory": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory"]
    },
    "vercel": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.vercel.com"
    },
    "railway": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@railway/mcp-server"]
    }
  },
  "projects": {
    "disabledMcpServers": [
      "firecrawl",
      "railway",
      "vercel",
      "memory"
    ]
  }
}
```

**Impact:**
- Before: 6 MCPs × 8 tools = 48 tools (~36k tokens)
- After: 2 MCPs × 8 tools = 16 tools (~12k tokens)
- **Recovered:** ~24k tokens

**Best practice:** Configure 20-30 MCPs, enable only 4-6 per project.

**Sources:** [README.md:313-340](), [the-shortform-guide.md:312-340]()

### Alternative: Replace MCPs with CLI Skills

MCPs often wrap platform CLIs. A skill-based wrapper uses the `Bash` tool directly, avoiding MCP overhead.

**Comparison:**

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph MCPApproach
        GitHubMCP[githubMCP]
        GitHubMCP --> MCPTools["Tools: create_issue,<br/>list_repos, create_pr<br/>~8k tokens"]
    end
    
    subgraph SkillApproach
        GitHubSkill[skillsGitHubCLI]
        GitHubSkill --> BashTool["Bash tool:<br/>gh pr create<br/>~500 tokens"]
    end
    
    MCPTools -.16x overhead.-> BashTool
```

**Example skill:** `~/.claude/skills/github-cli/SKILL.md`

```markdown
---
name: github-cli
description: GitHub operations via gh CLI
---

# GitHub CLI Skill

Use `gh` CLI for GitHub operations:

**Create PR:**
```bash
gh pr create --title "feat: add feature" --body "Description" --base main
```

**Check status:**
```bash
gh pr status
```

**Merge PR:**
```bash
gh pr merge --squash --auto
```
```

**When to use:**
- Platform has a robust CLI (`gh`, `vercel`, `railway`)
- MCP overhead > 5k tokens
- You only need 3-5 MCP operations

**When to keep MCP:**
- Complex multi-step workflows
- Need contextual suggestions from MCP
- No CLI available

**Sources:** [the-longform-guide.md:24-33]()

### Project-Level MCP Disabling

**File:** `.claude/settings.json` (project-specific)

```json
{
  "disabledMcpServers": [
    "vercel",
    "railway",
    "supabase"
  ]
}
```

**Alternative:** Document in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` and use `/mcp` command interactively.

**Precedence order:**
1. `.claude/settings.json` (project-level, highest priority)
2. `~/.claude/settings.json` (user-level)
3. `~/.claude.json` `projects.disabledMcpServers` (legacy format)

**Use case:** Different MCP sets per project type:
- Web projects: `github`, `vercel`, `supabase`
- Data projects: `github`, `clickhouse`, `memory`
- Go projects: `github`, `railway`

**Sources:** [README.md:509-523](), [the-shortform-guide.md:139-153]()

### Disable Unused Plugins

**Method 1: Interactive toggle via `/plugins` command**

1. Run `/plugins` in Claude Code
2. Navigate to **Installed** tab
3. Toggle off unused plugins

**Method 2: Edit `~/.claude/settings.json`**

```json
{
  "enabledPlugins": {
    "typescript-lsp@claude-plugins-official": true,
    "everything-claude-code@everything-claude-code": true,
    "pyright-lsp@claude-plugins-official": false,
    "hookify@claude-plugins-official": false
  }
}
```

**Common plugins to disable:**

| Plugin | When to Disable |
|--------|-----------------|
| `typescript-lsp@claude-plugins-official` | Not working in TypeScript projects |
| `pyright-lsp@claude-plugins-official` | Not working in Python projects |
| `frontend-design@claude-code-plugins` | Backend-only work |
| `security-guidance@claude-code-plugins` | Not doing security review |

**Sources:** [README.md:509-523](), [the-shortform-guide.md:289-308]()

### Manual Compaction

**Command:** `/compact`

Triggers context window compaction when conversation history grows too large.

**Hook execution flow:**

```mermaid
graph TD
    CompactCmd[userRunsCompact]
    
    CompactCmd --> PreCompactHook[PreCompactHookFires]
    PreCompactHook --> Script["hooks/hooks.json<br/>matcher: *"]
    
    Script --> PreCompactJS[scriptsHooksPreCompactJS]
    PreCompactJS --> SaveState["Save to:<br/>~/.claude/sessions/<br/>YYYY-MM-DD-shortid-session.tmp"]
    
    SaveState --> ExitCode{exitCode}
    ExitCode -->|0| ProceedCompact[claudeCompacts]
    ExitCode -->|"!= 0"| BlockCompact[compactionBlocked]
    
    ProceedCompact --> Result["Older messages removed<br/>Context reduced"]
```

**Files involved:**
- Hook config: `hooks/hooks.json` `PreCompact` section
- Hook script: `scripts/hooks/pre-compact.js`
- Session storage: `~/.claude/sessions/`

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:235](), [the-longform-guide.md:78-85]()

---

## Prevention Strategies

### Strategy 1: Configured-But-Selective Approach

**Best Practice:** Configure many MCPs/plugins in user config, but enable only what's needed per project.

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph "User Configuration (~/.claude.json)"
        Configured["20-30 MCPs configured<br/>20-30 plugins installed"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project A: Web Development"
        EnabledA["Enabled:<br/>- github (6 tools)<br/>- vercel (8 tools)<br/>- supabase (5 tools)<br/>- typescript-lsp (12 tools)<br/>Total: ~31 tools"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project B: Data Engineering"
        EnabledB["Enabled:<br/>- github (6 tools)<br/>- clickhouse (10 tools)<br/>- memory (4 tools)<br/>- pyright-lsp (10 tools)<br/>Total: ~30 tools"]
    end
    
    subgraph "Project C: Go Backend"
        EnabledC["Enabled:<br/>- github (6 tools)<br/>- railway (8 tools)<br/>- memory (4 tools)<br/>Total: ~18 tools"]
    end
    
    Configured --> EnabledA
    Configured --> EnabledB
    Configured --> EnabledC
    
    style Configured fill:#f9f9f9
    style EnabledA fill:#f9f9f9
    style EnabledB fill:#f9f9f9
    style EnabledC fill:#f9f9f9
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:339]()

### Strategy 2: Context Window Monitoring

Configure custom statusline to always display context percentage:

```bash
/statusline
# Add: ctx:{{context_percentage}}%
```

This provides continuous feedback on context health.

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:363-371]()

### Strategy 3: Suggest-Compact Hook

**ECC's strategic compaction hook** tracks tool usage and suggests `/compact` at optimal intervals.

**Hook configuration:** `hooks/hooks.json`

```json
{
  "PostToolUse": [
    {
      "matcher": "*",
      "hooks": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "node scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**How it works:**

```mermaid
graph TB
    ToolExec[ToolExecuted]
    
    ToolExec --> PostHook[PostToolUseHookFires]
    PostHook --> ScriptRuns[suggestCompactJS]
    
    ScriptRuns --> ReadCounter["Read:<br/>~/.claude/.tool-count"]
    ReadCounter --> Increment[incrementCounter]
    Increment --> WriteCounter["Write:<br/>~/.claude/.tool-count"]
    
    WriteCounter --> CheckThreshold{counterGTE50}
    
    CheckThreshold -->|No| End[endHook]
    CheckThreshold -->|Yes| Suggest[outputToStderr]
    
    Suggest --> Message["[Hook] Consider /compact<br/>(50 tool uses)"]
    Message --> ResetCounter[counterEquals0]
```

**Configuration:**
- Default threshold: 50 tool uses
- Counter file: `~/.claude/.tool-count`
- Hook script: `scripts/hooks/suggest-compact.js`

**Related skill:** `skills/strategic-compact/` for detailed compaction strategy.

**Sources:** [README.md:241-242](), [skills/strategic-compact/SKILL.md:1-50]()

### Strategy 4: Regular Audits

Periodically review enabled MCPs/plugins:

```bash
# Monthly audit checklist:
1. Run /mcp - verify only needed MCPs are enabled
2. Run /plugins - verify only needed plugins are enabled
3. Check ~/.claude.json projects.disabledMcpServers
4. Review context percentage in recent sessions
5. Disable anything unused for > 2 weeks
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:137-154]()

---

## The 80-Tool Rule

**Critical threshold:** Total active tools > 80 causes severe context degradation (200k → ~70k usable).

### Performance Impact by Tool Count

| Tool Count | Usable Context | Status |
|------------|----------------|--------|
| < 60 | ~180k tokens | ✅ Optimal |
| 60-80 | ~140k tokens | ⚠️ Acceptable |
| 80-100 | ~100k tokens | ❌ Degraded |
| > 100 | ~70k tokens | ❌ Severely degraded |

### Calculation Examples

**Scenario A: 80 tools (acceptable)**

```
Core tools:   15 tools × 600 tokens =   9k tokens
MCPs (6):     48 tools × 600 tokens =  29k tokens
Plugins (4):  17 tools × 600 tokens =  10k tokens
Rules:        ---                   =  10k tokens
                                       ────────
Total overhead:                        58k tokens
Usable context:                       142k tokens ✅
```

**Scenario B: 120 tools (degraded)**

```
Core tools:   15 tools × 600 tokens =   9k tokens
MCPs (10):    80 tools × 600 tokens =  48k tokens
Plugins (6):  25 tools × 600 tokens =  15k tokens
Rules:        ---                   =  10k tokens
                                       ────────
Total overhead:                        82k tokens
Usable context:                       118k tokens ⚠️
```

**Scenario C: 150 tools (critical)**

```
Core tools:   15 tools × 600 tokens =   9k tokens
MCPs (14):   112 tools × 600 tokens =  67k tokens
Plugins (8):  23 tools × 600 tokens =  14k tokens
Rules:        ---                   =  10k tokens
                                       ────────
Total overhead:                       100k tokens
Usable context:                       100k tokens ❌
```

**Formula:**
```
Overhead = (Tool_Count × 600) + 10k
Usable = 200k - Overhead
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:144-147](), [README.md:176-203]()

---

## Compaction Failures

### Symptoms

- `/compact` command fails with error
- Context percentage unchanged after compaction
- Critical context lost after compaction
- `PreCompact` hook error messages in stderr

### Cause: PreCompact Hook Failures

**Hook configuration:** `hooks/hooks.json`

```json
{
  "PreCompact": [
    {
      "matcher": "*",
      "hooks": [
        {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "node scripts/hooks/pre-compact.js"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Debug procedure:**

```mermaid
graph TD
    Failure[CompactFails]
    
    Failure --> CheckScript[checkScriptExists]
    CheckScript --> ScriptPath["ls scripts/hooks/pre-compact.js"]
    
    ScriptPath --> TestManually[testManually]
    TestManually --> RunScript["node scripts/hooks/pre-compact.js"]
    
    RunScript --> CheckErrors{errorType}
    
    CheckErrors -->|ENOENT| MissingDir[missingSessionsDir]
    CheckErrors -->|EACCES| PermError[permissionDenied]
    CheckErrors -->|SyntaxError| NodeVersion[wrongNodeVersion]
    
    MissingDir --> FixDir["mkdir -p ~/.claude/sessions"]
    PermError --> FixPerms["chmod 755 ~/.claude/sessions"]
    NodeVersion --> UpgradeNode["Upgrade to Node.js 18+"]
```

**Common errors:**

| Error | Cause | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `ENOENT: no such file or directory` | `~/.claude/sessions/` doesn't exist | `mkdir -p ~/.claude/sessions` |
| `EACCES: permission denied` | Wrong permissions on sessions dir | `chmod 755 ~/.claude/sessions` |
| `SyntaxError: Unexpected token` | Node.js < 18 | Upgrade Node.js to 18+ |
| `Command not found: node` | Node.js not installed | Install Node.js |

**Temporary workaround:** Comment out `PreCompact` section in `hooks/hooks.json` to allow compaction without state saving.

**Sources:** [README.md:480-489]()

### Cause: Insufficient Memory

Compaction loads full conversation into memory. Low-RAM systems (< 8GB) may fail.

**Alternatives to compaction:**

| Method | Command | Use Case |
|--------|---------|----------|
| Rewind | `/rewind` | Go back to earlier state |
| Fork | `/fork` | Start fresh conversation with same context |
| Session files | Load from `~/.claude/sessions/` | Continue in new session with summary |

**Recovery flow:**

```mermaid
graph TD
    LowMem[CompactFailsLowMem]
    
    LowMem --> CloseApps[closeOtherApps]
    CloseApps --> Retry[retryCompact]
    
    Retry --> Success{compactSucceeds}
    Success -->|Yes| Done[continueSession]
    Success -->|No| Alternatives[useAlternatives]
    
    Alternatives --> Method1[useRewind]
    Alternatives --> Method2[useFork]
    Alternatives --> Method3[loadSessionFile]
    
    Method3 --> SessionScript["scripts/hooks/session-end.js<br/>saves summaries"]
```

**Sources:** [the-shortform-guide.md:232](), [the-longform-guide.md:78-86]()

---

## Recovery Checklist

**Symptom:** Usable context < 100k tokens early in session

**Diagnostic steps:**

1. ☐ Run `/mcp` - count enabled MCPs (target: ≤ 6)
2. ☐ Run `/plugins` - count enabled plugins (target: ≤ 5)
3. ☐ Calculate total tools: `15 + (MCPs × 8) + (Plugins × 5)` (target: < 80)
4. ☐ Check `/statusline` for context percentage

**Immediate fixes:**

5. ☐ Edit `~/.claude.json` - add unused MCPs to `projects.disabledMcpServers`
6. ☐ Edit `~/.claude/settings.json` - set unused plugins to `false` in `enabledPlugins`
7. ☐ Restart Claude Code to apply changes
8. ☐ Verify context percentage improved in new session

**If still degraded:**

9. ☐ Check for large files (> 1,000 lines) in recent reads - refactor to smaller modules
10. ☐ Temporarily disable LSP plugins (`typescript-lsp`, `pyright-lsp`)
11. ☐ Move rarely-used rules from `~/.claude/rules/` to `~/.claude/skills/`
12. ☐ Replace high-overhead MCPs with CLI skills (see [Alternative: Replace MCPs with CLI Skills](#alternative-replace-mcps-with-cli-skills))

**Nuclear option:**

13. ☐ Create minimal config - only `github` MCP, no plugins, common rules only
14. ☐ Test in isolated project directory with `.claude/settings.json` override

**Sources:** [README.md:176-203](), [the-shortform-guide.md:137-154]()

