## Configuration Validation

### Validate hooks.json Schema

Use the CI validator to check configuration:

```bash
# Run validator
node scripts/ci/validate-hooks.js

# Expected output:
# ✓ Valid JSON structure
# ✓ All event types valid
# ✓ All hooks have required fields
# ✓ Inline JS syntax valid
# Validated 8 event types with 23 hooks
```

Sources: [tests/ci/validators.test.js:240-353]()

### Common Configuration Errors

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["hooks.json"] --> B{"Valid JSON?"}
    B -->|No| C["Error: Invalid JSON"]
    B -->|Yes| D{"Valid event type?"}
    D -->|No| E["Error: Unknown event<br/>(PreToolUse, PostToolUse, etc.)"]
    D -->|Yes| F{"Has matcher?"}
    F -->|No| G["Error: Missing matcher field"]
    F -->|Yes| H{"Has hooks array?"}
    H -->|No| I["Error: Missing hooks array"]
    H -->|Yes| J{"Each hook has type?"}
    J -->|No| K["Error: Missing type field"]
    J -->|Yes| L{"Each hook has command?"}
    L -->|No| M["Error: Missing command field"]
    L -->|Yes| N{"Inline JS valid?"}
    N -->|No| O["Error: Invalid inline syntax"]
    N -->|Yes| P["✓ Valid Configuration"]
```

Sources: [scripts/ci/validate-hooks.js]() (implied by test coverage)

### Required Fields Checklist

| Field | Required | Type | Notes |
|-------|----------|------|-------|
| `hooks` | Yes | Object | Top-level container |
| `hooks.<EventType>` | Yes | Array | Event type must be valid |
| `hooks.<EventType>[].matcher` | Yes | String | Tool name pattern or `*` |
| `hooks.<EventType>[].hooks` | Yes | Array | Hook definitions |
| `hooks.<EventType>[].hooks[].type` | Yes | String | Must be `"command"` |
| `hooks.<EventType>[].hooks[].command` | Yes | String | Executable command |
| `hooks.<EventType>[].hooks[].async` | No | Boolean | Default: false |
| `hooks.<EventType>[].hooks[].timeout` | No | Number | Default: 30 (seconds) |

**Valid Event Types:**
- `PreToolUse`
- `PostToolUse`
- `SessionStart`
- `SessionEnd`
- `Stop`
- `PreCompact`

Sources: [hooks/hooks.json:1-194](), [tests/ci/validators.test.js:268-308]()

