## Security Considerations

### Command Injection Prevention

The package manager system validates all user input to prevent shell command injection:

**Allowed Characters:**

| Input Type | Regex | Example |
|------------|-------|---------|
| PM name | `^[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+$` | `pnpm`, `yarn`, `bun` |
| Script name | `^[@a-zA-Z0-9_./-]+$` | `dev`, `@scope/bin` |
| Arguments | `^[@a-zA-Z0-9\s_./:=,'"*+-]+$` | `--watch --port=3000` |

**Rejected Patterns:**

Shell metacharacters are rejected to prevent injection:

```
; | & ` $ ( ) { } < > !
```

**Code Reference:**

```javascript
// Validation in getRunCommand
const SAFE_NAME_REGEX = /^[@a-zA-Z0-9_./-]+$/;
if (!SAFE_NAME_REGEX.test(script)) {
  throw new Error(`Script name contains unsafe characters: ${script}`);
}

// Validation in getExecCommand
const SAFE_ARGS_REGEX = /^[@a-zA-Z0-9\s_./:=,'"*+-]+$/;
if (args && typeof args === 'string' && !SAFE_ARGS_REGEX.test(args)) {
  throw new Error(`Arguments contain unsafe characters: ${args}`);
}
```

**Sources:** [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:284-285](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:319](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:292-299](), [scripts/lib/package-manager.js:327-340]()

