This page covers troubleshooting for plugin installation problems, including marketplace addition failures, duplicate hooks detection, missing rules, and version compatibility issues. For issues with individual plugin components after successful installation, see [Hook Failures](#14.2) or [Package Manager Issues](#14.3). For general installation guidance, see [Plugin Installation](#4.1).

---

## Overview

The Everything Claude Code plugin can be installed via the plugin marketplace or manually. The plugin system has specific requirements and limitations that can cause installation to fail or behave unexpectedly. This page documents common failure modes and their solutions.

**Sources:** [README.md:296-318](), [README.md:69-101]()

---

## Plugin Architecture and Distribution Model

Understanding how Claude Code loads plugin components from `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` helps diagnose installation issues. The plugin manifest declares `agents/`, `commands/`, and `skills/` explicitly, while `hooks/hooks.json` is auto-loaded by convention in v2.1.0+.

### Component Loading and File Structure

**Plugin Manifest Structure:**
```json
{
  "name": "everything-claude-code",
  "version": "1.7.0",
  "description": "...",
  "agents": ["agents/*.md"],
  "commands": ["commands/*.md"],
  "skills": ["skills/*/SKILL.md"]
}
```

**Directory Layout:**
```
everything-claude-code/
├── .claude-plugin/
│   ├── plugin.json          # Declares agents, commands, skills
│   └── marketplace.json     # Marketplace metadata
├── agents/*.md              # Auto-loaded from plugin.json
├── commands/*.md            # Auto-loaded from plugin.json
├── skills/*/SKILL.md        # Auto-loaded from plugin.json
├── hooks/hooks.json         # Auto-loaded by CONVENTION (v2.1.0+)
├── rules/*.md               # NOT distributable (manual only)
└── mcp-configs/             # NOT distributable (manual only)
```

### Component Loading Behavior Diagram

```mermaid
graph TB
    PLUGIN_JSON[".claude-plugin/plugin.json"]
    MARKETPLACE_JSON[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json"]
    
    AGENTS["agents/<br/>planner.md<br/>architect.md<br/>tdd-guide.md"]
    COMMANDS["commands/<br/>plan.md<br/>tdd.md<br/>verify.md"]
    SKILLS["skills/<br/>coding-standards/<br/>tdd-workflow/<br/>search-first/"]
    HOOKS["hooks/hooks.json"]
    
    RULES["rules/<br/>security.md<br/>coding-style.md<br/>testing.md"]
    SETTINGS["~/.claude/settings.json"]
    CLAUDE_JSON["~/.claude.json"]
    
    PLUGIN_JSON -->|"Explicit declaration"| AGENTS
    PLUGIN_JSON -->|"Explicit declaration"| COMMANDS
    PLUGIN_JSON -->|"Explicit declaration"| SKILLS
    PLUGIN_JSON -.->|"NO declaration<br/>(v2.1.0+ auto-loads)"| HOOKS
    
    HOOKS -->|"Convention-based loading"| AUTO_LOAD["Claude Code v2.1.0+<br/>searches for hooks/hooks.json"]
    
    PLUGIN_JSON -.->|"Blocked by platform"| RULES
    PLUGIN_JSON -.->|"Blocked by platform"| SETTINGS
    PLUGIN_JSON -.->|"Blocked by platform"| CLAUDE_JSON
```

**Key Points:**
- `plugin.json` contains fields: `name`, `version`, `description`, `author`, `homepage`, `repository`, `license`, `keywords`
- Agent/command/skill paths are declared in `plugin.json` but hooks are NOT
- `hooks/hooks.json` is discovered automatically by Claude Code v2.1.0+ through directory scanning
- Rules cannot be distributed due to platform security constraints (would allow arbitrary system modifications)

**Sources:** [.claude-plugin/plugin.json:1-25](), [.claude-plugin/marketplace.json:1-49](), [README.md:309-318]()

