## Issue 2: Missing Rules After Installation

### Symptom

Plugin installs successfully but rules are not applied. Commands and agents work, but style guidelines and security checks defined in `rules/*.md` are not enforced.

### Root Cause

The Claude Code plugin system does not support distributing `rules` via plugins. This is an upstream limitation in the Claude Code plugin architecture.

### Solution

Rules must be manually copied after plugin installation. The repository contains these rule files in the `rules/` directory:

**Available rules:**
- `security.md` - Security scanning and secrets detection guidelines
- `coding-style.md` - Code formatting and style conventions
- `testing.md` - Test coverage and TDD guidelines
- `git-workflow.md` - Commit message format and branch strategies
- `agents.md` - Agent delegation and orchestration patterns
- `performance.md` - Performance optimization guidelines

**Option A: User-level rules (applies to all projects)**

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git

# Copy all rules to global config
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/* ~/.claude/rules/
```

**Option B: Project-level rules (applies to current project only)**

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/affaan-m/everything-claude-code.git

# Copy rules to project config
mkdir -p .claude/rules
cp -r everything-claude-code/rules/* .claude/rules/
```

**Option C: Language-specific installation using `install.sh`**

```bash
# Install only TypeScript-relevant rules
npx ecc-install typescript

# Install only Python-relevant rules
npx ecc-install python

# Install all rules
npx ecc-install
```

**Verification:**

```bash
# Check rules are installed
ls -la ~/.claude/rules/
# Expected output: security.md, coding-style.md, testing.md, git-workflow.md, agents.md, performance.md

# Verify rules are being applied (Claude will mention them in responses)
echo "Do we have any coding rules?" | claude -p
```

**Sources:** [README.md:80-88](), [README.md:355-368](), [install.sh:1-10](), [package.json:79-81]()

